&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Breaking Changes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Notable Behavioral Changes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes and Operator&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM worker services use short names&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;VllmWorker&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;VllmPrefillWorker&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;VllmDecodeWorker&lt;/code&gt; -&amp;gt; &lt;code&gt;worker&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;prefill&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;decode&lt;/code&gt;), matching the SGLang, TensorRT-LLM, and Mocker backends and keeping generated names under Grove&#39;s 45-character limit (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4497532241&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/9848&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/9848/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/9848&quot;&gt;#9848&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Update DynamoGraphDeployment manifests, overrides, scripts, dashboards, and alerts that reference the old vLLM service names. Pod names, Kubernetes Service names, and the &lt;code&gt;dynamo_component&lt;/code&gt; metric label change with them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo Operator no longer adopts resources it does not own&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5283064444&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13990&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13990/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13990&quot;&gt;#13990&lt;/a&gt;). An existing object that shares a name with an Operator-managed child but has no controller owner, or a different one, is no longer adopted, updated, or deleted; the deployment reports an ownership conflict instead.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Before upgrading, delete or rename any pre-existing Deployments, Services, or other objects that collide by name with Operator-managed children.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multinode settings are validated more strictly&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5385558718&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14468&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14468/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14468&quot;&gt;#14468&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5397917678&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14533&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14533/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14533&quot;&gt;#14533&lt;/a&gt;). &lt;code&gt;multinode&lt;/code&gt; is accepted only on &lt;code&gt;worker&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;prefill&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;decode&lt;/code&gt; components, &lt;code&gt;roles[]&lt;/code&gt; takes at most two entries, and a declared role must carry a complete PodTemplate that owns its launch command.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Remove &lt;code&gt;multinode&lt;/code&gt; from frontend, Planner, EPP, and other non-engine components, trim each &lt;code&gt;roles&lt;/code&gt; list to a leader and a worker, and give every declared role a full PodTemplate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Init container named &lt;code&gt;runtime&lt;/code&gt; is reserved&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5471236822&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14927&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14927/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14927&quot;&gt;#14927&lt;/a&gt;). Declaring it with &lt;code&gt;restartPolicy: Always&lt;/code&gt; switches the component into Dynamo native sidecar mode, and the runtime version then resolves from that container&#39;s image.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Rename any unrelated init container called &lt;code&gt;runtime&lt;/code&gt; before upgrading. In sidecar mode, make sure the runtime image carries a semantic-version tag or set &lt;code&gt;runtimeVersionOverride&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grove v0.1.0-alpha.14 is required for new multinode deployments created by Dynamo Operator v1.6.0&lt;/strong&gt;, and the Operator now owns the &lt;code&gt;DYNAMO_RANK&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;DYNAMO_LEADER_ADDRESS&lt;/code&gt; environment variables on those components (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5631128275&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15374&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15374/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15374&quot;&gt;#15374&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5728458702&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15704&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15704/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15704&quot;&gt;#15704&lt;/a&gt;). Existing deployments keep their current environment and command lines.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Upgrade an externally managed Grove and its CRDs to &lt;code&gt;v0.1.0-alpha.14&lt;/code&gt; before creating new multinode deployments, and rename any user-defined &lt;code&gt;DYNAMO_RANK&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;DYNAMO_LEADER_ADDRESS&lt;/code&gt; variables in component pod templates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grove Coherent updates are opt-in&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5764690872&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15903&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15903/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15903&quot;&gt;#15903&lt;/a&gt;). Without the &lt;code&gt;nvidia.com/grove-update-strategy: Coherent&lt;/code&gt; annotation, every DynamoGraphDeployment uses Grove&#39;s RollingRecreate default.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Set the &lt;code&gt;nvidia.com/grove-update-strategy: Coherent&lt;/code&gt; annotation on deployments that should keep coherent rollouts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operator-managed namespace discovery is strict for Dynamo v1.6.0 runtimes&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5677753631&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15561&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15561/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15561&quot;&gt;#15561&lt;/a&gt;). A frontend in deployment &lt;code&gt;foo&lt;/code&gt; no longer discovers workers from deployment &lt;code&gt;foo-bar&lt;/code&gt;; it still admits &lt;code&gt;foo&lt;/code&gt;, its &lt;code&gt;foo-&amp;lt;8 hex&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; worker generations, and &lt;code&gt;foo-legacy&lt;/code&gt;.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; If you relied on discovery across deployments that share a name prefix, rename the deployments or set &lt;code&gt;DYN_NAMESPACE_PREFIX_STRICT=false&lt;/code&gt; on the affected frontend and EPP containers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GB200 nodes report GPU SKU &lt;code&gt;gb200&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; instead of &lt;code&gt;gb200_sxm&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5731000285&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15711&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15711/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15711&quot;&gt;#15711&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Update automation and profiling configuration that reads the Operator-populated &lt;code&gt;gpuSku&lt;/code&gt; for GB200 nodes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Snapshot enables CUDA shared-memory capture by default&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5739021653&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15791&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15791/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15791&quot;&gt;#15791&lt;/a&gt;). Automatic checkpoint jobs set &lt;code&gt;nvidia.com/cuda-shared-memory-support: enabled&lt;/code&gt;, the checkpoint target container must set &lt;code&gt;command&lt;/code&gt;, existing checkpoints are recaptured once because the compatibility hash now includes the annotation, and snapshot mode no longer forces the NCCL and TensorRT-LLM zero-copy variables off.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Add an explicit &lt;code&gt;command&lt;/code&gt; to the checkpoint target container, or set &lt;code&gt;nvidia.com/cuda-shared-memory-support: disabled&lt;/code&gt; on the DynamoGraphDeployment to keep the previous behavior. Set &lt;code&gt;NCCL_CUMEM_ENABLE&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;NCCL_NVLS_ENABLE&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;TLLM_NCCL_SYMMETRIC_ZERO_COPY&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt; yourself if you depended on snapshot mode disabling them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The platform chart blocks the Dynamo Operator update when an externally managed Grove is incompatible or still rolling out&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5939551974&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16891&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16891/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16891&quot;&gt;#16891&lt;/a&gt;). A preflight Job checks the Grove controller before the Operator installs or upgrades, and it pulls &lt;code&gt;docker.io/library/python:3.12-slim&lt;/code&gt; by default.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Upgrade the external Grove controller and its CRDs to &lt;code&gt;v0.1.0-alpha.14&lt;/code&gt; before upgrading the platform chart, and override &lt;code&gt;dynamo-operator.grovePreflight.image&lt;/code&gt; for internal registries. Set &lt;code&gt;dynamo-operator.grovePreflight.enabled=false&lt;/code&gt; only when a separate compatibility gate exists.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend and API&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remaining OpenAI routes return JSON errors&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5284046972&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14002&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14002/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14002&quot;&gt;#14002&lt;/a&gt;). Malformed requests to embeddings, image generation and edits, and audio now receive the standard JSON error envelope instead of a plain-text body.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Update clients that parse plain-text error bodies from these endpoints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Non-streaming &lt;code&gt;/v1/responses&lt;/code&gt; no longer infers tool calls from assistant text&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5460286701&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14846&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14846/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14846&quot;&gt;#14846&lt;/a&gt;). Only structured tool calls from the backend become function-call output items; &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;tool_call&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; markup in plain text stays text.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Enable a tool-call parser on the backend (for example &lt;code&gt;--dyn-tool-call-parser hermes&lt;/code&gt;) so tool calls arrive structured.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Forced tool choice wins over &lt;code&gt;response_format&lt;/code&gt; on SGLang&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5322417126&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14179&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14179/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14179&quot;&gt;#14179&lt;/a&gt;). &lt;code&gt;tool_choice=&quot;required&quot;&lt;/code&gt; or a named tool now constrains output to a tool call, and requests that cannot satisfy a forced tool choice, such as &lt;code&gt;required&lt;/code&gt; with no tools, are rejected.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Send a non-empty &lt;code&gt;tools&lt;/code&gt; array with &lt;code&gt;tool_choice=&quot;required&quot;&lt;/code&gt;, and use &lt;code&gt;tool_choice=&quot;auto&quot;&lt;/code&gt; when &lt;code&gt;response_format&lt;/code&gt; should shape the output.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Boundary-only reasoning parsers fail at startup&lt;/strong&gt; with the vLLM chat processor (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5484973987&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14991&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14991/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14991&quot;&gt;#14991&lt;/a&gt;). Parsers such as &lt;code&gt;openai_gptoss&lt;/code&gt; previously started and then failed each request with HTTP 500.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Remove or replace boundary-only reasoning parsers when using &lt;code&gt;--dyn-chat-processor vllm&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Anthropic billing preambles are stripped by default&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5750551364&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15826&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15826/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15826&quot;&gt;#15826&lt;/a&gt;). The &lt;code&gt;x-anthropic-billing-header&lt;/code&gt; preamble that Claude Code adds is removed from requests unless disabled, reducing tokens and prompt-cache variation.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Set &lt;code&gt;DYN_STRIP_ANTHROPIC_PREAMBLE=0&lt;/code&gt; or pass &lt;code&gt;--no-strip-anthropic-preamble&lt;/code&gt; to keep preambles intact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structural tags are on by default for supported parsers&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5767478451&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15916&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15916/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15916&quot;&gt;#15916&lt;/a&gt;). &lt;code&gt;DYN_ENABLE_STRUCTURAL_TAG&lt;/code&gt; now defaults to &lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;DYN_STRUCTURAL_TAG_SCOPE&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;always&lt;/code&gt;, so valid tool schemas that use constructs the grammar backend rejects, such as regex lookahead, can fail requests.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Set &lt;code&gt;DYN_ENABLE_STRUCTURAL_TAG=false&lt;/code&gt; if your tool schemas use constructs the grammar backend rejects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;/v1/models/&amp;lt;model&amp;gt;/ready&lt;/code&gt; returns 503 for a known but unready model&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5949408334&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16943&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16943/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16943&quot;&gt;#16943&lt;/a&gt;). It previously returned HTTP 200 with &lt;code&gt;ready: false&lt;/code&gt;. The diagnostic JSON body is unchanged.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Parse the JSON body on both &lt;code&gt;200&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;503&lt;/code&gt; responses in diagnostic clients, and treat &lt;code&gt;503&lt;/code&gt; as unready and retry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Router and Planner&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo Router policy YAML takes precedence over scoring flags&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5547780005&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15202&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15202/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15202&quot;&gt;#15202&lt;/a&gt;). Parameters under &lt;code&gt;worker_selection.instances[].parameters&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;--router-policy-config&lt;/code&gt; override the deprecated command-line flags and environment variables, and shared-cache hits now earn a default multiplier of &lt;code&gt;0.5&lt;/code&gt; when shared cache is enabled through YAML. The overlap-query response no longer returns &lt;code&gt;router_credit_blocks&lt;/code&gt;; use the raw cache-hit fields.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Audit policy YAML for parameters that now override existing flags, and set &lt;code&gt;shared_cache_multiplier: 0.0&lt;/code&gt; explicitly if shared-cache hits should earn no credit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Router requests always pass through the policy queue&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5321142073&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14176&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14176/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14176&quot;&gt;#14176&lt;/a&gt;). Uncontended requests no longer bypass the queue, and a policy class with no registered workers returns a no-endpoints (service unavailable) error instead of a queue-rejected error.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Update error handling that matched the queue-rejected error for an empty worker set.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo Planner caps throughput scaling at 8 replicas per decision&lt;/strong&gt; per component (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5342307544&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14296&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14296/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14296&quot;&gt;#14296&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Raise &lt;code&gt;max_throughput_scaling_replicas&lt;/code&gt; in the Planner configuration if you rely on larger single-step scaling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance-model options renamed from AIConfigurator to AISimulate&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;--aic-*&lt;/code&gt; -&amp;gt; &lt;code&gt;--ais-*&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;aic_perf_model&lt;/code&gt; -&amp;gt; &lt;code&gt;ais_perf_model.roles&lt;/code&gt;) across the Planner, Mocker, and replay tools (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5502358375&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15063&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15063/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15063&quot;&gt;#15063&lt;/a&gt;). Retired &lt;code&gt;DYN_AIC_*&lt;/code&gt; environment variables now fail at startup.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Rename &lt;code&gt;--aic-*&lt;/code&gt; flags to their &lt;code&gt;--ais-*&lt;/code&gt; equivalents, replace &lt;code&gt;DYN_AIC_*&lt;/code&gt; environment variables with their AIS equivalents, and move Planner performance-model settings under &lt;code&gt;ais_perf_model.roles&lt;/code&gt;. The old CLI spellings are accepted only temporarily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KV routing rejects text-input workers at discovery&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5948737351&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16938&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16938/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16938&quot;&gt;#16938&lt;/a&gt;). vLLM workers started with &lt;code&gt;--use-vllm-tokenizer&lt;/code&gt;, and other text-input workers, are no longer admitted when the effective Router mode requires KV routing.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Remove &lt;code&gt;--use-vllm-tokenizer&lt;/code&gt; so the frontend tokenizes, or select a non-KV Router mode for those workers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Runtime, Transport, and Metrics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Invalid &lt;code&gt;DYN_REQUEST_PLANE&lt;/code&gt; values fail at startup&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5055134781&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12612&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12612/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12612&quot;&gt;#12612&lt;/a&gt;). Empty or unrecognized values previously fell back to TCP silently.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Unset &lt;code&gt;DYN_REQUEST_PLANE&lt;/code&gt; or set it to &lt;code&gt;tcp&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;nats&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Invalid &lt;code&gt;DYN_EVENT_PLANE&lt;/code&gt; values fail at startup&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5893100962&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16712&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16712/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16712&quot;&gt;#16712&lt;/a&gt;). A misspelled value previously logged a warning and fell back to ZMQ.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Unset &lt;code&gt;DYN_EVENT_PLANE&lt;/code&gt; or set it to &lt;code&gt;nats&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;zmq&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unbracketed IPv6 ZMQ endpoints are rejected&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5634929659&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15383&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15383/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15383&quot;&gt;#15383&lt;/a&gt;). An address such as &lt;code&gt;tcp://2001:db8::10:5555&lt;/code&gt; now fails fast instead of retrying forever, IPv4 and hostname endpoints bind as IPv4 again, and a &lt;code&gt;::&lt;/code&gt; system-status bind advertises a non-loopback IPv4 address when no non-loopback IPv6 address exists.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Bracket IPv6 hosts in event-plane endpoints (&lt;code&gt;tcp://[2001:db8::10]:5555&lt;/code&gt;), and set an explicit advertise host if you relied on &lt;code&gt;::1&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Histogram bucket variables take effect under their documented names&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;DYN_HISTOGRAM_DYN_METRICS_*&lt;/code&gt; -&amp;gt; &lt;code&gt;DYN_METRICS_*&lt;/code&gt;) (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5394339609&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14514&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14514/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14514&quot;&gt;#14514&lt;/a&gt;). The documented &lt;code&gt;DYN_METRICS_&amp;lt;HISTOGRAM&amp;gt;_MIN&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;_MAX&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;_COUNT&lt;/code&gt; variables were previously ignored and now change bucket boundaries.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Audit existing &lt;code&gt;DYN_METRICS_*&lt;/code&gt; histogram settings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NIXL telemetry settings are validated at startup&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5415419348&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14625&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14625/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14625&quot;&gt;#14625&lt;/a&gt;). Unrecognized &lt;code&gt;NIXL_TELEMETRY_ENABLE&lt;/code&gt; values and invalid ports are rejected, and the default NIXL Prometheus port changes from 19090 to 9090.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Set &lt;code&gt;NIXL_TELEMETRY_ENABLE&lt;/code&gt; to a boolean value such as &lt;code&gt;y&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;n&lt;/code&gt;, and set &lt;code&gt;NIXL_TELEMETRY_PROMETHEUS_PORT&lt;/code&gt; explicitly if your scrape configuration expects 19090.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backends&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;--publish-kv-events&lt;/code&gt; no longer turns on TensorRT-LLM performance metrics&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4974335251&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12162&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12162/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12162&quot;&gt;#12162&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5323022629&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14181&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14181/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14181&quot;&gt;#14181&lt;/a&gt;). The flag now publishes KV events only; iteration statistics and forward-pass metrics have their own opt-in.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Add &lt;code&gt;--publish-metrics&lt;/code&gt; to TensorRT-LLM workers that relied on &lt;code&gt;--publish-kv-events&lt;/code&gt; for performance or forward-pass metrics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM sidecar speaks the OpenEngine gRPC API&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5353127902&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14349&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14349/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14349&quot;&gt;#14349&lt;/a&gt;). Engines that serve only the older TensorRT-LLM gRPC service no longer work with the sidecar.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Run a TensorRT-LLM build that serves the OpenEngine (&lt;code&gt;openengine.v1&lt;/code&gt;) gRPC API.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM-Omni diffusion options no longer carry hardcoded defaults&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5421798834&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14702&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14702/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14702&quot;&gt;#14702&lt;/a&gt;). &lt;code&gt;--boundary-ratio&lt;/code&gt; no longer defaults to &lt;code&gt;0.875&lt;/code&gt;, and the offload, VAE slicing, and VAE tiling switches stay unset unless provided, so each model&#39;s own defaults apply.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Pass &lt;code&gt;--boundary-ratio 0.875&lt;/code&gt; or the matching &lt;code&gt;--no-*&lt;/code&gt; flags explicitly if you depended on the previous values.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang accepts top-logprob requests without an opt-in and validates &lt;code&gt;top_logprobs&lt;/code&gt; strictly&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5947511977&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16927&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16927/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16927&quot;&gt;#16927&lt;/a&gt;). &lt;code&gt;logprobs: true&lt;/code&gt; without &lt;code&gt;top_logprobs&lt;/code&gt; returns only the sampled token, and a positive &lt;code&gt;top_logprobs&lt;/code&gt; without &lt;code&gt;logprobs: true&lt;/code&gt;, or a negative, boolean, or non-integer value, returns HTTP 400.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Send &lt;code&gt;logprobs: true&lt;/code&gt; with any positive &lt;code&gt;top_logprobs&lt;/code&gt;, set &lt;code&gt;top_logprobs&lt;/code&gt; explicitly to receive alternatives, and remove &lt;code&gt;DYN_SGL_ALLOW_TOP_LOGPROBS&lt;/code&gt; from deployments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deprecated and Removed&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Removed the TensorRT-LLM AutoDeploy backend&lt;/strong&gt;, which TensorRT-LLM &lt;code&gt;v1.3.0rc29&lt;/code&gt; deleted upstream with no replacement (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5645849853&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15418&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15418/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15418&quot;&gt;#15418&lt;/a&gt;). PyTorch is now the only TensorRT-LLM backend, and &lt;code&gt;backend: _autodeploy&lt;/code&gt; raises a clear error.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Remove &lt;code&gt;backend: _autodeploy&lt;/code&gt; from TensorRT-LLM extra engine arguments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Removed the &lt;code&gt;dynamo.mocker._worker&lt;/code&gt; compatibility module&lt;/strong&gt; that v1.5.x retained for existing configurations (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5327171993&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14209&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14209/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14209&quot;&gt;#14209&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Launch live Mocker workers with &lt;code&gt;python3 -m dynamo.mocker&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deprecated &lt;code&gt;DYN_ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_PARSERS_V2&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; in favor of &lt;code&gt;DYN_PARSER_VERSION&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5478666328&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14950&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14950/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14950&quot;&gt;#14950&lt;/a&gt;). The old variable still works with a warning, and a value that conflicts with &lt;code&gt;DYN_PARSER_VERSION&lt;/code&gt; stops startup.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Replace &lt;code&gt;DYN_ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_PARSERS_V2=1&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;DYN_PARSER_VERSION=2&lt;/code&gt;, or leave both unset to use each model family&#39;s default.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deprecated component &lt;code&gt;minAvailable&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; in favor of native provider overrides, &lt;code&gt;value.spec.minAvailable&lt;/code&gt; for standalone cliques and &lt;code&gt;value.minAvailable&lt;/code&gt; for scaling groups (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5764690872&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15903&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15903/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15903&quot;&gt;#15903&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Move component &lt;code&gt;minAvailable&lt;/code&gt; settings into the matching provider override.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deprecated the Router scoring and selection flags&lt;/strong&gt; in favor of &lt;code&gt;--router-policy-config&lt;/code&gt;, including the six scoring flags, &lt;code&gt;--load-aware&lt;/code&gt;, the prefill and decode selection and queue-threshold flags, and their environment variables such as &lt;code&gt;DYN_SHARED_CACHE_MULTIPLIER&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5547780005&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15202&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15202/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15202&quot;&gt;#15202&lt;/a&gt;). They are slated for removal in Dynamo v1.7.0.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Move these settings into the policy YAML passed to &lt;code&gt;--router-policy-config&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deprecated &lt;code&gt;--publish-events-and-metrics&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; for TensorRT-LLM workers in favor of &lt;code&gt;--publish-kv-events&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;--publish-metrics&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4974335251&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12162&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12162/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12162&quot;&gt;#12162&lt;/a&gt;). The combined flag works for one more release.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Replace it with one or both of the split flags.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deprecated the legacy worker names in DynamoGraphDeploymentRequest overrides&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;VllmWorker&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;VllmPrefillWorker&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;VllmDecodeWorker&lt;/code&gt;, and the matching SGLang and TensorRT-LLM names) (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4497532241&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/9848&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/9848/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/9848&quot;&gt;#9848&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Target &lt;code&gt;worker&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;prefill&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;decode&lt;/code&gt; in DGDR overrides.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deprecated the &lt;code&gt;gb200_sxm&lt;/code&gt; GPU SKU&lt;/strong&gt; in DGDR v1beta1 in favor of &lt;code&gt;gb200&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5731000285&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15711&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15711/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15711&quot;&gt;#15711&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Set &lt;code&gt;spec.hardware.gpuSku: gb200&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deprecated the &lt;code&gt;planner.powerAwareness.enabled&lt;/code&gt; Helm value&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5418216014&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14671&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14671/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14671&quot;&gt;#14671&lt;/a&gt;). The Planner service account now always receives namespace-level &lt;code&gt;pods/list&lt;/code&gt; permission, and power awareness is controlled by &lt;code&gt;enable_power_awareness&lt;/code&gt; in the Planner configuration.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Remove the value from your Helm values file.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deprecated the doubled &lt;code&gt;DYN_HISTOGRAM_DYN_METRICS_*&lt;/code&gt; variable names&lt;/strong&gt;, which still work but log a warning (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5394339609&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14514&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14514/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14514&quot;&gt;#14514&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Use the documented &lt;code&gt;DYN_METRICS_*&lt;/code&gt; names.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Features &amp;amp; Improvements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend &amp;amp; Agents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responses Tool Selection Hardening:&lt;/strong&gt; Rejected unsupported tools and &lt;code&gt;tool_choice&lt;/code&gt; variants on &lt;code&gt;/v1/responses&lt;/code&gt; with an actionable HTTP 400 instead of dropping them silently (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5381184344&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14440&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14440/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14440&quot;&gt;#14440&lt;/a&gt;), supported function-only &lt;code&gt;tool_choice.allowed_tools&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5484683976&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14990&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14990/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14990&quot;&gt;#14990&lt;/a&gt;), removed text-based tool call inference from non-streaming responses (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5460286701&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14846&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14846/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14846&quot;&gt;#14846&lt;/a&gt;), and restored original function names and namespaces (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5640656654&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15401&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15401/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15401&quot;&gt;#15401&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Parsers V2 Structural Tags:&lt;/strong&gt; Added opt-in V2 parsers for GLM, DeepSeek V4/V4.1, Kimi K2/K3, Gemma 4, Muse, and Qwen3 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5478666328&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14950&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14950/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14950&quot;&gt;#14950&lt;/a&gt;), configured through &lt;code&gt;--dyn-structural-tag&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5820090263&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16217&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16217/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16217&quot;&gt;#16217&lt;/a&gt;). Structural tags are on by default for supported parsers (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5767478451&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15916&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15916/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15916&quot;&gt;#15916&lt;/a&gt;), and vLLM tool-call tags can start inside reasoning (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5820228669&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16220&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16220/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16220&quot;&gt;#16220&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KServe Tensor Protocol Fidelity:&lt;/strong&gt; Added half-precision &lt;code&gt;Float16&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;BFloat16&lt;/code&gt; KServe tensor variants (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5318286141&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14150&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14150/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14150&quot;&gt;#14150&lt;/a&gt;), reported &lt;code&gt;ModelMetadata&lt;/code&gt; datatypes by KServe v2 wire names (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5479612880&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14957&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14957/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14957&quot;&gt;#14957&lt;/a&gt;), and translated Triton &lt;code&gt;ModelConfig.dims&lt;/code&gt; to KServe shapes (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5485912885&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14996&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14996/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14996&quot;&gt;#14996&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Semantic Error HTTP Mapping:&lt;/strong&gt; Centralized semantic error mapping to HTTP status codes in Dynamo Frontend for protocol-correct OpenAI and Anthropic failures without internal diagnostics (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5363694701&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14396&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14396/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14396&quot;&gt;#14396&lt;/a&gt;), and extended the JSON error envelope to the remaining OpenAI routes (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5284046972&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14002&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14002/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14002&quot;&gt;#14002&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DeepSeek V4.1 Frontend Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Added mainline frontend support for DeepSeek V4.1 Flash reasoning and tool calling, enabled when workers pass both &lt;code&gt;--dyn-tool-call-parser deepseek_v41&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;--dyn-reasoning-parser deepseek_v41&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5494248284&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15030&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15030/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15030&quot;&gt;#15030&lt;/a&gt;), with native V4.1 image inputs and tool-result image ordering aligned to the rendered prompt by consuming the selected formatter&#39;s media order from &lt;code&gt;dynamo-renderer&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5507913248&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15097&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15097/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15097&quot;&gt;#15097&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SSE Streaming Lifecycle Hardening:&lt;/strong&gt; Reworked SSE streams to end on a hard kill, not a graceful stop, so delayed events still finish (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5417000286&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14645&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14645/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14645&quot;&gt;#14645&lt;/a&gt;), and made streaming handlers wait for the first backend event so an exception before output returns the non-streaming HTTP status (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5417944317&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14662&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14662/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14662&quot;&gt;#14662&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tokenizer Cache Lifecycle Hardening:&lt;/strong&gt; Replaced the process-global tokenizer pool with a weak-reference registry that shuts down each tokenizer&#39;s thread pool once collected (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5170832841&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13368&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13368/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13368&quot;&gt;#13368&lt;/a&gt;), and turned &lt;code&gt;DYN_TOKENIZER_CACHE_BYTES&lt;/code&gt; into one combined budget per process, keeping the 64 MiB default (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5636247640&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15387&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15387/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15387&quot;&gt;#15387&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Root-Level Thinking Token Budget:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a root-level &lt;code&gt;thinking_token_budget&lt;/code&gt; field to chat completion and Responses requests (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5057203596&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12624&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12624/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12624&quot;&gt;#12624&lt;/a&gt;) and carried it into SGLang, which requires strict-thinking mode and a reasoning parser (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5519875108&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15120&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15120/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15120&quot;&gt;#15120&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Cross-Encoder Reranking Endpoint:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an OpenAI-compatible &lt;code&gt;POST /v1/rerank&lt;/code&gt; endpoint for SGLang text-only cross-encoder models with a dedicated &lt;code&gt;--rerank-worker&lt;/code&gt; mode and support for &lt;code&gt;top_n&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5296873019&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14032&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14032/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14032&quot;&gt;#14032&lt;/a&gt;), and fixed scheduler crashes in rerank workers serving XLM-RoBERTa cross-encoders (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5825273120&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16286&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16286/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16286&quot;&gt;#16286&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend HTTP Mutual TLS:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a &lt;code&gt;--tls-client-ca-cert-path&lt;/code&gt; flag and &lt;code&gt;DYN_TLS_CLIENT_CA_CERT_PATH&lt;/code&gt; environment variable to the frontend HTTP server, requiring a CA-signed client certificate when set, with validation that rejects a client CA supplied without both a server certificate and key. Server-only TLS behavior remained unchanged (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5320628087&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14173&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14173/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14173&quot;&gt;#14173&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Opt-In Jemalloc Preload:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an opt-in jemalloc allocator preload for &lt;code&gt;python -m dynamo.frontend&lt;/code&gt;, activated by &lt;code&gt;DYN_FRONTEND_JEMALLOC=1&lt;/code&gt;, that continues with the default allocator when the library is missing (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5418751458&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14678&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14678/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14678&quot;&gt;#14678&lt;/a&gt;), with &lt;code&gt;libjemalloc2&lt;/code&gt; installed in the SGLang, TensorRT-LLM, and vLLM runtime images so the switch takes effect (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5132431011&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13101&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13101/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13101&quot;&gt;#13101&lt;/a&gt;) and documentation on bounding frontend host memory growth (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5132121322&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13099&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13099/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13099&quot;&gt;#13099&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Typed Chunk Metrics Path:&lt;/strong&gt; Carried chunk metrics in the typed &lt;code&gt;llm_metrics&lt;/code&gt; field instead of annotation comments, reducing mean inter-token latency by 6.21% with a 5.57% gain in output token throughput in a local A/B run (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5516290181&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15115&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15115/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15115&quot;&gt;#15115&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Opaque Agent Header Preservation:&lt;/strong&gt; Replaced the agent-compaction field with an &lt;code&gt;agent_headers&lt;/code&gt; map of the &lt;code&gt;x-claude-code-*&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;x-codex-*&lt;/code&gt; header families, so new coding-agent hints no longer require an envelope schema change (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5625486519&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15367&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15367/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15367&quot;&gt;#15367&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raw Completion Stop Preservation:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an optional &lt;code&gt;no_stop_trim&lt;/code&gt; field to &lt;code&gt;/v1/completions&lt;/code&gt; that retains matched stop strings and stop/EOS token text so callers can see terminal markers, defaulting to false (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5667315438&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15519&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15519/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15519&quot;&gt;#15519&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scheduling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Session Prefix Indexing and Lineage:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an opt-in session prefix index (&lt;code&gt;--enable-session-prefix-index&lt;/code&gt;) that tracks the KV blocks each session has built per worker and DP rank from vLLM KV events (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5252602419&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13807&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13807/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13807&quot;&gt;#13807&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5252601482&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13806&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13806/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13806&quot;&gt;#13806&lt;/a&gt;), hardened worker-removal handling and capped session identifiers at 256 bytes (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5623172707&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15362&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15362/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15362&quot;&gt;#15362&lt;/a&gt;), and grouped subagent requests under their parent session so they land on one worker (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5394819295&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14521&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14521/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14521&quot;&gt;#14521&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standalone EPP Routing Enablement:&lt;/strong&gt; Passed &lt;code&gt;expected_output_tokens&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;policy_class&lt;/code&gt; from the standalone endpoint picker (EPP) into its selection service (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5201950202&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13595&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13595/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13595&quot;&gt;#13595&lt;/a&gt;), routed runtime EPP requests by the &lt;code&gt;x-dynamo-meta-policy-class&lt;/code&gt; header (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5389991071&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14480&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14480/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14480&quot;&gt;#14480&lt;/a&gt;), added cache namespace and salt resolution (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5236092286&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13714&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13714/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13714&quot;&gt;#13714&lt;/a&gt;) and &lt;code&gt;sglang-renderer&lt;/code&gt; tokenizer support (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5392766928&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14501&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14501/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14501&quot;&gt;#14501&lt;/a&gt;), and made native EPP atomically reserve KV-routed prefill capacity (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5123796543&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13042&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13042/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13042&quot;&gt;#13042&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pluggable Router Flow Control:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a pluggable request-classifier hook to the KV Router that can defer a request, override scheduling inputs, or suggest a worker without overriding explicit pins (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5315591177&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14123&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14123/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14123&quot;&gt;#14123&lt;/a&gt;), with a deadline-ordered policy queue for every request (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5321142073&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14176&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14176/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14176&quot;&gt;#14176&lt;/a&gt;), async classifier lifecycle events (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5321142597&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14177&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14177/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14177&quot;&gt;#14177&lt;/a&gt;), and one plugin registration catalog (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5318116777&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14149&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14149/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14149&quot;&gt;#14149&lt;/a&gt;). Skipped capacity checks for policy classes with queueing disabled (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5649883752&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15423&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15423/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15423&quot;&gt;#15423&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ThunderAgent Builtin Router Plugin:&lt;/strong&gt; Shipped ThunderAgent as a builtin router plugin enabled through &lt;code&gt;--router-policy-config&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5535805009&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15164&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15164/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15164&quot;&gt;#15164&lt;/a&gt;), made its cost model DP-rank aware so SGLang data-parallel attention workers no longer fail program-lifecycle requests (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5283760437&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14000&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14000/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14000&quot;&gt;#14000&lt;/a&gt;), and made it honor the Router&#39;s pinned worker and check that worker&#39;s live capacity (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5598789985&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15290&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15290/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15290&quot;&gt;#15290&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KV Router Slot Tracker Recovery:&lt;/strong&gt; Cut slot tracker overhead by sharding its locks (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5669674233&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15531&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15531/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15531&quot;&gt;#15531&lt;/a&gt;), tied standalone replica sync to each request&#39;s reservation so peer routers no longer see a re-added request&#39;s prefill as complete (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5681645233&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15578&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15578/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15578&quot;&gt;#15578&lt;/a&gt;), reworked the recovery snapshot cache (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5673224616&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15551&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15551/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15551&quot;&gt;#15551&lt;/a&gt;), and restored buffer-first gap recovery that keeps the existing index on a KV event gap (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5415688128&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14627&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14627/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14627&quot;&gt;#14627&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planner GPU Budget Enforcement:&lt;/strong&gt; Added runtime reconfiguration of endpoint floors and &lt;code&gt;min_gpu_budget&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;max_gpu_budget&lt;/code&gt; bounds through &lt;code&gt;PATCH /v1/min-endpoints&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5329301264&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14218&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14218/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14218&quot;&gt;#14218&lt;/a&gt;), treated &lt;code&gt;min_gpu_budget&lt;/code&gt; as a scale-down guard (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5330021870&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14231&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14231/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14231&quot;&gt;#14231&lt;/a&gt;), and preserved the decode replica count when a raised GPU floor would reduce it (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5655963502&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15466&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15466/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15466&quot;&gt;#15466&lt;/a&gt;). Applied &lt;code&gt;min_endpoint&lt;/code&gt; in single-pool load scaling (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5669615608&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15530&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15530/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15530&quot;&gt;#15530&lt;/a&gt;) and distinguished startup from drain and rollout so falling demand cannot cancel pending capacity or drain serving workers (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5418216014&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14671&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14671/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14671&quot;&gt;#14671&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planner Gym Autoscaler Evaluation:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an experimental Planner Gym under &lt;code&gt;gyms/planner-gym&lt;/code&gt; that compares Planner, KEDA/HPA-style, reactive, and static autoscaling policies (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5681479529&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15576&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15576/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15576&quot;&gt;#15576&lt;/a&gt;), resolved its defaults through the production Planner configuration (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5719657494&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15678&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15678/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15678&quot;&gt;#15678&lt;/a&gt;), and removed stale offline replay restrictions so Planner policies run on agentic Mooncake and Dynamo or Weka traces (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5650763598&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15435&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15435/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15435&quot;&gt;#15435&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Phase-Aware Prefill Accounting:&lt;/strong&gt; Gated prefill-start recording off for decode-only requests (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5293329953&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14019&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14019/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14019&quot;&gt;#14019&lt;/a&gt;), moved SGLang prefill completion to after the background prefill stream ends (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5480708574&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14968&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14968/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14968&quot;&gt;#14968&lt;/a&gt;), and fixed output-block undercounting across block boundaries and batched those updates (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5411192003&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14613&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14613/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14613&quot;&gt;#14613&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5652988971&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15448&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15448/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15448&quot;&gt;#15448&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct ZMQ Subscriber Multiplexing:&lt;/strong&gt; Added opt-in fan-in via &lt;code&gt;DYN_ROUTER_ZMQ_ENDPOINTS_PER_SUB&lt;/code&gt; so direct-ZMQ subscribers share one SUB socket across many publisher endpoints (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5329327024&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14219&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14219/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14219&quot;&gt;#14219&lt;/a&gt;), and coalesced pending KV load metrics (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5684967713&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15587&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15587/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15587&quot;&gt;#15587&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standalone Indexer Lifecycle Delegates:&lt;/strong&gt; Added ownership callbacks to the standalone KV indexer that notify consumers when a block hash gains its first owner or its last owner releases it (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5477377119&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14945&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14945/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14945&quot;&gt;#14945&lt;/a&gt;), made cleanup safe for absent blocks and backpressure (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5417395569&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14652&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14652/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14652&quot;&gt;#14652&lt;/a&gt;), and bounded the KV state-agent discovery wait at vLLM startup (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5284564333&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14003&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14003/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14003&quot;&gt;#14003&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unified Selection Core:&lt;/strong&gt; Unified Dynamo Frontend, standalone selection service, and EPP worker selection on one shared core (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5406232938&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14570&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14570/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14570&quot;&gt;#14570&lt;/a&gt;) and reduced scheduler and dispatch overhead for large worker pools (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5417975573&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14666&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14666/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14666&quot;&gt;#14666&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TokenSpeed Disaggregation with KV Routing:&lt;/strong&gt; Added prefill/decode disaggregation for the TokenSpeed backend over Mooncake and published native KV-cache events, so the Router can send prompts to the prefill worker already holding their prefix. Included bootstrap validation and transfer-error handling (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4395004710&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/9237&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/9237/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/9237&quot;&gt;#9237&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Native KV Cache Events:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a native TensorRT-LLM KV cache event mode that subscribes directly to each attention-DP rank&#39;s ZMQ stream, bypassing the legacy polling and republishing path (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4976085724&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12167&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12167/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12167&quot;&gt;#12167&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Throughput Scaling Replica Cap:&lt;/strong&gt; Added the &lt;code&gt;max_throughput_scaling_replicas&lt;/code&gt; Planner configuration option, defaulting to 8, and applied it per component to both throughput scale-up and scale-down targets, with capped targets fitted against GPU and power ceilings while preserving explicit endpoint and out-of-band budget recovery (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5342307544&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14296&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14296/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14296&quot;&gt;#14296&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relay WAN gRPC Transport:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a &lt;code&gt;dynamo.kvrelay.v1&lt;/code&gt; Protobuf contract and WAN adapter so consumers outside a data center can subscribe to cache locality, readiness, and KV occupancy streams through an opt-in listener (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5359914540&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14379&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14379/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14379&quot;&gt;#14379&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Router KV Hints Envelope:&lt;/strong&gt; Passed Router-produced KV hints to vLLM through vLLM&#39;s dedicated KV-hints request argument, keeping hint data separate from the KV connector&#39;s &lt;code&gt;kv_transfer_params&lt;/code&gt; on token, text, and prefill paths. In prefill/decode deployments the hint is applied once on the prefill worker, and decode handoff requests no longer replay it (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5467982422&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14890&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14890/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14890&quot;&gt;#14890&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Centralized Router Policy Configuration:&lt;/strong&gt; Moved Router scoring knobs into &lt;code&gt;--router-policy-config&lt;/code&gt; with a &lt;code&gt;router&lt;/code&gt; section for shared cache settings, deprecated the six scoring flags and &lt;code&gt;--load-aware&lt;/code&gt; while their behavior remains available for migration, and removed &lt;code&gt;router_credit_blocks&lt;/code&gt; from the overlap-query response (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5547780005&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15202&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15202/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15202&quot;&gt;#15202&lt;/a&gt;). Added a &lt;code&gt;soft-pin-repin&lt;/code&gt; policy example for soft session-affinity rebinding (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5318394710&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14152&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14152/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14152&quot;&gt;#14152&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Worker KV Reuse Telemetry:&lt;/strong&gt; Added router metrics for KV cache reuse per routing attempt across SGLang, TensorRT-LLM, and vLLM, labeled by &lt;code&gt;phase&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;model&lt;/code&gt;, so operators can compare routed prompt tokens against engine cache hits (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5652126501&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15443&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15443/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15443&quot;&gt;#15443&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KV Block Manager&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;File-Based Relay Source Mode:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a &lt;code&gt;--sources-file&lt;/code&gt; option to KV DC Relay that selects Dynamo namespaces from a versioned JSON file with live reload, and an &lt;code&gt;/engine/state&lt;/code&gt; route reporting readiness (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5453272404&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14807&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14807/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14807&quot;&gt;#14807&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal &amp;amp; Diffusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nemotron Omni Multimodal Routing:&lt;/strong&gt; Added exact multimodal KV routing for Nemotron 3 Nano Omni images by modeling vLLM dynamic-resolution geometry and model-specific delimiters (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5405563478&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14564&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14564/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14564&quot;&gt;#14564&lt;/a&gt;), and for video by sampling and decoding frames and grouping them into temporal tubelets (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5417427458&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14653&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14653/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14653&quot;&gt;#14653&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cascaded Nemotron Speech Example:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a self-contained deployment example exposing Nemotron ASR, LLM, and TTS endpoints through &lt;code&gt;/v1/realtime&lt;/code&gt; transcription and streaming &lt;code&gt;/v1/audio/speech&lt;/code&gt;, with a three-GPU DynamoGraphDeployment and a smoke client (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5050017996&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12567&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12567/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12567&quot;&gt;#12567&lt;/a&gt;), and added a client-driven ASR-to-LLM handoff for speculative prefix-cache warming (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5348764699&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14327&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14327/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14327&quot;&gt;#14327&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Omni Video Parameter Plumbing:&lt;/strong&gt; Preserved joint video-and-audio output from vLLM-Omni with per-output frame rate and audio sample rate metadata (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5230479845&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13707&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13707/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13707&quot;&gt;#13707&lt;/a&gt;), cloned sampling parameters so request-specific video controls do not leak across requests (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5230480767&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13708&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13708/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13708&quot;&gt;#13708&lt;/a&gt;), and forwarded &lt;code&gt;response_format&lt;/code&gt; so &lt;code&gt;b64_json&lt;/code&gt; is no longer dropped (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5459103782&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14844&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14844/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14844&quot;&gt;#14844&lt;/a&gt;). Also fixed the HTTP 500 on video requests carrying &lt;code&gt;nvext.negative_prompt&lt;/code&gt; and carried the value to the first-stage engine prompt (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5640878698&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15402&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15402/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15402&quot;&gt;#15402&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5671058226&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15541&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15541/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15541&quot;&gt;#15541&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MiniMax-H3 FastH3 Video Enablement:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a four-B200 aggregated vLLM-Omni launcher for MiniMax-H3 text-to-video-and-audio generation with the four-step Dense FastH3 startup adapter (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5200213785&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13589&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13589/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13589&quot;&gt;#13589&lt;/a&gt;), then enabled MiniMax-H3 video sparse attention (VSA) on vLLM-Omni with the &lt;code&gt;--fastvideo-vsa-topk&lt;/code&gt; option and B200 and GB300 hardware guards (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5421798834&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14702&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14702/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14702&quot;&gt;#14702&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shared Encoded-Image Cache Hardening:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an opt-in shared cache of encoded image bytes in Redis Cluster or Dragonfly, failing open on any cache error (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5418614375&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14676&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14676/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14676&quot;&gt;#14676&lt;/a&gt;). Fixed case-differing S3 and GCS paths collapsing onto one image cache entry (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5510341592&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15101&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15101/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15101&quot;&gt;#15101&lt;/a&gt;), made the embedding cache evict only while it needs space (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5664484927&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15497&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15497/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15497&quot;&gt;#15497&lt;/a&gt;), and stopped the NIXL embedding ring buffer from overlapping a live embedding (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5664594420&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15498&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15498/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15498&quot;&gt;#15498&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM External Encoder Handoff:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a public &lt;code&gt;ExternalEncoderHandoff&lt;/code&gt; API so external encoders built on &lt;code&gt;VisionEncoderBackend&lt;/code&gt; reuse Dynamo&#39;s image extraction and prompt reconstruction (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5156767651&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13293&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13293/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13293&quot;&gt;#13293&lt;/a&gt;), forwarded preprocessed multimodal features to vLLM&#39;s gRPC API (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5331050118&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14244&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14244/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14244&quot;&gt;#14244&lt;/a&gt;), and moved multimodal tensor transfer from pickle to typed msgpack (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5379924793&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14433&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14433/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14433&quot;&gt;#14433&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal UUID and Media Deduplication:&lt;/strong&gt; Extended client-provided multimodal UUID forwarding from images to all modalities for vLLM-based deployments (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5342476087&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14300&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14300/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14300&quot;&gt;#14300&lt;/a&gt;), and stopped inline &lt;code&gt;data:&lt;/code&gt; media from being sent twice on the TCP request plane (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5451998206&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14801&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14801/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14801&quot;&gt;#14801&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nemotron Audex Speech Synthesis:&lt;/strong&gt; Added Nemotron Audex text-to-speech support to the vLLM-Omni backend on the existing &lt;code&gt;/v1/audio/speech&lt;/code&gt; endpoint, covering &lt;code&gt;nvidia/Nemotron-Labs-Audex-2B&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;nvidia/Nemotron-Labs-Audex-30B-A3B&lt;/code&gt;. Added &lt;code&gt;cfg_scale&lt;/code&gt; to the frontend and worker request models for classifier-free guidance, and fixed cumulative waveform assembly so Audex requests no longer return silent or over-length audio (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5085390922&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12788&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12788/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12788&quot;&gt;#12788&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Qwen Video KV Routing:&lt;/strong&gt; Added video-aware KV cache routing for Qwen models on SGLang, mirroring SGLang&#39;s frame sampling in the frontend so repeated video requests hit cached prefix blocks (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5491739089&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15014&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15014/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15014&quot;&gt;#15014&lt;/a&gt;). Extended the Multimodal KV Routing guide with video identity handling, documenting vLLM support for Qwen3-VL, Qwen3.5, and Nemotron 3 Nano Omni (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5479668292&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14958&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14958/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14958&quot;&gt;#14958&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes Deployment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LPX Integration and Partition Selection:&lt;/strong&gt; Added the LPX component type for LPU-backed inference across API, controller, runtime, scheduler, Grove, and Helm (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5502287558&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15062&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15062/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15062&quot;&gt;#15062&lt;/a&gt;), let hybrid XT and HX (LP30) builds run some or all partitions on the Cyborg GPU via &lt;code&gt;lpx.experimental.localPartitions&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5678584933&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15563&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15563/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15563&quot;&gt;#15563&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5728819607&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15706&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15706/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15706&quot;&gt;#15706&lt;/a&gt;), packed LPU-only PropSync partitions into whole-node allocations (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5683335995&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15583&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15583/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15583&quot;&gt;#15583&lt;/a&gt;), and fixed HX hybrid deployments (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5742633491&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15804&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15804/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15804&quot;&gt;#15804&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rolling LPX Build Updates:&lt;/strong&gt; Routed compatible &lt;code&gt;lpx.buildId&lt;/code&gt; changes through Grove rolling updates so remaining replicas keep serving (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5701742093&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15607&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15607/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15607&quot;&gt;#15607&lt;/a&gt;), and excluded &lt;code&gt;RollingUpdate&lt;/code&gt; from the layout comparison so an unchanged PodCliqueSet is no longer recreated (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5718981900&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15672&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15672/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15672&quot;&gt;#15672&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role-Specific Multinode PodTemplate API:&lt;/strong&gt; Activated the &lt;code&gt;roles[].podTemplate&lt;/code&gt; API for multinode &lt;code&gt;worker&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;prefill&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;decode&lt;/code&gt; components so leader and worker Pods can come from different complete PodTemplates (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5385558718&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14468&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14468/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14468&quot;&gt;#14468&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5402574368&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14544&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14544/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14544&quot;&gt;#14544&lt;/a&gt;), added an explicit &lt;code&gt;roles[].replicas&lt;/code&gt; surface for role cardinality (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5389268699&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14477&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14477/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14477&quot;&gt;#14477&lt;/a&gt;), and restricted &lt;code&gt;multinode&lt;/code&gt; to inference-engine component types (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5397917678&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14533&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14533/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14533&quot;&gt;#14533&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Snapshot CUDA Shared Memory Capture:&lt;/strong&gt; Enabled CUDA shared-memory Snapshot capture so workers no longer disable NCCL cuMem, NVLS or TensorRT-LLM zero-copy, and existing checkpoints are recaptured because the compatibility hash includes the annotation (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5739021653&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15791&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15791/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15791&quot;&gt;#15791&lt;/a&gt;), with SGLang, TensorRT-LLM, and vLLM (v0.31.0 and later) releasing only the KV cache before capture instead of moving weights to host memory, which shrinks checkpoints and speeds restores (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5838182229&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16358&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16358/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16358&quot;&gt;#16358&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Snapshot-Backed Engine Failover:&lt;/strong&gt; Added snapshot-backed engine failover for SGLang and vLLM, including single-node multi-GPU workers, that replenishes a failed engine without replacing the worker Pod, with unsupported snapshot failover backends rejected at admission (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5768436382&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15924&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15924/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15924&quot;&gt;#15924&lt;/a&gt;), and propagated the compatibility hash to &lt;code&gt;WaitForCheckpoint&lt;/code&gt; references (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5890255902&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16687&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16687/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16687&quot;&gt;#16687&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Intel XPU GMS Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Added Intel XPU support to the GPU Memory Service (GMS), using Level-Zero interop for inter-process memory sharing, a C++ extension for tensor reconstruction, and SGLang and vLLM integration paths. XPU support runs on native torch.xpu with no IPEX dependency and requires PyTorch 2.13 or newer (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5028397243&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12484&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12484/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12484&quot;&gt;#12484&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GA Helm OCI Publishing:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a push of GA Helm charts to the NGC OCI registry alongside the existing ChartMuseum push, so consumers on OCI-only registries such as ACR, ECR, and Harbor can mirror released charts (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5218298645&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13657&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13657/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13657&quot;&gt;#13657&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KVCR Resiliency Deployment Example:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a two-node vLLM KV Cache Reuse (KVCR) example over RDMA. The memory-service sidecar keeps the KVCR Guard available across engine restarts (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5420136058&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14695&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14695/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14695&quot;&gt;#14695&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EPP Multi-Replica Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Removed the admission rule that restricted the Dynamo-mode endpoint picker (EPP) to exactly one replica, so native Rust EPP deployments can scale out and tolerate pod loss like the Frontend-hosted Router, while legacy Go EPP deployments still require a single replica. &lt;code&gt;DYN_ROUTER_REPLICA_SYNC&lt;/code&gt; remained off by default, matching the Frontend behavior (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5429909392&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14758&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14758/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14758&quot;&gt;#14758&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Portable Multinode Topology Variables:&lt;/strong&gt; Added &lt;code&gt;DYNAMO_RANK&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;DYNAMO_LEADER_ADDRESS&lt;/code&gt; to new multinode components so SGLang and vLLM commands no longer depend on Grove or LeaderWorkerSet syntax. Injection is gated on the operator origin version, so existing deployments keep their current environment and command lines, and Grove was upgraded to &lt;code&gt;v0.1.0-alpha.14&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5631128275&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15374&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15374/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15374&quot;&gt;#15374&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5728458702&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15704&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15704/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15704&quot;&gt;#15704&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo Sidecar&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dynamo Sidecar remains experimental in Dynamo v1.6.0.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Sidecar LoRA Lifecycle:&lt;/strong&gt; Added dynamic LoRA load, unload, and per-request adapter selection to the vLLM sidecar, with local, Hugging Face, and S3 adapters and no silent base-model fallback for unavailable adapters (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5126025545&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13068&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13068/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13068&quot;&gt;#13068&lt;/a&gt;). Added aggregated and NIXL prefill/decode launchers for local LoRA serving (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5406368072&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14574&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14574/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14574&quot;&gt;#14574&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM OpenEngine gRPC Sidecar:&lt;/strong&gt; Moved the TensorRT-LLM sidecar onto TensorRT-LLM&#39;s OpenEngine (&lt;code&gt;openengine.v1&lt;/code&gt;) gRPC API and added disaggregated serving (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5353127902&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14349&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14349/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14349&quot;&gt;#14349&lt;/a&gt;). Raised the shared sidecar gRPC startup deadline from 300 to 1,800 seconds for large model loads (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5455723400&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14825&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14825/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14825&quot;&gt;#14825&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Sidecar EPD Encode Role:&lt;/strong&gt; Added opt-in Encoder-Prefill-Decode support to the native vLLM gRPC sidecar with E+PD and E+P+D launchers (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5280409993&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13966&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13966/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13966&quot;&gt;#13966&lt;/a&gt;). Extended the Encode worker to accept video and combined image plus video requests (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5598176489&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15287&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15287/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15287&quot;&gt;#15287&lt;/a&gt;), and shipped the FFmpeg binaries video decode needs for VP8 and VP9 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5871972596&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16556&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16556/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16556&quot;&gt;#16556&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Sidecar KV Routing:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a disaggregated KV-aware routing launcher for SGLang sidecars (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5261159828&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13862&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13862/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13862&quot;&gt;#13862&lt;/a&gt;) and node-local KV event relay for multinode headless sidecars (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5468910816&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14908&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14908/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14908&quot;&gt;#14908&lt;/a&gt;). Published HiCache capacity so capacity-aware routers no longer treat HiCache workers as device-only (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5344155645&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14313&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14313/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14313&quot;&gt;#14313&lt;/a&gt;) and an EAGLE flag so KV routers use the engine&#39;s bigram hashing (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5355078761&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14374&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14374/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14374&quot;&gt;#14374&lt;/a&gt;), and moved the prefill bootstrap handoff into a nonterminal response (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5339047246&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14260&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14260/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14260&quot;&gt;#14260&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal-Aware vLLM KV Routing:&lt;/strong&gt; Resolved the image placeholder token for the vLLM KV event publisher, so repeated image requests match cached image blocks instead of only the text prefix. The token resolves once at startup with a 30 second fetch limit, and image requests fall back to text-prefix routing if resolution fails (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5168960438&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13360&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13360/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13360&quot;&gt;#13360&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standalone Decode Sidecar Contract:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a standalone decode sidecar for the inference gateway that validates &lt;code&gt;x-prefiller-host-port&lt;/code&gt; metadata so client-supplied prefill metadata cannot reach endpoint selection (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5219634755&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13669&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13669/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13669&quot;&gt;#13669&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engine-Primary Dynamo Native Sidecars:&lt;/strong&gt; Added operator support for separate inference engine and Dynamo runtime containers, selected per component via an init container named &lt;code&gt;runtime&lt;/code&gt;, while combined mode remains the default (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5471236822&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14927&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14927/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14927&quot;&gt;#14927&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shared Sidecar Transport Flags:&lt;/strong&gt; Added &lt;code&gt;--discovery-backend&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;--request-plane&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;--response-plane&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;--event-plane&lt;/code&gt; to the SGLang, TensorRT-LLM, and vLLM sidecars, so workers select &lt;code&gt;file&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;tcp&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;quic&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;zmq&lt;/code&gt; directly (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5717387826&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15653&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15653/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15653&quot;&gt;#15653&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sharded SGLang Worker Gateway:&lt;/strong&gt; Added &lt;code&gt;--gateway-workers&lt;/code&gt; to shard the &lt;code&gt;dynamo.sglang&lt;/code&gt; gateway across processes so tokenizer intake and output relay no longer share one GIL (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5506014621&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15078&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15078/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15078&quot;&gt;#15078&lt;/a&gt;), and fixed a startup &lt;code&gt;AttributeError&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5836117406&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16337&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16337/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16337&quot;&gt;#16337&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Cache Salt Routing:&lt;/strong&gt; Added cache salt support for SGLang text workers so differently salted requests use separate KV cache entries. Non-empty salts are rejected when the installed engine or request type cannot honor them. Upgrade all workers and routers before enabling salted traffic (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5452162496&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14803&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14803/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14803&quot;&gt;#14803&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generate Endpoint RL Parity:&lt;/strong&gt; Added reinforcement learning (RL) serving parity for the &lt;code&gt;dynamo.vllm&lt;/code&gt; worker in aggregated deployments, adapting native Generate token-in/token-out requests and publishing RL administration routes (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5543417152&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15179&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15179/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15179&quot;&gt;#15179&lt;/a&gt;). Carried typed &lt;code&gt;/inference/v1/generate&lt;/code&gt; controls such as sampling, stop-token IDs, and logprobs into Dynamo&#39;s internal request, preserving requests from v1.4 frontends (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5364381294&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14398&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14398/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14398&quot;&gt;#14398&lt;/a&gt;), with a fix that sent &lt;code&gt;top_k&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;min_p&lt;/code&gt; as unset when clients did not disable them (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5598175553&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15286&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15286/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15286&quot;&gt;#15286&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LMCacheMPConnector PD Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Registered a connector adapter so vLLM prefill/decode disaggregation works with &lt;code&gt;LMCacheMPConnector&lt;/code&gt;, which previously failed at request time with an unsupported connector error. Wrapper resolution now prefers a connector that produces KV transfer parameters, so &lt;code&gt;MultiConnector&lt;/code&gt; setups combining LMCacheMP with NixlConnector still resolve to NIXL (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5153721264&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13258&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13258/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13258&quot;&gt;#13258&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incremental Realtime Text Input:&lt;/strong&gt; Added text-only &lt;code&gt;/v1/realtime&lt;/code&gt; sessions to aggregated vLLM workers, with experimental input events so clients can forward ASR text during transcription and commit the final transcript (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5348552514&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14326&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14326/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14326&quot;&gt;#14326&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Triton&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FP16/BF16 Tensor Input Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Dropped the &lt;code&gt;dynamo.triton&lt;/code&gt; guard that rejected FP16 and BF16 inputs (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5456618462&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14835&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14835/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14835&quot;&gt;#14835&lt;/a&gt;), reinterpreted their values from raw &lt;code&gt;uint16&lt;/code&gt; bit patterns (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5889290289&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16683&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16683/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16683&quot;&gt;#16683&lt;/a&gt;), and passed BF16 as a raw-byte tensor (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5872325463&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16558&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16558/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16558&quot;&gt;#16558&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KServe Classification Output Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Added support for the KServe &lt;code&gt;classification&lt;/code&gt; requested-output parameter on the Triton worker and forwarded requested outputs from the frontend (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5414082562&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14618&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14618/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14618&quot;&gt;#14618&lt;/a&gt;), so the worker returns only the named tensors (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5445463185&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14783&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14783/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14783&quot;&gt;#14783&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Defunct Triton Example Removal:&lt;/strong&gt; Removed the out-of-date Triton Inference Server backend example, including its Dockerfile, launch scripts, model repository, and worker implementation. The Dynamo Triton Runtime under &lt;code&gt;components/src/dynamo/triton&lt;/code&gt; replaces it (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5541455032&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15170&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15170/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15170&quot;&gt;#15170&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Triton Classification Endpoint Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Added OpenAI-compatible &lt;code&gt;POST /v1/classify&lt;/code&gt; serving to the Triton backend, opt-in through &lt;code&gt;--task classify&lt;/code&gt; with input and output tensor names auto-detected from &lt;code&gt;config.pbtxt&lt;/code&gt; and overridable via &lt;code&gt;--classify-input-name&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;--classify-output-name&lt;/code&gt;. The default &lt;code&gt;--task tensor&lt;/code&gt; KServe path is unchanged, and text-only input is supported while token-ID variants and &lt;code&gt;encoding_format&lt;/code&gt; requests return HTTP 400 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5639399913&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15396&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15396/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15396&quot;&gt;#15396&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Model Loading &amp;amp; LoRA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Native LoRA Capacity Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Exposed native vLLM LoRA capacity through shared model registration, so a worker reporting &lt;code&gt;max_loras=4&lt;/code&gt; carries &lt;code&gt;max_gpu_lora_count=4&lt;/code&gt; into discovery (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5429647939&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14754&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14754/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14754&quot;&gt;#14754&lt;/a&gt;), and corrected LoRA allocation simulation with capacity-bounded adapter residency and churn, hit, and occupancy metrics (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5243057705&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13758&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13758/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13758&quot;&gt;#13758&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shared NGC Model Fetching:&lt;/strong&gt; Added shared NGC model fetching through ModelExpress for SGLang and vLLM, reusing cached models (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5651475513&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15441&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15441/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15441&quot;&gt;#15441&lt;/a&gt;). Local models served under custom names no longer trigger &lt;code&gt;hf://&lt;/code&gt; metadata fetches on offline hosts (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5773509041&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15964&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15964/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15964&quot;&gt;#15964&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Modeling &amp;amp; Replay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Typed Agentic Replay Adapters:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a streaming Weka importer in &lt;code&gt;dynamo-data-gen&lt;/code&gt;, lowered Weka and Claude/Codex/Dynamo request traces into versioned Agentic Mooncake v2 rows, and added Dynamo replay entrypoints for typed agentic lanes (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5199360837&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13586&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13586/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13586&quot;&gt;#13586&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Codex and Claude Trace Export:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an offline Codex trace exporter for agentic replay alongside the Claude exporter and fixed Claude export so a full local corpus replays. Claude export on a 216 MB project dropped from 49 s to 2.6 s and peak RSS from 2.3 GB to 1.3 GB (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5693273332&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15601&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15601/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15601&quot;&gt;#15601&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mocker Host-Memory KV Offload:&lt;/strong&gt; Wired AISimulate&#39;s vLLM host-memory KV offload into the Mocker with tier-aware KV routing, so the Router tracks host-resident blocks and &lt;code&gt;--num-host-blocks&lt;/code&gt; alone enables host offload (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5716210269&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15647&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15647/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15647&quot;&gt;#15647&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AISimulate Canonical Configuration:&lt;/strong&gt; Moved performance-model consumers across the Planner, Profiler, Router, Frontend, Mocker, and replay to AISimulate&#39;s canonical configuration interface, carrying complete configurations through Planner roles and the related CLI consumers (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5502358375&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15063&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15063/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15063&quot;&gt;#15063&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fault Tolerance &amp;amp; Observability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend NUMA Affinity Warning:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a startup check that warns when the frontend&#39;s allowed CPUs span multiple NUMA nodes, a likely source of degraded performance (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4797506509&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11184&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11184/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11184&quot;&gt;#11184&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tokio Queue Overload Warnings:&lt;/strong&gt; Added detection of sustained Tokio runnable-queue pressure in the runtime metrics loop, with worker-scaled thresholds, hot-worker detection, hysteresis, and sample-gap checks. Warnings log once per overload episode and repeat at most every five minutes while it continues, and the count is exported as &lt;code&gt;dynamo_tokio_queue_overload_warnings_total&lt;/code&gt; for operators (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5122461946&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13027&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13027/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13027&quot;&gt;#13027&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OTLP Metrics Export:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a periodic OTLP exporter that ships Dynamo and engine metrics to a collector over gRPC, configured through standard &lt;code&gt;OTEL_*&lt;/code&gt; variables and off unless &lt;code&gt;OTEL_METRICS_EXPORTER=otlp&lt;/code&gt; is set (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5304130881&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14071&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14071/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14071&quot;&gt;#14071&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Per-Request Lifecycle Instrumentation:&lt;/strong&gt; Added opt-in runtime tracing that models each inference request as a finite-state machine, recording state timing and terminal outcome for aggregated and disaggregated serving (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5308557247&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14101&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14101/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14101&quot;&gt;#14101&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Buffered JSONL FPM Recording:&lt;/strong&gt; Added &lt;code&gt;--output&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;--log-metrics&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;--flush-interval&lt;/code&gt; options to the forward pass metrics (FPM) receiver, writing one JSON record per message to a new file and flushing on an interval (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5393633193&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14511&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14511/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14511&quot;&gt;#14511&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NVTX Ranges in Wheels:&lt;/strong&gt; Compiled the runtime&#39;s NVTX ranges into published wheels, so the &lt;code&gt;preprocess.*&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;route.*&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;transport.*&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;detokenize&lt;/code&gt; ranges appear in Nsight reports when &lt;code&gt;DYN_ENABLE_RUST_NVTX&lt;/code&gt; is set, and removed the dependency on &lt;code&gt;libnvToolsExt.so&lt;/code&gt;, which CUDA 12.9 dropped (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5560578772&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15242&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15242/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15242&quot;&gt;#15242&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Runtime &amp;amp; Transport&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Request-Plane Transport Configuration Hardening:&lt;/strong&gt; Added &lt;code&gt;DYN_EVENT_PLANE_HOST&lt;/code&gt; to override the address advertised by direct ZMQ event publishers (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4916455080&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11870&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11870/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11870&quot;&gt;#11870&lt;/a&gt;). Restricted &lt;code&gt;DYN_REQUEST_PLANE&lt;/code&gt; to default to TCP only when absent, so invalid values surface as startup errors (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5055134781&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12612&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12612/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12612&quot;&gt;#12612&lt;/a&gt;), and defaulted the event-plane context to four libzmq I/O threads with a &lt;code&gt;DYN_ZMQ_IO_THREADS&lt;/code&gt; override (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5394471600&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14517&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14517/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14517&quot;&gt;#14517&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Configurable Etcd Startup Retry:&lt;/strong&gt; Made the etcd startup retry timeout configurable, keeping 120 seconds as the default and bounding each individual connection attempt by the remaining retry window (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5240862065&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13742&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13742/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13742&quot;&gt;#13742&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Batched QUIC Response Transport:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an opt-in batched QUIC response plane selected with &lt;code&gt;--response-plane quic&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;DYN_RESPONSE_PLANE=quic&lt;/code&gt; on each frontend and worker. TCP remains the default (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4944484713&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11996&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11996/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11996&quot;&gt;#11996&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Packed Int32 Token IDs:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an opt-in &lt;code&gt;DYN_TOKEN_IDS_AS_BYTES&lt;/code&gt; flag that serializes &lt;code&gt;token_ids&lt;/code&gt; as a packed int32 blob on request-plane codecs. It must stay off until all msgpack workers run a release containing the new reader (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5618713704&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15326&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15326/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15326&quot;&gt;#15326&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unary Endpoint Helper APIs:&lt;/strong&gt; Added unary endpoint utilities that serve a handler result and collect unary responses and LLM token streams while preserving request context (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5107154097&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12920&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12920/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12920&quot;&gt;#12920&lt;/a&gt;), then promoted them to &lt;code&gt;dynamo.runtime&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;dynamo.llm&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5546573264&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15195&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15195/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15195&quot;&gt;#15195&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shared Prompt Token Storage:&lt;/strong&gt; Made copies of a preprocessed request share one prompt-token buffer, reducing clone cost for disaggregated prefill and migration, though direct Rust consumers of &lt;code&gt;token_ids&lt;/code&gt; may need adaptation (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5421041795&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14701&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14701/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14701&quot;&gt;#14701&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unary Chat Model Publisher:&lt;/strong&gt; Added &lt;code&gt;UnaryChatModel&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;dynamo.llm&lt;/code&gt;, which registers and serves a Chat model endpoint, plus &lt;code&gt;LLMUnaryClient.connect&lt;/code&gt;, which waits for a routable instance (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5673573998&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15552&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15552/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15552&quot;&gt;#15552&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recipes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;New Recipes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813 vLLM Recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; The GB200 recipes require the custom &lt;a href=&quot;https://catalog.ngc.nvidia.com/orgs/nvidia/teams/ai-dynamo/containers/vllm-runtime/tags&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;vllm-runtime:1.5.0-deepseek-v4-pro-0813-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; container. Added aggregated and disaggregated recipes for &lt;code&gt;deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813&lt;/code&gt; on H200 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5250397726&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13783&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13783/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13783&quot;&gt;#13783&lt;/a&gt;), relaxed GB200 prefill liveness probing so vLLM JIT kernel compilation no longer triggers a crashloop (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5427379321&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14735&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14735/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14735&quot;&gt;#14735&lt;/a&gt;), and replaced the removed &lt;code&gt;use_fp4_indexer_cache&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;indexer_kv_dtype: mxfp4&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5649954923&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15427&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15427/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15427&quot;&gt;#15427&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A.X-K2 vLLM Recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Requires the custom &lt;a href=&quot;https://catalog.ngc.nvidia.com/orgs/nvidia/teams/ai-dynamo/containers/vllm-runtime/tags&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;vllm-runtime:1.4.1-a.x-k2-post.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; container. Added FP8 H200 targets with 4xTP8 aggregated and 2P2D TP8 disaggregated layouts, KV-aware routing, and EAGLE3 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5346039684&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14318&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14318/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14318&quot;&gt;#14318&lt;/a&gt;), and A.X-K2-NVFP4 B200 recipes on vLLM v0.26.0 with TP4 aggregated and disaggregated deployments (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5416274534&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14635&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14635/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14635&quot;&gt;#14635&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solar Open2 250B NVFP4 Recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Requires the custom &lt;a href=&quot;https://catalog.ngc.nvidia.com/orgs/nvidia/teams/ai-dynamo/containers/vllm-runtime/tags&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;vllm-runtime:1.4.1-solar-open2-250b-post.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; container. Added aggregated and disaggregated B200 recipes with a reasoning parser fix for the checkpoint&#39;s special tokens (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5356228940&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14376&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14376/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14376&quot;&gt;#14376&lt;/a&gt;), then repointed benchmark manifests at the public AIPerf v0.12.0 image (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5479566632&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14956&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14956/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14956&quot;&gt;#14956&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;K-EXAONE 2.0 vLLM Recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Requires the custom &lt;a href=&quot;https://catalog.ngc.nvidia.com/orgs/nvidia/teams/ai-dynamo/containers/vllm-runtime/tags&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;vllm-runtime:1.4.1-k-exaone-2.0-750b-post.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; container. Added vLLM recipes for &lt;code&gt;LGAI-EXAONE/K-EXAONE-2.0-750B-A37B-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt; on B200 with aggregated TP=4 and disaggregated 1P1D variants (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5455388304&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14822&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14822/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14822&quot;&gt;#14822&lt;/a&gt;), then moved recipe notes into the Fern page and corrected the InfiniBand component, image, and resource settings (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5491810914&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15015&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15015/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15015&quot;&gt;#15015&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gemma 4 31B Recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Requires the custom &lt;a href=&quot;https://catalog.ngc.nvidia.com/orgs/nvidia/teams/ai-dynamo/containers/tensorrtllm-runtime/tags&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;tensorrtllm-runtime:1.5.0-gemma-4-31b-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; container. Added Gemma 4 31B deployment recipes for B200, GB200, and H200 GPUs with TensorRT-LLM aggregated configurations, model cache setup, and benchmarking workflows, plus documentation in the recipe catalog and a Google provider filter (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5146407671&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13221&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13221/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13221&quot;&gt;#13221&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inkling-NVFP4 GB300 Agentic Recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Requires the custom &lt;a href=&quot;https://catalog.ngc.nvidia.com/orgs/nvidia/teams/ai-dynamo/containers/vllm-runtime/tags&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;vllm-runtime:1.5.0-inkling-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; container. Added aggregated (2 replicas x TP4) and disaggregated (1P1D, TP4 per role) Dynamo plus vLLM recipes for thinkingmachines/Inkling-NVFP4 on GB300, tuned for an agentic workload with KV-aware routing, MTP-8 speculative decoding, and 1M context, along with an AIPerf trace-replay benchmark Job and Kustomize overlays for generic and AWS RoCE clusters (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5251788981&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13798&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13798/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13798&quot;&gt;#13798&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qwen3.6-35B-A3B SGLang Recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Added SGLang multi-token prediction deployment recipes for Qwen3.6-35B-A3B on B200, GB200, and H200 GPUs, along with model-download configurations, smoke tests, benchmark results, and catalog and documentation entries (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5279526493&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13958&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13958/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13958&quot;&gt;#13958&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qwen3.8-Flash-Next vLLM Recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Requires the custom upstream &lt;a href=&quot;https://hub.docker.com/r/vllm/vllm-openai/tags?name=qwen38-flash-next&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;vllm/vllm-openai:qwen38-flash-next&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; image, which installs &lt;code&gt;ai-dynamo&lt;/code&gt; at pod startup. Added aggregated (4-GPU TP4, 8-GPU 2xTP4, 12-GPU 3xTP4) and disaggregated 1P1D and 2P1D vLLM deployment recipes for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next on B200, including model-cache setup, AIPerf trace-replay benchmarks, and a docs catalog entry (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5297157313&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14033&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14033/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14033&quot;&gt;#14033&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash SGLang Recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Requires the custom &lt;a href=&quot;https://catalog.ngc.nvidia.com/orgs/nvidia/teams/ai-dynamo/containers/sglang-runtime/tags&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;sglang-runtime:1.6.0-deepseek-v4.1-flash-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; container. Added day-0 aggregated and disaggregated recipes on 8x GB200 with KV-aware routing on the aggregated target. Both serve up to 1,048,576 tokens of context and neither is benchmarked (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5419198469&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14682&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14682/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14682&quot;&gt;#14682&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Motif-3 NVFP4 Serving Recipe:&lt;/strong&gt; Requires the custom &lt;a href=&quot;https://catalog.ngc.nvidia.com/orgs/nvidia/teams/ai-dynamo/containers/vllm-runtime/tags&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;vllm-runtime:1.5.0-motif-3-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; container. Added the Motif-3 NVFP4 aggregated serving recipe for vLLM on B200, along with model-cache and benchmark manifests, a Fern documentation page, and a catalog entry that brings the recipe catalog to 25 model families and 125 deployable configurations (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5670233304&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15534&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15534/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15534&quot;&gt;#15534&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deployment Recipe Starter Templates:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a catalog of copyable deployment recipe templates covering aggregated and disaggregated serving for SGLang, TensorRT-LLM, and vLLM, along with Kustomize components for caching, placement, scheduling, probes, networking, and registry credentials, plus contribution and validation guidance for building new recipes (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5237577037&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13724&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13724/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13724&quot;&gt;#13724&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recipe Updates&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provider Networking Kustomize Components:&lt;/strong&gt; Ported the disaggregated provider-networking Kustomize Components for GKE RoCE and InfiniBand to the v1beta1 copy-and-fill scaffold, and extended the recipe validator to enforce the networking-slot ordering and worker-only networking-delta contract, so recipes carry no cluster-specific values in the base (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5317459414&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14142&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14142/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14142&quot;&gt;#14142&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kimi Recipe Configuration Fixes:&lt;/strong&gt; Set &lt;code&gt;DYN_SELF_HOST_METADATA=1&lt;/code&gt; on every Kimi K3 worker role in SGLang and vLLM configurations (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5413861090&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14617&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14617/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14617&quot;&gt;#14617&lt;/a&gt;), and removed &lt;code&gt;--request-plane nats&lt;/code&gt; from the Kimi K2.5 aggregated recipe to use the default TCP transport (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5649969111&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15428&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15428/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15428&quot;&gt;#15428&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo Frontend Image for Recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Switched the GLM-5.3-Flash recipes&#39; Frontend to the &lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/ai-dynamo/dynamo-frontend&lt;/code&gt; image, dropping the inline &lt;code&gt;pip install ai-dynamo&lt;/code&gt; step (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5329741074&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14229&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14229/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14229&quot;&gt;#14229&lt;/a&gt;), and applied it to Qwen3.6 SGLang MTP recipes with &lt;code&gt;--dyn-reasoning-parser qwen3&lt;/code&gt; so reasoning lands in &lt;code&gt;message.reasoning_content&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5387263910&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14472&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14472/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14472&quot;&gt;#14472&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GB300 Max Model Length:&lt;/strong&gt; Corrected the SGLang chat configuration in the Qwen3 recipe README to document a 262,144-token context length for the GB300 aggregated and disaggregated profiles, while GB200 values remained unchanged (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5301671582&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14048&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14048/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14048&quot;&gt;#14048&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shared DGD Environment Merging:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the generated Kustomize OpenAPI schema so environment variables on DynamoGraphDeployment resources merge by name instead of producing duplicate entries, preserving existing values when recipes patch shared environment variables (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5502914285&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15064&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15064/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15064&quot;&gt;#15064&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qwen3-32B-FP8 Decode Mode Flag:&lt;/strong&gt; Added the &lt;code&gt;--disaggregation-mode decode&lt;/code&gt; flag to the decode worker in the Qwen3-32B-FP8 vLLM disaggregated recipe, which previously started as an aggregated worker and left the Frontend reporting no model despite a &lt;code&gt;Ready&lt;/code&gt; deployment (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5930046210&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16821&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16821/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16821&quot;&gt;#16821&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qwen3-VL Worker Startup:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the Qwen3-VL-32B-FP8 vLLM recipes so their worker containers pass command-line arguments correctly; the disaggregated encode and decode workers previously exited cleanly without ever starting, leaving no error explaining the missing workers (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5933703401&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16855&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16855/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16855&quot;&gt;#16855&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Refreshed Kimi-K3 Recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Requires the custom &lt;a href=&quot;https://catalog.ngc.nvidia.com/orgs/nvidia/teams/ai-dynamo/containers/vllm-runtime/tags&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;vllm-runtime:1.5.0-kimi-k3-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href=&quot;https://catalog.ngc.nvidia.com/orgs/nvidia/teams/ai-dynamo/containers/sglang-runtime/tags&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;sglang-runtime:1.5.0-kimi-k3-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; container. Expanded the Kimi-K3 recipes with SGLang and vLLM aggregated and disaggregated targets for H200, GB200, and GB300 and added Mooncake trace benchmarking workflows (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5112255858&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12944&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12944/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12944&quot;&gt;#12944&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bug Fixes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend &amp;amp; Agents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Anthropic Tool-Call Conversion Fidelity:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed Anthropic Messages conversion so buffered tool calls are emitted after an early finish reason (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5523907819&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15129&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15129/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15129&quot;&gt;#15129&lt;/a&gt;) and the single-call limit from &lt;code&gt;tool_choice.disable_parallel_tool_use&lt;/code&gt; is applied (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5408774327&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14605&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14605/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14605&quot;&gt;#14605&lt;/a&gt;). Preserved &lt;code&gt;tool.strict&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5819158991&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16206&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16206/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16206&quot;&gt;#16206&lt;/a&gt;), mapped &lt;code&gt;output_config.format&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;response_format&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5819163216&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16207&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16207/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16207&quot;&gt;#16207&lt;/a&gt;), and suppressed tool calls whose &lt;code&gt;tool_use.input&lt;/code&gt; is not a JSON object (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5819888716&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16214&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16214/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16214&quot;&gt;#16214&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Anthropic Messages Protocol Corrections:&lt;/strong&gt; Reworked Anthropic streaming so text after a tool call opens a new block (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5655968710&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15467&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15467/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15467&quot;&gt;#15467&lt;/a&gt;), reported &lt;code&gt;stop_reason: &quot;stop_sequence&quot;&lt;/code&gt; with the matched string (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5852224381&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16417&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16417/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16417&quot;&gt;#16417&lt;/a&gt;), and stripped the Claude Code billing preamble by default (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5750551364&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15826&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15826/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15826&quot;&gt;#15826&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Structured-Output Reasoning Gating:&lt;/strong&gt; Extended the reasoning gate to structured response formats so JSON no longer returns entirely in &lt;code&gt;reasoning_content&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5384659529&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14465&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14465/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14465&quot;&gt;#14465&lt;/a&gt;), gave forced &lt;code&gt;tool_choice&lt;/code&gt; precedence over &lt;code&gt;response_format&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5322417126&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14179&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14179/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14179&quot;&gt;#14179&lt;/a&gt;), gated &lt;code&gt;tool_choice=&quot;auto&quot;&lt;/code&gt; grammars on reasoning to avoid responses that contain neither an answer nor a tool call (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5557682252&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15227&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15227/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15227&quot;&gt;#15227&lt;/a&gt;), and bypassed the tool parser for ungated answer JSON (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5667056580&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15515&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15515/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15515&quot;&gt;#15515&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Chat Processor Parser Fixes:&lt;/strong&gt; Passed the checkpoint tokenizer to SGLang parsers so reasoning and tool calls are detected when checkpoint delimiters differ from defaults (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5667006988&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15509&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15509/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15509&quot;&gt;#15509&lt;/a&gt;), retained parser-declared tool closing delimiters during stop handling (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5667017824&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15510&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15510/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15510&quot;&gt;#15510&lt;/a&gt;), honored explicit &lt;code&gt;skip_special_tokens=false&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5408408952&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14602&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14602/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14602&quot;&gt;#14602&lt;/a&gt;), and returned chat-template errors as invalid-argument errors (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5667043110&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15511&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15511/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15511&quot;&gt;#15511&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Truncated Tool-Call Finish Reasons:&lt;/strong&gt; Preserved &lt;code&gt;finish_reason: &quot;length&quot;&lt;/code&gt; at &lt;code&gt;max_tokens&lt;/code&gt; rather than a completed tool call (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5250948547&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13791&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13791/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13791&quot;&gt;#13791&lt;/a&gt;), suppressed the incomplete final tool call in Chat Completions and Anthropic Messages (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5250967451&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13792&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13792/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13792&quot;&gt;#13792&lt;/a&gt;), and reported streams ending inside GLM-4.7 tool-call blocks as length-limited (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5543958911&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15184&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15184/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15184&quot;&gt;#15184&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Chat and Completion Logprobs Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Returned prompt logprobs at the root of non-streaming chat completion responses (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5276112267&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13957&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13957/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13957&quot;&gt;#13957&lt;/a&gt;), emitted completion &lt;code&gt;top_logprobs&lt;/code&gt; as token-to-logprob maps (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5667378892&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15521&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15521/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15521&quot;&gt;#15521&lt;/a&gt;), and mapped chat logprobs onto vLLM sampling parameters instead of rejecting them (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5718672440&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15670&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15670/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15670&quot;&gt;#15670&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Request Parameter Validation Hardening:&lt;/strong&gt; Returned HTTP 400 instead of generic 500 for conflicting guided-decoding options (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5250945918&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13790&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13790/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13790&quot;&gt;#13790&lt;/a&gt;), and aligned stop-sequence limits so excess &lt;code&gt;stop&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;stop_token_ids&lt;/code&gt; entries fail with 400 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5383887014&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14462&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14462/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14462&quot;&gt;#14462&lt;/a&gt;). Also rejected an explicit empty &lt;code&gt;tools&lt;/code&gt; array (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5821254647&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16231&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16231/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16231&quot;&gt;#16231&lt;/a&gt;) and &lt;code&gt;logit_bias&lt;/code&gt; keys that are not non-negative 32-bit integers (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5834903667&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16322&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16322/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16322&quot;&gt;#16322&lt;/a&gt;), and validated &lt;code&gt;strict: true&lt;/code&gt; function parameter schemas before inference (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5820206249&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16219&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16219/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16219&quot;&gt;#16219&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Configurable HTTP Listen Backlog:&lt;/strong&gt; Replaced the frontend HTTP listener&#39;s 128-entry queue with a configurable backlog defaulting to 4096, preventing &lt;code&gt;Connection reset by peer&lt;/code&gt; during connection bursts (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5506179151&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15080&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15080/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15080&quot;&gt;#15080&lt;/a&gt;), and restored the TCP call-home listener&#39;s 4096 backlog (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5577656355&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15270&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15270/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15270&quot;&gt;#15270&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal Media Forwarding Fixes:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed SGLang and vLLM chat processors to read media from &lt;code&gt;tool&lt;/code&gt; messages too, avoiding image count mismatches (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5559487473&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15237&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15237/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15237&quot;&gt;#15237&lt;/a&gt;), converted Responses &lt;code&gt;function_call_output&lt;/code&gt; image parts instead of rejecting them (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5610508357&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15306&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15306/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15306&quot;&gt;#15306&lt;/a&gt;), and closed validation for audio, image, and video requests (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5649027203&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15420&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15420/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15420&quot;&gt;#15420&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raw Reasoning Output Preservation:&lt;/strong&gt; Preserved backend &lt;code&gt;reasoning_content&lt;/code&gt; in the &lt;code&gt;/v1/responses&lt;/code&gt; API, with non-streaming responses returning &lt;code&gt;reasoning_text&lt;/code&gt; content instead of &lt;code&gt;summary_text&lt;/code&gt; and streaming responses emitting &lt;code&gt;response.reasoning_text.delta&lt;/code&gt; plus the corresponding added and done events. Reasoning, text, and tool-call ordering is retained across interleaved reasoning spans, and &lt;code&gt;summary&lt;/code&gt; remains as a compatibility fallback (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4875763280&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11604&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11604/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11604&quot;&gt;#11604&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scoped Tool-Call Array Bound:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed guided decoding so the &lt;code&gt;maxItems=1&lt;/code&gt; constraint applied when &lt;code&gt;parallel_tool_calls=False&lt;/code&gt; is limited to &lt;code&gt;tool_choice=&quot;required&quot;&lt;/code&gt; schemas instead of also hitting named function choices. Array-typed function parameters no longer get truncated to a single element, and the caller&#39;s request dictionary is no longer mutated in place (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5149576562&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13242&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13242/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13242&quot;&gt;#13242&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Speculative Prefill Warmup Lifetime:&lt;/strong&gt; Bounded prefill warmup tasks to their preprocessor&#39;s lifetime with a 60-second warmup deadline after the client response finishes and a process-wide limit of four concurrent speculative preprocessing operations, so stalled backends or never-ending response streams no longer retain request resources indefinitely (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5176936859&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13438&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13438/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13438&quot;&gt;#13438&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incremental Tool-Call Streaming:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed vLLM preprocessing to stream tool-call deltas as the parser emits them instead of buffering them until the end of a completion, so consumers receive incremental SSE frames (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5281314990&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13975&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13975/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13975&quot;&gt;#13975&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Token ID Bounds:&lt;/strong&gt; Added client token id validation for &lt;code&gt;nvext.token_data&lt;/code&gt;, completion &lt;code&gt;prompt&lt;/code&gt;, and embedding &lt;code&gt;input&lt;/code&gt;, so an id at or above the vocabulary bound returns HTTP 400 instead of reaching the engine (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5388722052&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14475&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14475/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14475&quot;&gt;#14475&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Worker Routing Hints:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the SGLang chat processor to forward &lt;code&gt;backend_instance_id&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;decode_worker_id&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;prefill_worker_id&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;dp_rank&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;prefill_dp_rank&lt;/code&gt; from &lt;code&gt;nvext&lt;/code&gt; into the request routing fields. Requests pinned to a specific worker or data-parallel rank previously reached the Router unpinned and could be sent to a different worker (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5420585603&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14696&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14696/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14696&quot;&gt;#14696&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kimi Dynamic Tool Declarations:&lt;/strong&gt; Added support for Kimi K3 message extensions so tools declared only in &lt;code&gt;system.tools&lt;/code&gt; are treated like top-level OpenAI tools across request validation, tool-choice handling, guided decoding, parser definitions, stop-token behavior, and response gating, with dynamic declarations preserved at their original message positions to maintain prompt ordering and prefix-cache behavior (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5429664185&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14755&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14755/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14755&quot;&gt;#14755&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Null Optional Completion Parameters:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the frontend to treat explicit &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; values as omitted for recognized passthrough fields such as &lt;code&gt;cache_salt&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;stop_token_ids&lt;/code&gt;, and for &lt;code&gt;stream_options.include_usage&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;stream_options.continuous_usage_stats&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;/v1/chat/completions&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;/v1/completions&lt;/code&gt;. OpenAI-compatible clients that serialize unset optional parameters as &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; no longer receive HTTP 400 validation errors (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5460295290&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14847&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14847/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14847&quot;&gt;#14847&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responses API Metadata Echo:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the Responses API to echo request &lt;code&gt;metadata&lt;/code&gt; in both non-streaming and streaming responses, which was previously replaced with an empty map when Dynamo built the response. Requests without metadata continue to return an empty object (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5510411248&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15102&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15102/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15102&quot;&gt;#15102&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Renderer Message Rewrite Preservation:&lt;/strong&gt; Made the frontend render transformed messages, preserving tool argument normalization and the &lt;code&gt;continue_final_message&lt;/code&gt; marker instead of falling back to the original history. Ordinary requests keep the typed fast path (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5535466324&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15163&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15163/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15163&quot;&gt;#15163&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reordered Message Continuation Guard:&lt;/strong&gt; Rejected &lt;code&gt;continue_final_message&lt;/code&gt; requests with an &lt;code&gt;InvalidArgument&lt;/code&gt; error before tokenization when the prompt formatter moves the final input message ahead of other messages, preventing silently truncated prompts and discarded tool results. Continuation still works for ordered tool results and assistant prefixes (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5562710310&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15247&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15247/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15247&quot;&gt;#15247&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Anthropic Hosted Tool Rejection:&lt;/strong&gt; Changed &lt;code&gt;/v1/messages&lt;/code&gt; to return HTTP 400 with &lt;code&gt;invalid_request_error&lt;/code&gt; instead of HTTP 501 for unsupported hosted tools, so clients stop retrying a deterministic rejection, and aligned the behavior with the &lt;code&gt;/v1/responses&lt;/code&gt; hosted-tool policy while preserving &lt;code&gt;NotImplemented&lt;/code&gt; request metrics (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5657413374&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15468&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15468/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15468&quot;&gt;#15468&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Refusal Text Preservation:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed aggregated non-streaming chat responses dropping refusal text by accumulating refusal fragments per choice and retaining them in the final message, so clients receive the full refusal content. Responses without refusal text remain unchanged (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5667107064&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15516&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15516/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15516&quot;&gt;#15516&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Streaming Cached-Token Usage:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed SGLang and vLLM streaming so sparsely reported cached-token usage reaches the client and explicit zero cache counts are preserved. Streaming usage now follows &lt;code&gt;stream_options.include_usage&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;continuous_usage_stats&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5949418906&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16944&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16944/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16944&quot;&gt;#16944&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scheduling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planner Load Predictor Correctness:&lt;/strong&gt; Clamped Kalman forecasts at zero so they no longer go negative (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5392318283&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14497&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14497/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14497&quot;&gt;#14497&lt;/a&gt;), scored failed simulation presets honestly (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5394353908&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14515&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14515/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14515&quot;&gt;#14515&lt;/a&gt;), weighted frontend histogram averages by observation count (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5422207637&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14705&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14705/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14705&quot;&gt;#14705&lt;/a&gt;), and reported unreadable request counts as unknown rather than zero (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5433866222&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14766&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14766/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14766&quot;&gt;#14766&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Per-Rank DP Capacity Handling:&lt;/strong&gt; Normalized aggregate vLLM KV capacity to per-rank values and rejected zero data-parallel rank counts (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5339013243&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14258&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14258/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14258&quot;&gt;#14258&lt;/a&gt;), and hardened the Router for empty prompts, DP ranges, and large KV events (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5609667992&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15303&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15303/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15303&quot;&gt;#15303&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KV Router Lookup Repair:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed lazy cross-worker reverse-lookup repair in the KV Router compressed radix tree so repair updates only existing entries, preventing scrubbed keys from being recreated and reviving phantom tracked blocks. Store paths retained their insertion behavior for newly stored blocks (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4924867774&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11891&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11891/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11891&quot;&gt;#11891&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Non-Blocking Prometheus Metrics Collection:&lt;/strong&gt; Moved Planner traffic, KV-only, and accept-length collection to a background thread so slow Prometheus queries no longer block the event loop, keeping control API requests responsive. Shared metrics are published on the event loop only after a successful collection, and &lt;code&gt;collect_accept_length()&lt;/code&gt; is now async across provider and environment protocols (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5357153061&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14377&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14377/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14377&quot;&gt;#14377&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Atomic Planner Decision Publishing:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the virtual Planner to publish worker counts and decision ID in a single etcd transaction, so clients no longer observe partial scaling decisions (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5453694455&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14809&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14809/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14809&quot;&gt;#14809&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pending Virtual Connector Decisions:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed &lt;code&gt;VirtualConnectorClient.wait()&lt;/code&gt; in the Planner to return immediately when an unacknowledged scaling decision already exists in etcd, instead of only reporting decisions published after the watch started. Consumers no longer miss a decision published before they began waiting (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5458162587&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14841&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14841/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14841&quot;&gt;#14841&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rust Worker Topology Policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Added topology policy loading in &lt;code&gt;dynamo-backend-common&lt;/code&gt; so Rust workers read topology settings before model registration and publish the same topology fields as Python workers. The loader waits up to 30 seconds for delayed projection (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5469140168&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14909&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14909/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14909&quot;&gt;#14909&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KV Router Lease Leak Fix:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed a reference cycle between the KV Router scheduler and lease manager, so dropped or failed routers no longer leak scheduler and lease state (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5570826258&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15258&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15258/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15258&quot;&gt;#15258&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Non-Finite Router Weight Rejection:&lt;/strong&gt; Made Router configuration reject infinite and NaN values for &lt;code&gt;overlap_score_credit_decay&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;prefill_load_scale&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;router_temperature&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;decode_active_request_weight&lt;/code&gt; at validation time instead of failing on every request after startup. Finite values, including the largest representable value, behave as before (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5669615194&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15529&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15529/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15529&quot;&gt;#15529&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Mooncake Key Prefix:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed shared-cache lookups with &lt;code&gt;--shared-cache-type hicache&lt;/code&gt; so the Router matches SGLang&#39;s Mooncake keys, which are prefixed with the backend tag and model name (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5854465042&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16427&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16427/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16427&quot;&gt;#16427&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prefill Activation Fail-Closed:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed disaggregated serving during rollouts so requests arriving while the prefill binding is activating receive a retryable 503 instead of being forwarded straight to decode without &lt;code&gt;bootstrap_info&lt;/code&gt;, so clients receive the 503 instead of a 500 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5949407669&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16942&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16942/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16942&quot;&gt;#16942&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stale Router Discovery Record Removal:&lt;/strong&gt; Removed the obsolete &lt;code&gt;router-discovery&lt;/code&gt; advertisement, whose stale transport could prevent a KV-routing frontend from initializing after a container restart. Worker discovery and request and response formats are unchanged, and a KV frontend without another RPC endpoint no longer binds &lt;code&gt;DYN_TCP_RPC_PORT&lt;/code&gt;. The last release that consumed the record was Dynamo v1.3.1 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5931774049&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16828&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16828/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16828&quot;&gt;#16828&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal &amp;amp; Diffusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qwen3-ASR Realtime Example Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Reworked the vLLM realtime launch example to use vLLM&#39;s native &lt;code&gt;Qwen3ASRRealtimeGeneration&lt;/code&gt; instead of forcing the Voxtral architecture (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5661674719&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15481&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15481/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15481&quot;&gt;#15481&lt;/a&gt;), and set &lt;code&gt;Qwen/Qwen3-ASR-0.6B&lt;/code&gt; as the default realtime ASR model (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5855520212&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16438&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16438/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16438&quot;&gt;#16438&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal Request Error Propagation:&lt;/strong&gt; Surfaced image generation failures instead of returning HTTP 200 with empty data (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5116974675&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13000&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13000/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13000&quot;&gt;#13000&lt;/a&gt;), mapped timeouts and connection failures on user-supplied image URLs to 408 and 400 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5330959873&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14240&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14240/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14240&quot;&gt;#14240&lt;/a&gt;), preserved malformed &lt;code&gt;data:&lt;/code&gt; URIs as 400 rather than collapsing to 500 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5408512645&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14603&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14603/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14603&quot;&gt;#14603&lt;/a&gt;), and returned 400 for multimodal requests to text-only vLLM prefill workers (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5610449726&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15305&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15305/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15305&quot;&gt;#15305&lt;/a&gt;). The Rust frontend with &lt;code&gt;--frontend-decoding&lt;/code&gt; now returns HTTP 400 naming the modality instead of HTTP 500 for &lt;code&gt;image_url&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;video_url&lt;/code&gt; parts that fail (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5931981374&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16829&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16829/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16829&quot;&gt;#16829&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shared HTTP Client Media Fetching:&lt;/strong&gt; Routed remote media downloads through the shared HTTP client with URL validation and size limits for TensorRT-LLM &lt;code&gt;.safetensors&lt;/code&gt; embedding URLs (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5355051385&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14373&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14373/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14373&quot;&gt;#14373&lt;/a&gt;) and vLLM-Omni &lt;code&gt;ref_audio&lt;/code&gt; voice-cloning downloads (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5355012241&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14372&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14372/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14372&quot;&gt;#14372&lt;/a&gt;), and enforced the &lt;code&gt;DYN_MM_MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB&lt;/code&gt; cap, 64 MiB by default, on remote image, audio, and video downloads (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5488976127&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15005&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15005/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15005&quot;&gt;#15005&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EPD Encode Worker Hardening:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the vLLM E/P/D encode worker answering 503 forever instead of reporting healthy (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5650525599&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15434&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15434/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15434&quot;&gt;#15434&lt;/a&gt;), and enabled per-worker port isolation and readiness checks in the multimodal launch scripts (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5429378851&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14751&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14751/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14751&quot;&gt;#14751&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qwen DeepStack Embedding Size:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed Qwen multimodal placeholder generation in vLLM to use the model&#39;s actual vision embedding dimension instead of a fixed value, resolving tensor splitting errors when running DeepStack-based models such as the Qwen3-VL series (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4820982524&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11244&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11244/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11244&quot;&gt;#11244&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal Processor Kwargs Forwarding:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the TensorRT-LLM backend dropping per-request &lt;code&gt;mm_processor_kwargs&lt;/code&gt;, which were hardcoded to an empty dictionary before reaching &lt;code&gt;generate_async&lt;/code&gt; while the request still returned HTTP 200. The value is now read from the top-level field with an &lt;code&gt;extra_args&lt;/code&gt; fallback, matching the precedence used by the vLLM backend (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5260496516&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13856&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13856/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13856&quot;&gt;#13856&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data URI Video Decoding:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed TensorRT-LLM multimodal handling so inline &lt;code&gt;data:&lt;/code&gt; URI videos are base64-decoded and passed through the same codec probe and NVDEC path as fetched HTTP(S) bytes, instead of failing with an undetected codec error. Malformed or non-base64 URIs and payloads exceeding &lt;code&gt;max_file_size_bytes&lt;/code&gt; now return HTTP 400 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5556587040&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15219&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15219/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15219&quot;&gt;#15219&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Idle Media-Loader CPU Fix:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed media-loader NIXL agent busy-polling by setting a 1 ms progress-thread delay, dropping idle frontend CPU use from 200% to 1.9% per multimodal worker set, and drained per-read notifications that leaked about 110 bytes per image (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5598245182&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15289&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15289/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15289&quot;&gt;#15289&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal Decode KV Identity:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed non-Qwen vLLM decode workers clearing &lt;code&gt;multi_modal_data&lt;/code&gt;, which let same-size images collide in the decode prefix cache so a request could reuse another request&#39;s image KV (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5627564276&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15371&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15371/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15371&quot;&gt;#15371&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TTS Task Type Validation:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed vLLM Omni to reject a &lt;code&gt;task_type&lt;/code&gt; the Qwen3-TTS checkpoint cannot serve with a 400 instead of terminating the stage, so later valid requests no longer fail (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5685525634&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15591&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15591/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15591&quot;&gt;#15591&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unsupported Diffusion Layer Count:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed vLLM-Omni image and video worker startup by omitting the obsolete &lt;code&gt;layerwise_num_gpu_layers&lt;/code&gt; field by default, which the diffusion configuration validator rejected before engine initialization completed. Explicit legacy CLI or environment values are now rejected during Dynamo configuration validation with guidance to use &lt;code&gt;--enable-layerwise-offload&lt;/code&gt; without a layer-count override (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5821491267&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16238&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16238/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16238&quot;&gt;#16238&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes Deployment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unified vLLM Flag Parsing:&lt;/strong&gt; Consolidated the Operator&#39;s vLLM argument readers so every flag spelling resolved identically (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5493627302&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15028&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15028/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15028&quot;&gt;#15028&lt;/a&gt;), and resolved repeated flags to the last occurrence, correcting world size derivation (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5557395319&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15224&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15224/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15224&quot;&gt;#15224&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DGDR GPU SKU Discovery:&lt;/strong&gt; Added canonical SKU identifiers to DGDR GPU discovery, starting with &lt;code&gt;b300_sxm&lt;/code&gt; for &lt;code&gt;NVIDIA B300&lt;/code&gt; variants, so an omitted &lt;code&gt;spec.hardware.gpuSku&lt;/code&gt; no longer persisted an enum-invalid product name (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5552366997&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15216&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15216/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15216&quot;&gt;#15216&lt;/a&gt;). Canonicalized GB200 to &lt;code&gt;gb200&lt;/code&gt;, retaining &lt;code&gt;gb200_sxm&lt;/code&gt; as a deprecated value with an admission warning (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5731000285&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15711&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15711/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15711&quot;&gt;#15711&lt;/a&gt;), and added Vera Rubin NVL72 support as &lt;code&gt;vr_nvl72&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5781341760&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15996&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15996/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15996&quot;&gt;#15996&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Snapshot Memory Saver Fixes:&lt;/strong&gt; Enabled the SGLang memory saver during argument parsing when Dynamo snapshot mode is active and suppressed raw forward-pass metrics during snapshot startup including restored pods carrying &lt;code&gt;DYN_FORWARDPASS_METRIC_PORT&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5404773661&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14555&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14555/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14555&quot;&gt;#14555&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DGD Adoption and Metadata Validation:&lt;/strong&gt; Hardened DGDR adoption to reject an unrelated DGD with the same name and refuse to replace its confirmed deployment (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5262731731&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13885&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13885/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13885&quot;&gt;#13885&lt;/a&gt;), and validated durable metadata on terminating DGD updates, which previously accepted every mutation (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5185655964&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13486&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13486/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13486&quot;&gt;#13486&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Oversized Metadata Header Status:&lt;/strong&gt; Changed the standalone endpoint picker provider (EPP) to return HTTP 431 Request Header Fields Too Large for oversized scheduling metadata headers instead of 400, and kept the too-many-entries and too-large cases distinguishable, matching the integrated frontend behavior (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5410288646&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14612&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14612/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14612&quot;&gt;#14612&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Worker Hash Input Normalization:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the Operator worker hash computation to canonicalize semantically equivalent configurations, including empty Grove wrappers, &lt;code&gt;forceScalingGroup: false&lt;/code&gt;, disabled checkpoint settings, and explicit backend-default compilation-cache mount paths. Representation-only differences no longer change the &lt;code&gt;nvidia.com/dynamo-worker-hash&lt;/code&gt; label, though deployments using the explicit forms may see a one-time hash change after upgrading (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5424094788&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14721&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14721/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14721&quot;&gt;#14721&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Init Container Pull Secrets:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed image pull secret discovery in the Operator to scan init container images in addition to regular containers, so components with a public main image and a private initialization image no longer fail to start without explicitly configured credentials. Explicit pull secrets, deduplication, and discovery-disable behavior were preserved (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5470281727&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14922&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14922/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14922&quot;&gt;#14922&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bounded Dynamo Namespace Labels:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed derived Dynamo namespaces that exceeded the 63-byte Kubernetes label limit by shortening them to a readable prefix plus a hash, preventing Grove from rejecting a generated PodCliqueSet (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5851976218&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16414&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16414/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16414&quot;&gt;#16414&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shadow-Mode KV Sizing Fix:&lt;/strong&gt; Reserved the co-located peer engine&#39;s non-KV memory in the shadow-mode vLLM scratch-KV budget, charging each engine 2 GiB for allocations outside PyTorch&#39;s allocator plus 1.25 GiB for the CUDA context, so the failover winner&#39;s KV cache fits instead of timing out while the peer is still resident (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5893075391&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16710&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16710/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16710&quot;&gt;#16710&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Authored Frontend Command Handling:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the Operator so an authored &lt;code&gt;command&lt;/code&gt; on a frontend container or frontend sidecar owns the entire argv, dropping the default frontend &lt;code&gt;Args&lt;/code&gt; that previously duplicated &lt;code&gt;-m dynamo.frontend&lt;/code&gt; and crash-looped the pod. Legacy Go EPP deployments keep their generated pool, config-file, and gRPC arguments (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5929617304&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16814&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16814/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16814&quot;&gt;#16814&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;v1alpha1 envFromSecret Preservation:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed DGDR overrides that set v1alpha1 &lt;code&gt;envFromSecret&lt;/code&gt; on a service whose v1beta1 main container already had &lt;code&gt;envFrom&lt;/code&gt;, such as &lt;code&gt;hf-token-secret&lt;/code&gt;, which previously dropped the requested Secret during conversion. &lt;code&gt;envFrom&lt;/code&gt; is now additive like &lt;code&gt;env&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;volumeMounts&lt;/code&gt;, so the result matches the equivalent v1beta1 override (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5951621342&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16966&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16966/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16966&quot;&gt;#16966&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GMS V1 Snapshot Loader Restart Loop:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the &lt;code&gt;gms-loader&lt;/code&gt; container exiting after a successful load with &lt;code&gt;DYN_GMS_USE_V1=true&lt;/code&gt;, which made the restarted loader crash-loop and left the pod &lt;code&gt;Ready=False&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5946503280&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16915&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16915/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16915&quot;&gt;#16915&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo Sidecar&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dynamo Sidecar remains experimental in Dynamo v1.6.0.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Sidecar Parser Passthrough:&lt;/strong&gt; Accepted &lt;code&gt;--dyn-tool-call-parser&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;--dyn-reasoning-parser&lt;/code&gt; in the vLLM sidecar so the frontend parses output as in-process workers do (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5670947555&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15539&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15539/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15539&quot;&gt;#15539&lt;/a&gt;), and started vLLM with &lt;code&gt;--reasoning-parser none&lt;/code&gt; so thinking requests no longer returned 400 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5720690016&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15684&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15684/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15684&quot;&gt;#15684&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sidecar Streaming Payload Fidelity:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the vLLM sidecar to forward buffered empty text deltas as empty strings instead of dropping them, so the frontend waits for vLLM to release its stop-string buffer rather than detokenizing the token IDs and duplicating completion text (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5420825751&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14699&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14699/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14699&quot;&gt;#14699&lt;/a&gt;), with corrected hidden stop-token reporting and preserved cancelled prefill responses (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5561143851&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15243&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15243/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15243&quot;&gt;#15243&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Effective Attention Block Size:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the vLLM sidecar to register and publish KV events with the engine-reported effective attention block size, so routing retains KV cache information under decode context parallelism (DCP) (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5418480744&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14673&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14673/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14673&quot;&gt;#14673&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decode Worker KV Indexing:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the shared Rust worker forcing &lt;code&gt;enable_local_indexer&lt;/code&gt; off for decode workers, so sidecars and other callers can create local KV indexes and recovery endpoints for declared event sources with matching model metadata. Explicit &lt;code&gt;enable_local_indexer=false&lt;/code&gt; and the encode-role exclusion remain unchanged (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5482850565&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14981&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14981/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14981&quot;&gt;#14981&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Early Sidecar Health Probes:&lt;/strong&gt; Started sidecar health probes before waiting for the inference engine, so Kubernetes can pass the sidecar startup probe and launch the engine container while readiness stays independent of model loading (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5495855411&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15051&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15051/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15051&quot;&gt;#15051&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Incremental Streaming Validation:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a discovery check that rejects SGLang sidecar startup unless &lt;code&gt;GetServerInfo&lt;/code&gt; reports incremental streaming output as enabled, with an error directing users to relaunch SGLang with &lt;code&gt;--incremental-streaming-output&lt;/code&gt;. This prevents duplicated output and inflated completion-token counts caused by cumulative output IDs being treated as new tokens (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5533391113&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15150&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15150/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15150&quot;&gt;#15150&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Sidecar Refusal Messages:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed SGLang sidecar request validation so refusals return their specific reason in the HTTP 400 response body instead of a generic &quot;Invalid request&quot; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5598174485&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15285&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15285/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15285&quot;&gt;#15285&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Cached Token Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the SGLang sidecar to read &lt;code&gt;cached_tokens&lt;/code&gt; from the engine&#39;s &lt;code&gt;meta_info&lt;/code&gt; and report it as &lt;code&gt;usage.prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens&lt;/code&gt;, clamped to the prompt length, so OpenAI completions and chat responses reflect prefix-cache hits instead of always reporting zero (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5694025098&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15602&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15602/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15602&quot;&gt;#15602&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guided Decoding for Tool Choice:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed TensorRT-LLM sidecar launch scripts, deploy examples, and the README engine command to set &lt;code&gt;guided_decoding_backend: xgrammar&lt;/code&gt;, so chat completions requests with a required or named &lt;code&gt;tool_choice&lt;/code&gt; return a parsed tool call instead of a 500 error (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5716583259&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15649&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15649/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15649&quot;&gt;#15649&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Explicit Sidecar Launcher Resolution:&lt;/strong&gt; Applied a shared &lt;code&gt;resolve_sidecar&lt;/code&gt; helper across all 15 SGLang, TensorRT-LLM, and vLLM sidecar launch scripts, so each prefers a native sidecar command and falls back to &lt;code&gt;python3 -m dynamo.&amp;lt;backend&amp;gt;.sidecar&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5785819553&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16059&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16059/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16059&quot;&gt;#16059&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cancelled Sidecar Request Aborts:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the vLLM native gRPC sidecar to abort cancelled requests, so queued requests are released instead of occupying an engine slot until output is produced (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5818173941&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16201&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16201/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16201&quot;&gt;#16201&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM Sidecar Request Semantics:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the TensorRT-LLM sidecar to forward conversation identity across prefill and decode, disable engine detokenization when Dynamo handles it, advertise the configured default thinking mode, and accept logical rank zero while still rejecting unsupported nonzero rank targeting, so conversation-scoped KV cache reuse works and valid rank-zero requests reach the engine (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5834496360&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16315&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16315/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16315&quot;&gt;#16315&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid DP Rank Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the vLLM sidecar so a frontend owning only part of a data parallel group, such as ranks 4 to 7 of an eight-rank group, is no longer rejected at discovery. Each worker now registers its local rank range (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5420740794&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14697&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14697/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14697&quot;&gt;#14697&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Cancellation Lifecycle Hardening:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a bounded cancellation lifecycle for SGLang decode and aggregated workers that aborts requests cancelled before the first output token (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5445338278&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14781&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14781/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14781&quot;&gt;#14781&lt;/a&gt;), extended it to disaggregated prefill workers and their paired decode-side state (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5445338845&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14782&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14782/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14782&quot;&gt;#14782&lt;/a&gt;), and returned SGLang validation aborts as request errors before placeholder tokens or a successful finish could be emitted (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5502932645&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15065&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15065/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15065&quot;&gt;#15065&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DCP Attention Backend Validation:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a startup check that rejects &lt;code&gt;--dcp-size&lt;/code&gt; on attention backends that do not read the DCP parallel state, where the SGLang worker would kill its scheduler (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5451957204&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14800&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14800/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14800&quot;&gt;#14800&lt;/a&gt;), and extended it to MLA decode context parallel, suggesting &lt;code&gt;--attention-backend flashinfer&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;trtllm_mla&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;cutedsl_mla&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5822029378&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16255&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16255/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16255&quot;&gt;#16255&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Guided Decoding Fix:&lt;/strong&gt; Removed &lt;code&gt;--skip-tokenizer-init&lt;/code&gt; from SGLang manifests and docs, because the flag caused &lt;code&gt;response_format: json_schema&lt;/code&gt; requests to return content that did not satisfy the schema (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5206977400&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13605&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13605/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13605&quot;&gt;#13605&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disaggregated Parallel Sampling Rejection:&lt;/strong&gt; Added validation that rejects SGLang disaggregated requests with &lt;code&gt;n &amp;gt; 1&lt;/code&gt; using an HTTP 400 error instead of letting them hang indefinitely. Aggregated parallel sampling and disaggregated &lt;code&gt;n=1&lt;/code&gt; requests continue to work (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5314158805&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14112&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14112/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14112&quot;&gt;#14112&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang API Compatibility Shims:&lt;/strong&gt; Added compatibility shims for &lt;code&gt;get_model_config&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;use_mla_backend&lt;/code&gt;, which SGLang moved from &lt;code&gt;ServerArgs&lt;/code&gt; to its &lt;code&gt;overrides&lt;/code&gt; module, fixing an &lt;code&gt;AttributeError&lt;/code&gt; that prevented the SGLang worker from starting against newer SGLang versions (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5330372663&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14234&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14234/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14234&quot;&gt;#14234&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prefill DP Rank Forwarding:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed SGLang disaggregated serving so the Router forwards the prefill data-parallel rank to decode, dropping decode &lt;code&gt;bootstrap_duration&lt;/code&gt; from 150 ms to 650 ms down to 0.3 ms to 0.6 ms on GLM-5.2 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5562361352&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15246&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15246/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15246&quot;&gt;#15246&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prefill First-Token Logprobs:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed disaggregated prefill in SGLang to forward the generated-token logprobs option through the shared helper, so the first generated token now carries its log-probability data. Prompt-wide logprobs remain excluded because prefill discards that metadata and the Router does not merge it into the decode response (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5667053080&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15512&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15512/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15512&quot;&gt;#15512&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Text-Only Engine Media Rejection:&lt;/strong&gt; Added SGLang worker validation that returns a 400 error for image, video, or audio content on a text-only model, instead of silently dropping the media (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5667359036&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15520&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15520/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15520&quot;&gt;#15520&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attention-DP Rank Counting Fix:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed SGLang DP rank counting to match &lt;code&gt;dp_size * attn_dp_size&lt;/code&gt;, so attention-DP workers register every rank instead of only rank 0 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5875230414&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16598&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16598/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16598&quot;&gt;#16598&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Crash Exit Delay:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed a 60-second delay in worker exit and pod restart after an SGLang child process died by defaulting &lt;code&gt;SGLANG_CUDA_COREDUMP_BEFORE_CRASH_WAIT_SECS&lt;/code&gt; to 0 unless the user sets it, sets &lt;code&gt;CUDA_ENABLE_USER_TRIGGERED_COREDUMP=1&lt;/code&gt;, or passes &lt;code&gt;--crash-dump-folder&lt;/code&gt;. On one A100, worker exit after a killed detokenizer dropped from 66 seconds to 6 seconds (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5950102851&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16952&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16952/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16952&quot;&gt;#16952&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Request-Local Pre-Submit Validation Errors:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed TensorRT-LLM handling of pre-submit &lt;code&gt;ValueError&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;TypeError&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;NotImplementedError&lt;/code&gt; failures so they return a request-scoped error instead of shutting down a healthy engine, while worker shutdown is preserved for unhealthy engines and errors raised during result iteration (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5285018361&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14006&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14006/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14006&quot;&gt;#14006&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decode Cached Token Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed &lt;code&gt;usage.prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens&lt;/code&gt; on the TensorRT-LLM generation-only path, which reported the transferred prompt as a cache hit, so benchmarks, dashboards, and routing decisions that read the usage block get accurate cache-hit data when &lt;code&gt;return_perf_metrics&lt;/code&gt; is enabled (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5637114879&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15389&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15389/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15389&quot;&gt;#15389&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salted TensorRT-LLM Health Checks:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed TensorRT-LLM workers aborting when attention data parallelism and the V2 KV cache manager were enabled by giving the health-check probe request its own cache salt, so it no longer shares a reuse namespace with the engine&#39;s dummy requests. A caller-supplied salt still takes precedence (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5890368536&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16688&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16688/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16688&quot;&gt;#16688&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MPI Child Failure Exit:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed TensorRT-LLM workers hanging until Kubernetes killed the container after an MPI engine child died. The worker now exits promptly with code 1 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5948325006&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16931&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16931/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16931&quot;&gt;#16931&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Snapshot Restore MPI Transport:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed restored TensorRT-LLM engines with TP greater than 1 failing their first collective with &lt;code&gt;ucx send failed: Endpoint timeout&lt;/code&gt;. Snapshot mode now defaults &lt;code&gt;OMPI_MCA_pml=ob1&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;OMPI_MCA_btl=tcp,self&lt;/code&gt;, because Open MPI&#39;s UCX transport enables TCP keepalive probes that abort inter-rank connections during the checkpoint dump. Explicit settings still take precedence (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5949254716&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16941&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16941/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16941&quot;&gt;#16941&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ModelExpress RL Version Declaration:&lt;/strong&gt; Reworked vLLM weight version reporting to report &lt;code&gt;version: null&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;version_declared: false&lt;/code&gt; until declared, adding a &lt;code&gt;set_weight_version&lt;/code&gt; route (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5123662896&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13041&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13041/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13041&quot;&gt;#13041&lt;/a&gt;). Workers loading through the ModelExpress RL loader now declare &lt;code&gt;MX_REFIT_DESIRED_VERSION_UID&lt;/code&gt; at startup (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5563394048&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15252&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15252/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15252&quot;&gt;#15252&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prefill Worker Lifecycle Hardening:&lt;/strong&gt; Shut down EngineCore when a prefill worker exits and made FPM self-benchmark inputs reproducible with retained input, timing, execution, preparation, and worker provenance (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5927299736&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16789&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16789/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16789&quot;&gt;#16789&lt;/a&gt;), with prefill health probes no longer requesting a KV connector handoff, which previously left unclaimed KV transfer state on idle prefill workers and blocked KV cache resets (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5930875235&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16825&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16825/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16825&quot;&gt;#16825&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Elastic EP Grow Rollback:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed vLLM &lt;code&gt;scale_elastic_ep&lt;/code&gt; so a failed grow rolls back to the previous data-parallel size and keeps serving instead of wedging the engine (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5115933142&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12991&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12991/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12991&quot;&gt;#12991&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engine-Expanded Prompt ID Metadata:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed vLLM &lt;code&gt;nvext.engine_data&lt;/code&gt; to report the engine-processed prompt tokens, so training consumers can align them with completion tokens and log probabilities (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5658145080&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15470&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15470/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15470&quot;&gt;#15470&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Model Loading &amp;amp; LoRA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LoRA Card Registration Fix:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed LoRA adapter registration in the SGLang and vLLM handlers by passing &lt;code&gt;ignore_weights=True&lt;/code&gt;, so card registration no longer downloads base-model weights on a cache miss and fails before publishing the adapter (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4791293800&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11164&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11164/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11164&quot;&gt;#11164&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Modeling &amp;amp; Replay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Forward-Pass Metrics KV Warm-Up:&lt;/strong&gt; Settled KV warm-up so decode sweeps no longer abort when attention-DP ranks report READY in different steps, with hybrid KDA/Mamba fixes (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5426644700&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14728&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14728/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14728&quot;&gt;#14728&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5411636760&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14614&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14614/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14614&quot;&gt;#14614&lt;/a&gt;). Snapshot-restored vLLM replicas now stay visible to the Planner (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5044637630&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12545&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12545/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12545&quot;&gt;#12545&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fault Tolerance &amp;amp; Observability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Request Trace Record Accuracy:&lt;/strong&gt; Reworked audit records to derive &lt;code&gt;payload_complete&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;payload_drop_reason&lt;/code&gt; from the actual response (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5317631227&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14143&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14143/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14143&quot;&gt;#14143&lt;/a&gt;), and wrote &lt;code&gt;request_end&lt;/code&gt; for requests cancelled before the first response item (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5451816502&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14799&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14799/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14799&quot;&gt;#14799&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Histogram Bucket Configuration Fixes:&lt;/strong&gt; Raised the default inter-token latency bucket ceiling from 2.0s to 80.0s (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5457319553&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14839&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14839/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14839&quot;&gt;#14839&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Etcd and NATS Connection Resilience:&lt;/strong&gt; Added etcd watch retry with backoff, enabled HTTP/2 keepalive by default with a 15s ping interval and 10s acknowledgment timeout, and raised the default lease TTL from 10s to 30s (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5574613885&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15266&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15266/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15266&quot;&gt;#15266&lt;/a&gt;). Startup now retries temporary NATS connection failures for up to 120 seconds (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5577548923&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15269&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15269/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15269&quot;&gt;#15269&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;System Status Listener Rebinding:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the system status server to rebind its TCP listener after accept failures instead of retrying a stale descriptor indefinitely, keeping status endpoints reachable after process restore while retaining the originally bound address, including an assigned ephemeral port (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4955016186&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12059&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12059/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12059&quot;&gt;#12059&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prefill Worker KV Gauges:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed missing &lt;code&gt;dynamo_component_total_blocks&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;dynamo_component_gpu_cache_usage_percent&lt;/code&gt; samples on disaggregated vLLM prefill workers, which now publish configured total capacity at startup (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5047826297&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12559&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12559/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12559&quot;&gt;#12559&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pending Handshake Cancellation:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed requests hanging when a worker left discovery before sending the response prologue, so worker removal unblocks the requester with a migratable &lt;code&gt;Disconnected&lt;/code&gt; error (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5129979543&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13095&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13095/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13095&quot;&gt;#13095&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Worker Error Preservation:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed finish-reason handling in the backend so a worker&#39;s error finish reason is no longer overwritten by local stop detection, token limits, or user-defined stop strings, preventing failed requests from returning HTTP 200 with &lt;code&gt;finish_reason: &quot;stop&quot;&lt;/code&gt; and malformed output (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5507429521&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15094&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15094/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15094&quot;&gt;#15094&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migration Handshake Cancellation Accounting:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the Frontend to record client cancellation during a migration handshake as &lt;code&gt;outcome=&quot;cancelled&quot;&lt;/code&gt; instead of &lt;code&gt;outcome=&quot;success&quot;&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;dynamo_frontend_model_migration_duration_seconds&lt;/code&gt;, so migration metrics match the HTTP outcome for the same request (#16440).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Invalid Request Refusal Handling:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed worker routability after a worker refused an invalid request before opening the response stream, returning the worker&#39;s own error instead of wrapping it in &lt;code&gt;CannotConnect&lt;/code&gt;. Clients now receive HTTP 400 and the worker stays routable rather than being marked down and causing HTTP 503 on the next valid request (#16597).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Runtime &amp;amp; Transport&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IPv6-Only Networking Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Reworked local address resolution to prefer non-loopback IPv4, then IPv6, then loopback (#13126), with the ZMQ event plane reusing it (#15324). Narrowed &lt;code&gt;ZMQ_IPV6&lt;/code&gt; to bracketed IPv6 endpoints, fixed remaining IPv6-only gaps in listeners, SGLang KV events, and vLLM multinode (#15383), and changed automatic host selection to prefer the routed source address (#15628).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUIC Response Plane Reliability:&lt;/strong&gt; Carried typed pre-stream errors through the QUIC response plane, mapping &lt;code&gt;InvalidArgument&lt;/code&gt; to HTTP 400 (#14789), and updated Quinn to v0.11.12 to fix &lt;code&gt;too many gaps in stream buffer&lt;/code&gt; failures (#14876).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Endpoint Identity-Scoped TCP Routing:&lt;/strong&gt; Scoped TCP endpoint routing and cleanup by full endpoint identity, so endpoints registered under the same name in one process no longer overwrite or tear down each other&#39;s handlers (#14723, #14271).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Oversized TCP Frame Rejection:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a preflight size check in the TCP client that rejects requests exceeding &lt;code&gt;DYN_TCP_MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE&lt;/code&gt; before connection lookup and admission, returning &lt;code&gt;InvalidArgument&lt;/code&gt; which the HTTP layer maps to a 400 response instead of letting the oversized frame reach the worker and close the connection during decode (#14110).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ZMQ Socket Exhaustion Guidance:&lt;/strong&gt; Added error messages when event-plane socket creation fails with &lt;code&gt;EMFILE&lt;/code&gt;, so operators hitting file-descriptor limits see advice to reduce direct-ZMQ peers or raise &lt;code&gt;ulimit -n&lt;/code&gt; (#14145).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shared Fetch Model Runtime:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed &lt;code&gt;fetch_model()&lt;/code&gt; creating a second Tokio runtime when called before a Dynamo runtime existed, and the Python Worker mutating the process environment when applying transport overrides (#14534).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ZMQ Publisher Port Race:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed a race during concurrent ZMQ publisher startup by binding the publisher socket directly to an ephemeral port instead of probing with a temporary TCP listener, and read the assigned address back from the socket for logging and discovery, so concurrent publishers no longer collide on the same port (#14566).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discovery Watch Establishment Ordering:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed discovery list-and-watch to return only after the backend watch is established, preventing missed &lt;code&gt;Removed&lt;/code&gt; events (#14769). Every watch now opens with one Added event per matching instance and one Resync snapshot, so a reopened watch replaces state without a separate list call (#15143).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Container Images&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Root Cache Mount Target:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed &lt;code&gt;container/run.sh&lt;/code&gt; so that user overrides with a group suffix, such as &lt;code&gt;--user root:root&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;0:1000&lt;/code&gt;, mount the Hugging Face cache at &lt;code&gt;/root/.cache/huggingface&lt;/code&gt; instead of the Dynamo user cache directory. Non-root users with group 0 continue to use the Dynamo user cache (#14820).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;New Content&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EPP Mode Boundary Documentation:&lt;/strong&gt; Clarified which EPP mode operator-generated resources apply to and the RBAC boundary with standalone mode (#14756, #14620). Documented the &lt;code&gt;FailClose&lt;/code&gt; endpoint-picker failure mode, required a &lt;code&gt;VLLM_IMAGE&lt;/code&gt; variable in the on-ramp example, and corrected docs left over from the Go EPP deprecation (#14811, #14481, #14263).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operator Deployment Caveat Docs:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a warning that &lt;code&gt;compilationCache&lt;/code&gt; PVC contents must be cleared after a backend, torch, or CUDA upgrade (#14381), and documented that creating a DGDR carries the same authority as creating a Job or Pod in that namespace, while Pod-level security stays enforced by Pod Security Admission (#14429).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Snapshot API Documentation:&lt;/strong&gt; Replaced the &lt;code&gt;DynamoCheckpoint Auto mode&lt;/code&gt; wording with the &lt;code&gt;SnapshotJob&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;PodSnapshot&lt;/code&gt; workflow (#16037), with a Kubernetes capture and restore quickstart including TensorRT-LLM examples for Qwen3-0.6B on one GPU and pinned GLM 5.3 NVFP4 on eight B200s (#16044).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KV Cache Transfer Docs Corrections:&lt;/strong&gt; Corrected the TensorRT-LLM docs to state &lt;code&gt;TRTLLM_USE_UCX_KVCACHE&lt;/code&gt; enables direct UCX even with &lt;code&gt;cache_transceiver_config.backend: DEFAULT&lt;/code&gt;, and added a warning that mounting host &lt;code&gt;/opt/amazon/efa&lt;/code&gt; breaks the NIXL LIBFABRIC backend (#13048).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure Deployment Guidelines Documentation:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a Secure Deployment Guidelines page documenting Dynamo&#39;s trust model, securing the external inference API, authenticating the discovery, event, and request planes, and running with least privilege (#13505).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nightly Install Selector Accuracy:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the nightly install selector rows to show the shipped backend versions, or &quot;not currently available&quot; instead of the stable tag (#13599).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planner Mode Selection Guide:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a Choose a Planner Mode guide, split the overview by whether users have TTFT/ITL SLA targets, and documented KV cache reuse and speculative decoding (#14335).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EPD Disaggregation Blog Post:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a blog post on when to use encode-prefill-decode (EPD) disaggregation for multimodal serving, and listed the Pinterest Engineering article on building a VLM serving stack with Dynamo in the external publications page (#14630).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LongCat TokenSpeed Disaggregation Example:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an experimental LongCat-Flash TokenSpeed disaggregated example with KV-aware routing, and its GB300 configuration raises sequence and KV-cache capacity (&lt;code&gt;--max-num-seqs&lt;/code&gt; 4 to 32, &lt;code&gt;--max-total-tokens&lt;/code&gt; 262144 to 917504) and selects &lt;code&gt;trtllm_mla&lt;/code&gt; to address long-context decode slowdown (#15013).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nemotron-3-Ultra Performance Table:&lt;/strong&gt; Restored the Expected Performance table, covering all 12 aggregated and disaggregated profiles across B200, GB200, and H200 at 256K and 1M context lengths (#15194).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Speculative Decoding Guide:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a documentation page for EAGLE3 speculative decoding with SGLang, covering aggregated quick start, disaggregated serving with the KV router, and &lt;code&gt;sglang:spec_*&lt;/code&gt; metrics, and marked SGLang speculative decoding as supported in the speculative decoding overview, the SGLang feature matrix, and the compatibility tables (#15268).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Many-Model GPU Sharing Examples:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a Many-Model Serving section and &lt;code&gt;examples/gpu-sharing/&lt;/code&gt; directory benchmarking Qwen3-4B on one 8x A100 40GB node. At equal load per GPU, GPU fractions retained 60-88% of dedicated-GPU throughput versus 45-73% for HAMi, about 23% cheaper per output token at light per-model load (#15918).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sidecar Documentation Simplification:&lt;/strong&gt; Simplified the sidecar READMEs and Fern pages to one example per engine, added topology diagrams for SGLang, TensorRT-LLM, and vLLM, and corrected stale claims: the &lt;code&gt;dynamo-sidecar&lt;/code&gt; image is published to NGC starting with v1.6.0 (#16062).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tied-Embedding Policy Update Limitation:&lt;/strong&gt; Documented that the first policy update fails for Qwen2.5 and other tied-embedding models on vLLM v0.29.0 and later, with links to the upstream verl fixes, which no reviewed recipe snapshot selects yet (#16682).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Version Upgrades&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Major Dependencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang:&lt;/strong&gt; Upgraded from v0.5.18 to &lt;strong&gt;v0.5.21&lt;/strong&gt; (#15538).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM:&lt;/strong&gt; Upgraded from v1.3.0rc25 to &lt;strong&gt;v1.3.0rc29&lt;/strong&gt; (#15418).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM:&lt;/strong&gt; Upgraded from v0.28.0 to &lt;strong&gt;v0.31.0&lt;/strong&gt; (#15643).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM-Omni:&lt;/strong&gt; Upgraded from v0.28.0rc1 to &lt;strong&gt;v0.31.0rc1&lt;/strong&gt; on CUDA images, and from v0.28.0rc1 (CPU) and v0.27.0rc1 (XPU) to &lt;strong&gt;v0.30.0rc1&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Other Dependencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NIXL:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated SGLang from v1.4.0 to &lt;strong&gt;v1.5.0&lt;/strong&gt;, vLLM from v1.3.2 to &lt;strong&gt;v1.4.1&lt;/strong&gt;, and the Frontend from v1.3.2 to &lt;strong&gt;v1.5.0&lt;/strong&gt;. TensorRT-LLM stays on v1.3.1.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM (CPU and XPU):&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from v0.28.0 (CPU) and v0.27.1 (XPU) to &lt;strong&gt;v0.30.0&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang (XPU):&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from v0.5.11 to &lt;strong&gt;v0.5.19&lt;/strong&gt;, built against oneAPI 2026.0.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;libfabric:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from v2.4.0 to &lt;strong&gt;v2.6.0&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;etcd:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from v3.5.33 to &lt;strong&gt;v3.5.34&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NATS:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from v2.12.14 to &lt;strong&gt;v2.14.8&lt;/strong&gt; (#16845).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LMCache:&lt;/strong&gt; Raised the floor to &lt;strong&gt;v0.5.6&lt;/strong&gt; in the vLLM CUDA runtime image (#16845).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AIPerf:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from v0.12.0 to &lt;strong&gt;v0.13.0&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AISimulate:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from v0.12.0 to &lt;strong&gt;v0.13.0&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grove:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from v0.1.0-alpha.13 to &lt;strong&gt;v0.1.0-alpha.14&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ModelExpress:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from v0.6.0 to &lt;strong&gt;v0.7.0&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;dynamo-renderer:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from v5.1.2 to &lt;strong&gt;v8.0.3&lt;/strong&gt; (#16686).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;dynamo-tokenizers:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from v1.8.1 to &lt;strong&gt;v3.1.1&lt;/strong&gt; (#16686).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planner Image Python:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from CPython 3.12 to &lt;strong&gt;3.13&lt;/strong&gt; for the &lt;code&gt;dynamo-planner&lt;/code&gt; container (#14924).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Triton Runtime Image:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from &lt;code&gt;26.07-py3&lt;/code&gt; (CUDA 13.2) to &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;26.09-py3&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (CUDA 13.4).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Known Issues&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend (SGLang)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Out-of-Vocab Stop Token Crash&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A request whose &lt;code&gt;stop_token_ids&lt;/code&gt; includes an ID at or above the model&#39;s vocabulary size can crash the SGLang scheduler when any request in the batch sets &lt;code&gt;min_tokens&lt;/code&gt;, failing every request on that worker until it restarts. The issue also affects v1.5.0. No workaround is available yet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Snapshot and GMS CUDA Graph Startup Failure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SGLang workers in Dynamo Snapshot mode or with GPU Memory Service V1 checkpointing fail at startup with a &lt;code&gt;NotImplementedError&lt;/code&gt; from prefill CUDA graph initialization. The issue also affects v1.5.0. &lt;strong&gt;Workaround:&lt;/strong&gt; pass &lt;code&gt;--disable-cuda-graph&lt;/code&gt; to these workers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Redundant Memory Resume Crash&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With GPU Memory Service on SGLang, sending &lt;code&gt;resume_memory_occupation&lt;/code&gt; twice without a &lt;code&gt;release_memory_occupation&lt;/code&gt; in between crashes the scheduler. &lt;strong&gt;Workaround:&lt;/strong&gt; send each resume only after a matching release.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend (TensorRT-LLM)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Oversized Anthropic Messages Return 500&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On TensorRT-LLM, non-streaming &lt;code&gt;/v1/messages&lt;/code&gt; requests whose prompt exceeds the engine&#39;s &lt;code&gt;max_num_tokens&lt;/code&gt; return HTTP 500 instead of HTTP 400. No workaround is available yet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend (vLLM)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Omitted Max Tokens Generates to the Context Limit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On vLLM, a request without &lt;code&gt;max_tokens&lt;/code&gt; can generate up to the full remaining context window when the model sets no default output length. &lt;strong&gt;Workaround:&lt;/strong&gt; set &lt;code&gt;max_tokens&lt;/code&gt; on every request.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GMS Persisted KV Standby Wake Failure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With GPU Memory Service persisted KV failover (&lt;code&gt;DYN_GMS_PERSIST_KV&lt;/code&gt;), tensor parallelism, and an explicit &lt;code&gt;--kv-cache-memory-bytes&lt;/code&gt;, the vLLM standby engine fails to adopt the retained KV cache with &lt;code&gt;StaleMemoryLayoutError&lt;/code&gt;. The issue also affects v1.5.0. &lt;strong&gt;Workaround:&lt;/strong&gt; leave &lt;code&gt;DYN_GMS_PERSIST_KV&lt;/code&gt; unset.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLI &amp;amp; Tooling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Replay Module Entrypoint Removal&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;python -m dynamo.replay&lt;/code&gt; fails because the replay CLI moved into the AISimulate wheel in v1.5.0. &lt;strong&gt;Workaround:&lt;/strong&gt; use &lt;code&gt;aisimulate predict --stack dynamo --config &amp;lt;file&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. See &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/main/docs/fern/pages/cli/operations/simulation-with-dynosim/dynosim-replay.mdx&quot;&gt;the replay guide&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logit Bias Ignored&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Frontend accepts &lt;code&gt;logit_bias&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;/v1/chat/completions&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;/v1/completions&lt;/code&gt; but drops it before the engine, so no bias is applied. No workaround is available yet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Request Error Details Dropped&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When a worker rejects a request, the Frontend returns a generic error without the worker&#39;s message. The issue also affects v1.5.0. No workaround is available yet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planner&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inflated Capacity Estimate Suppresses Scaling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For aggregated vLLM deployments, a Dynamo Planner regression model seeded from worker self-benchmark data can overestimate per-engine capacity and refuse to scale up under load. &lt;strong&gt;Workaround:&lt;/strong&gt; use a pre-published AISimulate performance model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Runtime &amp;amp; Router&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GlobalRouter Pool Requests Find No Endpoints&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On Kubernetes with Grove, requests that the GlobalRouter sends to a pool can fail with no available endpoints even when the pool&#39;s worker is healthy. The issue also affects v1.5.0. No workaround is available yet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decode-Only Worker Pin Fails in Disaggregated Serving&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A request that pins only a decode worker fails instead of letting the Router select a prefill worker. The issue also affects v1.5.0. &lt;strong&gt;Workaround:&lt;/strong&gt; pin both workers with &lt;code&gt;x-dynamo-worker-instance-id&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;x-dynamo-prefill-instance-id&lt;/code&gt;, or pin neither.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes &amp;amp; Operator&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brief 404 Errors During Rolling Updates&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rolling updates of disaggregated deployments with a max surge of 1 and max unavailable of 0 can return HTTP 404 for up to about one second while a worker is replaced. The rollout still completes. The issue also affects v1.5.0. No workaround is available yet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EFA Network Plugin Not Loaded&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On AWS EFA clusters, SGLang and TensorRT-LLM workers configured from the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/main/docs/fern/pages/kubernetes/installation/rdma-setup/efa-on-aws.mdx&quot;&gt;EFA on AWS guide&lt;/a&gt; silently fall back to socket transport because the guide&#39;s &lt;code&gt;LD_LIBRARY_PATH&lt;/code&gt; entry is wrong. The issue also affects v1.5.0. &lt;strong&gt;Workaround:&lt;/strong&gt; use &lt;code&gt;/opt/amazon/ofi-nccl/lib&lt;/code&gt; instead of &lt;code&gt;/opt/aws-ofi-nccl/lib&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reinforcement Learning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Slime Weight Synchronization Failure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With the experimental Slime integration, the first weight update from the Slime trainer to SGLang v0.5.21 engines fails with HTTP 400, and restarting the trainer against engines still running from an earlier job also fails. A fix is planned for a future release. No workaround is available yet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Carried Forward&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The other v1.5.0 and v1.5.1 known issues are fixed in v1.6.0 or were closed as intended behavior.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Looking Ahead&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Runtime Router Policy Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A &lt;code&gt;/router_policy&lt;/code&gt; API on the Frontend reads and updates live worker-selection parameters and busy thresholds without a restart.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planner Reconfiguration &amp;amp; Batch Scheduling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Runtime reconfiguration extends beyond GPU budgets to a running Planner&#39;s SLA targets and load predictor. An opt-in batch scheduling policy reserves capacity for online traffic, with the Batch API served through the Frontend.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generation Artifacts for RL&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;vLLM workers can deliver bounded generation artifacts inline or to object stores for reinforcement learning pipelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes Deployment Search&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An experimental &lt;code&gt;v1beta2&lt;/code&gt; API runs simulation-backed deployment searches, and DisaggregatedSet joins Grove as an opt-in workload provider.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;</content>
    <author>
      <name>dagil-nvidia</name>
    </author>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/221734541?s=60&amp;v=4"/>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/942206898/v1.6.0-muse-spark-open-dev.1</id>
    <updated>2026-10-20T02:09:56Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/releases/tag/v1.6.0-muse-spark-open-dev.1"/>
    <title>Dynamo v1.6.0-muse-spark-open-dev.1</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Notes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo v1.6.0-muse-spark-open-dev.1&lt;/strong&gt; is an experimental snapshot build with early &lt;strong&gt;Meta Muse Spark Open&lt;/strong&gt; support on the Dynamo &lt;strong&gt;SGLang&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM&lt;/strong&gt; backends. It is &lt;strong&gt;not recommended for production&lt;/strong&gt; and is not a QA-gated release. APIs, behavior, and defaults may change before stable support. Use it for evaluation, testing, and early feedback only.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dynamo v1.6.0-muse-spark-open-dev.1 adds serving for &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;meta-models/Muse-Spark-Open-816B-A42B-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; on Dynamo &lt;strong&gt;SGLang&lt;/strong&gt; (recommended), &lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM&lt;/strong&gt;. The frontend gains the &lt;code&gt;muse_spark&lt;/code&gt; reasoning and tool-call parsers, plus Responses API support for native, deferred, and custom tools, commentary streaming, conversation replay, and client tool search. The vLLM and SGLang containers are built on digest-pinned public Muse Spark Open model images (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16700&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16700/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16700&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kubernetes recipes cover ten GB200 and GB300 targets: six SGLang (aggregated, 1P1D disaggregated, and KV-aware routed), two vLLM aggregated, and two TensorRT-LLM aggregated. All use TP4/EP4 with an FP8 KV cache and a 1M-token context, with shared model-cache manifests and an AIPerf agentic trace benchmark under &lt;code&gt;recipes/muse-spark-open-816b-a42b&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16553&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16553/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16553&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16557&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16557/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16557&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16567&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16567/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16567&lt;/a&gt;, brought onto this branch by &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16856&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16856/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16856&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base Branch&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;main&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Base Commit&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;165d854ba6b18df8f0bebfebe20e7e29b062b1b2&lt;/code&gt; (2026-09-03)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Release Branch&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;release/1.6.0-muse-spark-open-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Release Tip&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;6b9d12ebcd371ced77af980b0ae72e7f0f054c2d&lt;/code&gt; (2026-10-20)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;SGLang&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;lmsysorg/sglang:dev-muse-spark-open&lt;/code&gt; (digest-pinned, CUDA 13.0)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;vllm/vllm-openai:muse-spark-open&lt;/code&gt; (digest-pinned, CUDA 13.0)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;1.3.0rc25&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/tensorrt-llm/release&lt;/code&gt;, CUDA 13.1), NIXL v1.3.1&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Container Images&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Arch&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Image&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;SGLang (CUDA 13.0)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;multi-arch (&lt;code&gt;amd64&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;arm64&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/ai-dynamo/sglang-runtime:1.6.0-muse-spark-open-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;vLLM (CUDA 13.0)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;multi-arch (&lt;code&gt;amd64&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;arm64&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/ai-dynamo/vllm-runtime:1.6.0-muse-spark-open-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;TensorRT-LLM (CUDA 13.1)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;arm64&lt;/code&gt; only&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/ai-dynamo/tensorrtllm-runtime:1.6.0-muse-spark-open-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The recipes pin these images by digest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend Versions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Source&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;CUDA&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Python&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;SGLang&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Dynamo-built runtime on &lt;code&gt;lmsysorg/sglang:dev-muse-spark-open@sha256:8cfc5a72cb296771f5f8a4a4688cb6d05685610a830cbb616fa4ab0eb7bb2b0a&lt;/code&gt;, rebaselined on NVIDIA CUDA 13.0.3 for compliance&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;13.0&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;upstream image&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NIXL from the upstream SGLang image; VP8/VP9-only FFmpeg for Rust media decoding&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;vLLM&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Dynamo-built runtime on &lt;code&gt;vllm/vllm-openai:muse-spark-open@sha256:c91025b5be1039a93ca975d1d44f352b0e770bb6c8b142b5056cf92204ca137c&lt;/code&gt;, rebaselined on NVIDIA CUDA 13.0.3 for compliance&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;13.0&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;3.12&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Keeps the model image&#39;s Transformers stack; vLLM-Omni disabled; NIXL from the upstream vLLM image&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;TensorRT-LLM&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Dynamo-built runtime on &lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/tensorrt-llm/release:1.3.0rc25&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;13.1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;3.12&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NIXL v1.3.1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Models&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Model&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Precision&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;GPU&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;meta-models/Muse-Spark-Open-816B-A42B-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NVFP4 weights, FP8 KV cache&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;GB200, GB300&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;816B total / 42B active parameters; 1M-token context; TP4/EP4; &lt;code&gt;muse_spark&lt;/code&gt; reasoning and tool-call parsers&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Muse Spark Open&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Muse Spark Open&lt;/strong&gt; is a Meta mixture-of-experts model (816B total parameters, 42B active) published as &lt;code&gt;meta-models/Muse-Spark-Open-816B-A42B-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt; (NVFP4). This build serves it through Dynamo&#39;s SGLang, vLLM, and TensorRT-LLM backends, with aggregated, disaggregated, and KV-aware routed serving on SGLang and aggregated serving on vLLM and TensorRT-LLM.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Changelog&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend and Responses API&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Muse Spark Open parsers:&lt;/strong&gt; Added the &lt;code&gt;muse_spark&lt;/code&gt; reasoning and tool-call parsers on the unified parser path. Parser, protocol, and renderer crates are pinned to published versions across the root, Python, and KVBM workspaces, including &lt;code&gt;dynamo-parsers =8.2.0-muse-spark-open-dev.1&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16700&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16700/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16700&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tools:&lt;/strong&gt; Native, deferred, and custom tool support, with expanded &lt;code&gt;tool_choice&lt;/code&gt; handling (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16700&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16700/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16700&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responses API:&lt;/strong&gt; Commentary-phase streaming, conversation history replay, and client-side tool-search handling (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16700&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16700/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16700&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Backend&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Muse Spark Open runtime:&lt;/strong&gt; Built on a digest-pinned public SGLang model image, with compatibility fixes for the multimodal encode worker, argument handling, and model registration (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16700&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16700/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16700&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Backend&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Muse Spark Open runtime:&lt;/strong&gt; Built on a digest-pinned public vLLM model image that preserves the model&#39;s dependency combination. vLLM-Omni is disabled for this release and unused InstantTensor is removed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend compatibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixes for the embedding worker, renderer, and KV-event APIs, and an explicit &lt;code&gt;imageio&amp;gt;=2.37.0&lt;/code&gt; requirement for video request processing (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16700&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16700/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16700&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM Backend&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM 1.3.0rc25:&lt;/strong&gt; Runtime on the &lt;code&gt;1.3.0rc25&lt;/code&gt; release image with LLM worker updates and unit tests (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16700&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16700/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16700&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Containers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance:&lt;/strong&gt; Stricter license and attribution auditing for the shipped images, including exact Rust/Go binary dependencies, Python environments, and removal of unneeded development packages from the SGLang base. Native &lt;code&gt;amd64&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;arm64&lt;/code&gt; final-image audits are required (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16700&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16700/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16700&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recipes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Muse Spark Open recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Added &lt;code&gt;recipes/muse-spark-open-816b-a42b&lt;/code&gt; with shared model-cache PVC and download job, six SGLang targets (aggregated, 1P1D disaggregated with NIXL, and KV-aware routed on GB200 and GB300), two experimental vLLM aggregated targets, and a perf/trace reference (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16553&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16553/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16553&lt;/a&gt;) (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/tree/6b9d12ebcd371ced77af980b0ae72e7f0f054c2d/recipes/muse-spark-open-816b-a42b&quot;&gt;recipe folder&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/6b9d12ebcd371ced77af980b0ae72e7f0f054c2d/recipes/muse-spark-open-816b-a42b/README.md&quot;&gt;README&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Added experimental aggregated TensorRT-LLM targets for GB200 and GB300 (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16567&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16567/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16567&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Display name:&lt;/strong&gt; Capitalized &quot;Open&quot; in the recipe display name (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16557&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16557/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16557&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Getting Started&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deployment is Kubernetes-based (Dynamo Platform + &lt;code&gt;DynamoGraphDeployment&lt;/code&gt;). Full steps (namespace, Hugging Face token secret, model-cache PVC, model download job, DGD apply, and a &lt;code&gt;/v1/chat/completions&lt;/code&gt; smoke test) are in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/6b9d12ebcd371ced77af980b0ae72e7f0f054c2d/recipes/muse-spark-open-816b-a42b/README.md&quot;&gt;recipe README&lt;/a&gt; and the linked recipe page. Recipes expect a Hugging Face token secret named &lt;code&gt;hf-token-secret&lt;/code&gt; and a ReadWriteMany storage class for the &lt;code&gt;shared-model-cache&lt;/code&gt; PVC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Known Issues / Limitations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experimental snapshot build, not QA-gated; not for production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The vLLM and TensorRT-LLM recipes are experimental and aggregated only. Their results cover the first 500 trace requests and are functional validation, not full-trace benchmarks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SGLang disaggregated recipes do not support video requests (the image has no &lt;code&gt;decord2&lt;/code&gt;) or frontend decoding (&lt;code&gt;DYN_SGL_FRONTEND_DECODING=true&lt;/code&gt;) for image or video inputs. Use an aggregated SGLang recipe for video.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Disaggregated recipes omit provider-specific networking; configure RDMA for long-context requests. SGLang GB200 recipes and GB300 disaggregated recipes require ComputeDomain with Dynamic Resource Allocation (DRA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The TensorRT-LLM image is &lt;code&gt;arm64&lt;/code&gt; only, matching the GB200 and GB300 recipes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Targets Hopper and Blackwell GPUs. vLLM serving CI on A100 and L4 hardware hit CUDA &lt;code&gt;no kernel image is available&lt;/code&gt; errors, and broader backend serving CI was not fully green at merge of &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5892144709&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/16700&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16700/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16700&quot;&gt;#16700&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;</content>
    <author>
      <name>ynpandey-nv</name>
    </author>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20666257?s=60&amp;v=4"/>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/942206898/v1.6.0-beam-1.0-501b-dev.1</id>
    <updated>2026-10-19T23:39:54Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/releases/tag/v1.6.0-beam-1.0-501b-dev.1"/>
    <title>Dynamo v1.6.0-beam-1.0-501b-dev.1</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Notes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo v1.6.0-beam-1.0-501b-dev.1&lt;/strong&gt; is an experimental snapshot build with early &lt;strong&gt;Reflection Beam-1.0-501B-A23B&lt;/strong&gt; support on the Dynamo &lt;strong&gt;SGLang&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt; backends. It is &lt;strong&gt;not recommended for production&lt;/strong&gt; and is not a QA-gated release. APIs, behavior, and defaults may change before stable support. Use it for evaluation, testing, and early feedback only.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dynamo v1.6.0-beam-1.0-501b-dev.1 serves &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;reflection/Beam-1.0-501B-A23B&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; on Dynamo &lt;strong&gt;SGLang&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt;. The frontend adds a Beam parser family on the unified v2 route and derives a Beam turn grammar for every chat turn, so tool calls, structured answers, and reasoning follow the model&#39;s channel format. &lt;code&gt;/v1/completions&lt;/code&gt; can now echo the prompt with its logprobs. The vLLM runtime uses &lt;code&gt;vllm/vllm-openai:v0.31.0-ubuntu2404&lt;/code&gt; and the SGLang runtime uses &lt;code&gt;lmsysorg/sglang:v0.5.21-cu130-runtime&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16702&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16702/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16702&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kubernetes recipes cover aggregated and 1P1D disaggregated serving on both backends across H200, B200, B300, GB200, and GB300. Every target uses DFlash2 speculative decoding (block length 8), FP8 KV cache, KV-aware routing, and up to 1M tokens of context, with FP8 weights on H200 and NVFP4 weights on the Blackwell GPUs. The recipes include a shared model-cache PVC and download job, an AIPerf synthetic benchmark, and a recipe page on the docs site under &lt;code&gt;recipes/beam-1.0-501b&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16666&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16666/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16666&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16677&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16677/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16677&lt;/a&gt;, cherry-picked in &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16846&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16846/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16846&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Branch&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;release/1.6.0-beam-1.0-501b-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;, tip &lt;code&gt;ef20f7776f20f6c81f8159063918e086eda308d7&lt;/code&gt; (2026-10-19)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Base Commit&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;c5773baaa579eac59e84860d31e7273d14308a7c&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;main&lt;/code&gt; (2026-10-14)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;v0.31.0&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;vllm/vllm-openai&lt;/code&gt;, CUDA 13.0), NIXL v1.4.1&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;SGLang&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;v0.5.21&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;lmsysorg/sglang&lt;/code&gt;, CUDA 13.0), NIXL v1.5.0&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Container Images&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Arch&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Image&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;vLLM (CUDA 13.0)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;multi-arch (&lt;code&gt;amd64&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;arm64&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/ai-dynamo/vllm-runtime:1.6.0-beam-1.0-501b-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;SGLang (CUDA 13.0)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;multi-arch (&lt;code&gt;amd64&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;arm64&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/ai-dynamo/sglang-runtime:1.6.0-beam-1.0-501b-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend Versions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Source&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;CUDA&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Python&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;vLLM&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Dynamo-built runtime on &lt;code&gt;vllm/vllm-openai:v0.31.0-ubuntu2404&lt;/code&gt;, compliance baseline on &lt;code&gt;nvidia/cuda:13.0.2-base-ubuntu24.04&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;13.0&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;3.12&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NIXL v1.4.1; Beam parser crates &lt;code&gt;dynamo-parsers-v2&lt;/code&gt; 0.10.0 and &lt;code&gt;dynamo-renderer&lt;/code&gt; 8.1.0&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;SGLang&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Dynamo-built runtime on &lt;code&gt;lmsysorg/sglang:v0.5.21-cu130-runtime&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;13.0&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;3.12&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NIXL v1.5.0; publishes KV events for KV-aware routing&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Models&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Model&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Precision&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;GPU&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;reflection/Beam-1.0-501B-A23B-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NVFP4 weights, FP8 KV cache&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;B200, B300, GB200, GB300&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;served as &lt;code&gt;Beam-1.0-501B-A23B&lt;/code&gt;; up to 1,048,576 context tokens&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;reflection/Beam-1.0-501B-A23B-FP8&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;FP8 weights, FP8 KV cache&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;H200&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;served as &lt;code&gt;Beam-1.0-501B-A23B&lt;/code&gt;; up to 1,048,576 context tokens&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;reflection/Beam-1.0-501B-A23B-DFlash2&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;draft checkpoint&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;every target&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;DFlash2 speculative decoding, block length 8&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Beam-1.0-501B-A23B&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beam-1.0-501B-A23B&lt;/strong&gt; is Reflection&#39;s Beam 1.0 model, published on Hugging Face as &lt;code&gt;reflection/Beam-1.0-501B-A23B-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;reflection/Beam-1.0-501B-A23B-FP8&lt;/code&gt;, with a &lt;code&gt;reflection/Beam-1.0-501B-A23B-DFlash2&lt;/code&gt; draft checkpoint. This build serves it through Dynamo&#39;s SGLang and vLLM backends, aggregated or disaggregated, with DFlash2 speculative decoding and up to 1M tokens of context.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Changelog&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend (Beam Serving)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beam parser family:&lt;/strong&gt; Added the Beam parser family on the unified v2 route. The parser resumes in the channel an assistant prefill leaves open, and the Beam route keeps only the model&#39;s own stop-token text (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16702&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16702/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16702&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beam turn grammar:&lt;/strong&gt; Every chat turn is constrained by a structural-tag grammar derived from the Beam response template. Forced tool choices stay on the Harmony wire, &lt;code&gt;builtin_tools&lt;/code&gt; are declared by name for the 1.0 chat template, and a &lt;code&gt;response_format&lt;/code&gt; answer is held in the final channel with its tool arguments framed (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16702&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16702/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16702&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Request policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Tools whose &lt;code&gt;strict&lt;/code&gt; schema Beam cannot honor are served as non-strict, with one warning per request. &lt;code&gt;preserve_thinking=false&lt;/code&gt; is accepted as a no-op, and &lt;code&gt;allow_missing_thinking&lt;/code&gt; defaults to true (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16702&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16702/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16702&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Completions echo:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;/v1/completions&lt;/code&gt; echoes the prompt together with its logprobs (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16702&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16702/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16702&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Parser crates:&lt;/strong&gt; Pinned &lt;code&gt;dynamo-renderer&lt;/code&gt; 8.1.0 and &lt;code&gt;dynamo-parsers-v2&lt;/code&gt; 0.10.0 from &lt;code&gt;frontend-crates&lt;/code&gt; at the Beam release revision (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/frontend-crates/commit/ef8f401393a730cae8ac5c96fe1d564dcf48a017&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;ef8f4013&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/frontend-crates/pull/430&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/frontend-crates/pull/430/hovercard&quot;&gt;frontend-crates#430&lt;/a&gt;) (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16702&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16702/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16702&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Backend&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lazy engine-launch imports:&lt;/strong&gt; The vLLM engine-launch imports load lazily, which the Beam vLLM engine needs, and &lt;code&gt;chat_utils&lt;/code&gt; is imported from its new vLLM location when present (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16702&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16702/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16702&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recipes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beam-1.0-501B-A23B recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Added &lt;code&gt;recipes/beam-1.0-501b&lt;/code&gt; with a shared model-cache PVC and download job, an AIPerf benchmark, and a docs-site recipe page (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16666&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16666/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16666&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16677&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16677/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16677&lt;/a&gt;, cherry-picked in &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16846&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16846/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16846&lt;/a&gt;; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/tree/ef20f7776f20f6c81f8159063918e086eda308d7/recipes/beam-1.0-501b&quot;&gt;recipe folder&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/ef20f7776f20f6c81f8159063918e086eda308d7/docs/fern/pages/recipes/model-recipes/beam-1-0-501b.mdx&quot;&gt;recipe guide&lt;/a&gt;):
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SGLang and vLLM, aggregated and 1P1D disaggregated, on H200 (FP8, 8 GPUs aggregated or 16 disaggregated) and on B200, B300, GB200, and GB300 (NVFP4, 8 GPUs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DFlash2 block length 8, FP8 KV cache with 64-token pages, and up to 1,048,576 context tokens on every target.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;KV-aware routing: SGLang publishes KV events and vLLM uses prediction-based routing. Disaggregated targets move KV between prefill and decode over NIXL, and vLLM targets add native host offload.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An AIPerf synthetic chat benchmark (8,192 input and 1,024 output tokens, streaming, one concurrency point per Job).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reflection logo:&lt;/strong&gt; Added the Reflection provider logo to the recipe catalog (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16677&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16677/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16677&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Getting Started&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deployment is Kubernetes-based (Dynamo Platform + &lt;code&gt;DynamoGraphDeployment&lt;/code&gt;). Full steps — namespace, model-cache PVC, Hugging Face download job (target checkpoint plus the DFlash2 draft), DGD apply, and a &lt;code&gt;/v1/chat/completions&lt;/code&gt; smoke test — are in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/ef20f7776f20f6c81f8159063918e086eda308d7/recipes/beam-1.0-501b/README.md&quot;&gt;recipe README&lt;/a&gt;. The benchmark workflow is in &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/ef20f7776f20f6c81f8159063918e086eda308d7/recipes/beam-1.0-501b/perf/README.md&quot;&gt;perf/README.md&lt;/a&gt;. For gated Hugging Face repositories, add an &lt;code&gt;HF_TOKEN&lt;/code&gt; secret reference to the download Job.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Known Issues / Limitations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experimental snapshot build — not QA-gated; not for production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The &lt;code&gt;shared-model-cache&lt;/code&gt; PVC needs at least 2Ti on a ReadWriteMany storage class; set &lt;code&gt;storageClassName&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;model-cache/model-cache.yaml&lt;/code&gt; before applying it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Disaggregated targets need GPUDirect-capable RDMA devices on both roles and NIXL/UCX connectivity between them. A TCP fallback works without RDMA, but KV transfer then goes through host memory and the pod network.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;vLLM disaggregated targets register the whole KV pool as one memory region. If the NIC rejects it (&lt;code&gt;NIXL_ERR_BACKEND&lt;/code&gt;), lower &lt;code&gt;--gpu-memory-utilization&lt;/code&gt;; the B300 and GB300 disaggregated profiles already ship at 0.5.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Every target requires the DFlash2 draft checkpoint in addition to the target checkpoint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;</content>
    <author>
      <name>ynpandey-nv</name>
    </author>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20666257?s=60&amp;v=4"/>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/942206898/v1.6.0-nemotron-3.5-super-vl-dev.1</id>
    <updated>2026-10-15T22:09:49Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/releases/tag/v1.6.0-nemotron-3.5-super-vl-dev.1"/>
    <title>Dynamo v1.6.0-nemotron-3.5-super-vl-dev.1</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Notes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo v1.6.0-nemotron-3.5-super-vl-dev.1&lt;/strong&gt; is an experimental snapshot build with early &lt;strong&gt;NVIDIA Nemotron 3.5 Super VL&lt;/strong&gt; support on the Dynamo &lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM&lt;/strong&gt; backends. It is &lt;strong&gt;not recommended for production&lt;/strong&gt; and is not a QA-gated release. APIs, behavior, and defaults may change before stable support. Use it for evaluation, testing, and early feedback only.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dynamo v1.6.0-nemotron-3.5-super-vl-dev.1 serves &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Super-VL-120B-A12B-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, a multimodal MoE model with up to 1M-token context, on Dynamo &lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM&lt;/strong&gt;. The vLLM runtime moves to a CUDA 13.4 vLLM nightly with Mamba2, top-p sampling, and FlashInfer fixes. The TensorRT-LLM runtime uses &lt;code&gt;1.3.0rc29&lt;/code&gt; with quantized MTP head loading, draft KV-pool reuse, and a guided-decoding fix for multimodal input (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16549&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16549/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16549&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kubernetes recipes cover aggregated and disaggregated vLLM targets on H100, H200, B200, B300, GB200, GB300, and VR200, plus aggregated and disaggregated TensorRT-LLM targets on B200. Every target uses NVFP4 weights, FP8 KV cache, MTP speculative decoding, session-affinity routing, and 1M context. The recipes include a shared model-cache PVC and download job, and an AIPerf SWE-bench Pro trace-replay benchmark under &lt;code&gt;recipes/nemotron-3.5-super-vl-120b-a12b&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16544&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16544/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16544&lt;/a&gt;, cherry-picked in &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16552&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16552/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16552&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Branch&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;release/1.6.0-nemotron-3.5-super-vl-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;, tip &lt;code&gt;5f601dba872b1a26b40090c319df8edbb8f946bd&lt;/code&gt; (2026-10-15)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt;: nightly &lt;code&gt;cu134-nightly-bb87d227d4b964abb2a966cdf9194f3d376d9bbe&lt;/code&gt; base (CUDA 13.4), NIXL v1.3.2&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;1.3.0rc29&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/tensorrt-llm/release&lt;/code&gt;), NIXL v1.3.1&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Container Images&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Arch&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Image&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;vLLM (CUDA 13.4)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;multi-arch (&lt;code&gt;amd64&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;arm64&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/ai-dynamo/vllm-runtime:1.6.0-nemotron-3.5-super-vl-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;TensorRT-LLM (CUDA 13.1)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;multi-arch (&lt;code&gt;amd64&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;arm64&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/ai-dynamo/tensorrtllm-runtime:1.6.0-nemotron-3.5-super-vl-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend Versions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Source&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;CUDA&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Python&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;vLLM&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Dynamo-built runtime on &lt;code&gt;vllm/vllm-openai:cu134-nightly-bb87d227d4b964abb2a966cdf9194f3d376d9bbe&lt;/code&gt;, compliance baseline on &lt;code&gt;nvidia/cuda:13.4.1-base-ubuntu24.04&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;13.4&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;3.12&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NIXL v1.3.2; vLLM-Omni disabled on CUDA so the nightly&#39;s Transformers and tokenizers stay in place&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;TensorRT-LLM&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Dynamo-built runtime on &lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/tensorrt-llm/release:1.3.0rc29&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;13.1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;3.12&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NIXL v1.3.1; TensorRT-LLM #19303, #19558, #19597 backported&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Models&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Model&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Precision&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;GPU&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Super-VL-120B-A12B-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NVFP4 weights, FP8 KV cache&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;H100, H200, B200, B300, GB200, GB300, VR200&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;served as &lt;code&gt;nvidia/nemotron-3.5-super-vl-120b-a12b&lt;/code&gt;; &lt;code&gt;nemotron_v3&lt;/code&gt; reasoning and &lt;code&gt;qwen3_coder&lt;/code&gt; tool-call parsers; built-in MTP head for speculative decoding&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nemotron 3.5 Super VL&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nemotron 3.5 Super VL&lt;/strong&gt; is an NVIDIA 120B-A12B multimodal MoE preview model, published on Hugging Face as &lt;code&gt;nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Super-VL-120B-A12B-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;. It reasons before answering, supports tool calling, and serves up to 1M tokens of context. This build serves it through Dynamo vLLM on Hopper, Blackwell, and Rubin, and through Dynamo TensorRT-LLM on B200, with MTP speculative decoding on both.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Changelog&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Backend&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CUDA 13.4 runtime:&lt;/strong&gt; Moved the vLLM runtime to the &lt;code&gt;cu134-nightly-bb87d227&lt;/code&gt; base and refreshed the amd64 and arm64 compliance baselines against CUDA 13.4.1. vLLM-Omni is skipped on CUDA because the nightly needs Transformers 5.16.1 or later; CPU and XPU images keep Omni (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16549&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16549/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16549&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Model and sampling fixes:&lt;/strong&gt; Backported vLLM #60797, which stores the convolution history in Mamba2 prefill checkpoints so cached prefixes resume with the correct state, and vLLM #58231, which preserves forced large logits in split top-p masking (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16549&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16549/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16549&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FlashInfer kernels:&lt;/strong&gt; Backported FlashInfer &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;3792274229&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/5267&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;issue&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/5267/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/5267&quot;&gt;#5267&lt;/a&gt; (stochastic rounding on SM107) and an opt-in multi-wave KV split for long-context attention from FlashInfer &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;3954135233&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/6331&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;issue&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/6331/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/6331&quot;&gt;#6331&lt;/a&gt; and vLLM #61077, enabled with &lt;code&gt;VLLM_FLASHINFER_MULTI_WAVE_KV_SPLIT&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16549&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16549/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16549&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disaggregated serving with CPU offload:&lt;/strong&gt; Dynamo now detects NIXL inside a vLLM &lt;code&gt;MultiConnector&lt;/code&gt;, so a worker that combines NIXL transfer with CPU KV offload sets up the NIXL side channel correctly (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16549&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16549/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16549&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM Backend&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM 1.3.0rc29 with MTP fixes:&lt;/strong&gt; Backported TensorRT-LLM #19558 and #19597, which load quantized MTP heads and their replacement modules, and #19303, which publishes the one-model draft KV pool so the draft no longer attends over unwritten pages on reused prefixes (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16549&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16549/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16549&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal with guided decoding:&lt;/strong&gt; Guided decoding stays in CUDA graphs and drains its host functions before multimodal encoders run, avoiding a deadlock on image input. Dynamo also runs media preprocessing off the event loop so image decoding no longer blocks request handling (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16549&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16549/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16549&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Runtime attribution:&lt;/strong&gt; License attribution now covers system Python roots, vendored Python distributions, and Rust and Go dependencies embedded in shipped binaries, with architecture-specific completeness checks for both runtimes. AI Simulate is pinned to the published &lt;code&gt;0.13.0-dev.2&lt;/code&gt; release (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16549&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16549/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16549&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recipes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nemotron 3.5 Super VL recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Added &lt;code&gt;recipes/nemotron-3.5-super-vl-120b-a12b&lt;/code&gt;, with a shared model-cache PVC and download job and SWE-bench Pro deployments (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16544&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16544/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16544&lt;/a&gt;, cherry-picked in &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16552&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16552/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16552&lt;/a&gt;; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/tree/5f601dba872b1a26b40090c319df8edbb8f946bd/recipes/nemotron-3.5-super-vl-120b-a12b&quot;&gt;recipe folder&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/5f601dba872b1a26b40090c319df8edbb8f946bd/docs/fern/pages/recipes/model-recipes/nemotron-3-5-super-vl-120b-a12b.mdx&quot;&gt;recipe guide&lt;/a&gt;):
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;vLLM aggregated and disaggregated targets on H100, H200, B200, B300, GB200, GB300, and VR200, from 2 GPUs (H200) to 11 GPUs (VR200 7P4D). They use KV-aware routing with session affinity, MTP3 or MTP5, and CPU KV offload.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TensorRT-LLM aggregated (4 workers) and 2P2D disaggregated targets on B200 with MTP3, load-based placement, and session affinity for prefix reuse.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An AIPerf 0.13 job that replays 400 SWE-bench Pro agent trajectories (median input 222K tokens, 99% KV cache hit rate) to measure throughput and latency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Getting Started&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deployment is Kubernetes-based (Dynamo Platform + &lt;code&gt;DynamoGraphDeployment&lt;/code&gt;). Full steps — namespace and Hugging Face token secret, model-cache PVC, download job, DGD apply, and a &lt;code&gt;/v1/chat/completions&lt;/code&gt; smoke test — are in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/5f601dba872b1a26b40090c319df8edbb8f946bd/docs/fern/pages/recipes/model-recipes/nemotron-3-5-super-vl-120b-a12b.mdx&quot;&gt;recipe guide&lt;/a&gt;. The benchmark workflow is in &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/5f601dba872b1a26b40090c319df8edbb8f946bd/recipes/nemotron-3.5-super-vl-120b-a12b/perf/README.md&quot;&gt;perf/README.md&lt;/a&gt;. Recipes expect a Hugging Face token secret named &lt;code&gt;hf-token-secret&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Known Issues / Limitations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experimental snapshot build — not QA-gated; not for production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TensorRT-LLM recipes in this build cover B200 only.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TensorRT-LLM workers publish no KV events, so the router places new sessions by load and relies on session affinity for prefix-cache reuse.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The &lt;code&gt;shared-model-cache&lt;/code&gt; PVC needs a ReadWriteMany storage class; set &lt;code&gt;storageClassName&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;model-cache/model-cache.yaml&lt;/code&gt; before applying it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GB200, GB300, and VR200 disaggregated recipes require the NVIDIA DRA driver with ComputeDomain support for multi-node NVLink.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The published VR200 results used a synthetic MTP acceptance length; the VR200 recipes default to natural acceptance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;</content>
    <author>
      <name>ynpandey-nv</name>
    </author>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20666257?s=60&amp;v=4"/>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/942206898/v1.6.0-glm-5.3-flash-dev.1</id>
    <updated>2026-10-14T04:01:46Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/releases/tag/v1.6.0-glm-5.3-flash-dev.1"/>
    <title>Dynamo v1.6.0-glm-5.3-flash-dev.1</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Notes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo v1.6.0-glm-5.3-flash-dev.1&lt;/strong&gt; is an experimental snapshot build with early &lt;strong&gt;GLM-5.3-Flash&lt;/strong&gt; support on the Dynamo &lt;strong&gt;SGLang&lt;/strong&gt; backend. It is &lt;strong&gt;not recommended for production&lt;/strong&gt; and is not a QA-gated release. APIs, behavior, and defaults may change before stable support. Use it for evaluation, testing, and early feedback only.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dynamo v1.6.0-glm-5.3-flash-dev.1 serves &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;RadixArk/GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; on Dynamo &lt;strong&gt;SGLang&lt;/strong&gt;. The container is built from &lt;code&gt;lmsysorg/sglang:v0.5.21-cu130-runtime&lt;/code&gt; (CUDA 13) and applies GLM-5.3-Flash backports for prefill/decode accounting, linear-attention cache handling, SM100 PTX KDA, and Mamba slot cleanup, plus a scoped cuDNN workaround in the vision encoder. Transformers 5.19.0 and tokenizers 0.23.2 are pinned so image and video requests load &lt;code&gt;Glm5NextProcessor&lt;/code&gt; instead of falling back to text-only tokenization (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15751&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15751/hovercard&quot;&gt;#15751&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kubernetes recipes cover a 4-GPU aggregated profile on B200 or GB200 and a 12-GPU GB200 disaggregated profile (two TP4/EP4 prefill workers and one TP4 decode worker). Aggregated serving uses round-robin routing and accepts text, images, and video. Disaggregated serving uses KV-aware routing with worker KV events and Mooncake transfer over NVLink, and accepts text and images. All three profiles use NVFP4 weights, FP8 KV cache, EAGLE speculative decoding with ReplaySSM, and HiCache. A shared model-cache download pins revision &lt;code&gt;f46cf340d35a22d0d83d0c1dac8957cf2b1bcd35&lt;/code&gt;, and an AIPerf text-trace reference ships with the recipes (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15752&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15752/hovercard&quot;&gt;#15752&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16387&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16387/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16387&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Branch&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;release/1.6.0-glm-5.3-flash-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;, tip &lt;code&gt;6beb56900f9c83c3d7720432006ffc42d0c328c2&lt;/code&gt; (2026-10-14)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;SGLang&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;lmsysorg/sglang:v0.5.21-cu130-runtime&lt;/code&gt; (CUDA 13.0); disaggregated KV transfer uses Mooncake over NVLink&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Container Images&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Arch&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Image&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;SGLang (CUDA 13)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;multi-arch (&lt;code&gt;amd64&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;arm64&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/ai-dynamo/sglang-runtime:1.6.0-glm-5.3-flash-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend Versions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Source&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;CUDA&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Python&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;SGLang&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Dynamo-built runtime on &lt;code&gt;lmsysorg/sglang:v0.5.21-cu130-runtime&lt;/code&gt;, source &lt;code&gt;e00930c5489053f26d86b179cee0d087f846acbb&lt;/code&gt;, with six upstream GLM-5.3-Flash backports and one local vision-encoder workaround&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;13.0&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;3.12&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Transformers 5.19.0; tokenizers 0.23.2; NIXL/UCX are not added to the CUDA runtime&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Models&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Model&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Precision&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;GPU&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;RadixArk/GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NVFP4&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;4x B200 or 4x GB200 aggregated; 12x GB200 disaggregated&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;revision &lt;code&gt;f46cf340d35a22d0d83d0c1dac8957cf2b1bcd35&lt;/code&gt;; FP8 E4M3 KV; EAGLE ReplaySSM; text, image, and video on aggregated profiles&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About GLM-5.3-Flash&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GLM-5.3-Flash&lt;/strong&gt; is a Z.AI mixture-of-experts model (320B total parameters, 18B active) with hybrid sparse and linear attention and Manifold-Constrained Hyper-Connections. This preview serves the NVFP4 checkpoint &lt;code&gt;RadixArk/GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt; through Dynamo&#39;s SGLang backend, aggregated on B200 or GB200 or disaggregated on GB200.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Changelog&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Backend&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GLM-5.3-Flash runtime:&lt;/strong&gt; Builds the CUDA SGLang image on &lt;code&gt;lmsysorg/sglang:v0.5.21-cu130-runtime&lt;/code&gt; and applies upstream backports for prefill/decode latency and retraction accounting, linear-attention hooks and cache accounting, PTX KDA safety and SM100 support, and Mamba slot cleanup before decode preallocation. A local patch disables cuDNN only around the GLM vision downsample convolution. Transformers 5.19.0 and tokenizers 0.23.2 are pinned so AutoProcessor registers &lt;code&gt;Glm5NextProcessor&lt;/code&gt; for image and video inputs (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15751&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15751/hovercard&quot;&gt;#15751&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recipes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GLM-5.3-Flash SGLang recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Added &lt;code&gt;recipes/glm-5.3-flash/sglang&lt;/code&gt; — shared model-cache PVC and pinned Hugging Face download, B200 aggregated (&lt;code&gt;agg-b200-agentic&lt;/code&gt;, 1x TP4), GB200 aggregated (&lt;code&gt;agg-gb200-agentic&lt;/code&gt;, 1x TP4), and GB200 disaggregated (&lt;code&gt;disagg-gb200-agentic&lt;/code&gt;, 2 prefill TP4/EP4 + 1 decode TP4, Mooncake over NVLink) profiles, real EAGLE verification by default, and an AIPerf text-trace reference (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/tree/6beb56900f9c83c3d7720432006ffc42d0c328c2/recipes/glm-5.3-flash&quot;&gt;recipe folder&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/6beb56900f9c83c3d7720432006ffc42d0c328c2/recipes/glm-5.3-flash/README.md&quot;&gt;README&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15752&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15752/hovercard&quot;&gt;#15752&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16387&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16387/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16387&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Getting Started&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deployment is Kubernetes-based (Dynamo Platform and &lt;code&gt;DynamoGraphDeployment&lt;/code&gt;). GB200 profiles also create a ComputeDomain and require the NVIDIA DRA driver. Full steps — namespace, &lt;code&gt;hf-token-secret&lt;/code&gt;, model-cache PVC, pinned Hugging Face download, Kustomize render, DGD apply, and a &lt;code&gt;/v1/chat/completions&lt;/code&gt; smoke test — are in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/6beb56900f9c83c3d7720432006ffc42d0c328c2/recipes/glm-5.3-flash/README.md&quot;&gt;recipe README&lt;/a&gt;. The SGLang checkpoint is &lt;code&gt;RadixArk/GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt; and is not the checkpoint used by the sibling vLLM recipes. Recipes expect registry credentials for &lt;code&gt;nvcr.io&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Known Issues / Limitations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experimental snapshot build — not QA-gated; not for production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The disaggregated GB200 recipe accepts text and images only. Video input is available on the aggregated B200 and GB200 recipes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Disaggregated GB200 workers must share one NVLink clique and require the ComputeDomain CRD and NVIDIA DRA driver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthetic acceptance replaces real speculative verification and is for performance experiments only.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;End-to-end multimodal generation with this rebuilt image has not been validated. The image build checks that the GLM image and video processors load.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measured performance results are not included. The recipe ships an AIPerf text-trace job only.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;</content>
    <author>
      <name>ynpandey-nv</name>
    </author>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20666257?s=60&amp;v=4"/>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/942206898/v1.5.0-motif-3-dev.2</id>
    <updated>2026-10-14T05:11:54Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/releases/tag/v1.5.0-motif-3-dev.2"/>
    <title>Dynamo v1.5.0-motif-3-dev.2</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Notes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo v1.5.0-motif-3-dev.2&lt;/strong&gt; is an experimental snapshot build with early &lt;strong&gt;Motif-3 NVFP4&lt;/strong&gt; support on the Dynamo &lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt; backend. It is &lt;strong&gt;not recommended for production&lt;/strong&gt; and is not a QA-gated release. APIs, behavior, and defaults may change before stable support. Use it for evaluation, testing, and early feedback only.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dynamo v1.5.0-motif-3-dev.2 serves &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Motif-Technologies/Motif-3-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; on Dynamo &lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt;. The amd64 CUDA 13.0 runtime is built on Motif&#39;s vLLM &lt;code&gt;v0.26.0-motif3&lt;/code&gt; base, with vLLM-Omni disabled, and installs NIXL v1.3.2. The image bakes in Motif NIXL compatibility fixes: KV-cache rank follows the attention backend&#39;s MLA flag (rank 3 for MLA, rank 4 otherwise), and Motif keeps its NHD cache layout (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16291&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16291/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16291&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kubernetes recipes cover aggregated serving on two B200 GPUs and disaggregated 3P1D serving on eight B200 GPUs: three TP2 prefill workers and one TP2 decode worker, with KV-aware routing and NIXL transfer. Both profiles use expert parallelism, MTP2, an FP8 KV cache, a 262,144-token context, prefix caching, and a shared model cache. The 3P1D recipe from &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16314&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16314/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16314&lt;/a&gt; is on this branch in &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16392&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16392/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16392&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/tree/b3132ac9f4757db523c79dc2f2066b52e0412848/recipes/motif-3&quot;&gt;recipe folder&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base Branch&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;release/1.5.0&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Base Commit&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;f5802d355b59b5006c67a16c3ed1615cfcab5686&lt;/code&gt; (2026-08-18)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Preview Branch&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;release/1.5.0-motif-3-dev.2&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Preview Tip&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;b3132ac9f4757db523c79dc2f2066b52e0412848&lt;/code&gt; (2026-10-14)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;ghcr.io/motiftechnologies/vllm:v0.26.0-motif3@sha256:c90d471174ec29a0f6c5ecba718a6905a4180be72f2c6d37ce9dad4d799fa836&lt;/code&gt; (CUDA 13.0), NIXL v1.3.2&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Container Images&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Arch&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Image&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;vLLM (CUDA 13.0)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;amd64&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/ai-dynamo/vllm-runtime:1.5.0-motif-3-dev.2&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend Versions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Source&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;CUDA&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Python&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;vLLM&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Dynamo-built runtime on &lt;code&gt;ghcr.io/motiftechnologies/vllm:v0.26.0-motif3@sha256:c90d471174ec29a0f6c5ecba718a6905a4180be72f2c6d37ce9dad4d799fa836&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;13.0&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;3.12&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NIXL v1.3.2 (&lt;code&gt;nixl-cu13&lt;/code&gt;); vLLM-Omni disabled; Motif NIXL patch applied at build; amd64 only&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Models&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Model&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Precision&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;GPU&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;Motif-Technologies/Motif-3-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NVFP4 (&lt;code&gt;modelopt_nvfp4&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;2x B200&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;aggregated vLLM; TP2, expert parallelism, MTP2, FP8 KV cache, 262K context&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;Motif-Technologies/Motif-3-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NVFP4 (&lt;code&gt;modelopt_nvfp4&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;8x B200&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;disaggregated 3P1D; 3× TP2 prefill + 1× TP2 decode, KV-aware routing, NIXL transfer, MTP2, FP8 KV cache, 262K context&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Motif-3&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Motif-3 NVFP4&lt;/strong&gt; is Motif Technologies&#39; preview checkpoint published on Hugging Face as &lt;code&gt;Motif-Technologies/Motif-3-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;. This build serves it through Dynamo&#39;s vLLM backend as either an aggregated two-GPU B200 deployment or an eight-GPU 3P1D deployment with KV-aware routing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Changelog&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Backend&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Motif NIXL compatibility:&lt;/strong&gt; The runtime image patches the pinned Motif vLLM source during the build so workers can transfer KV cache without a writable source tree. Cache-rank checks use the attention backend&#39;s MLA flag, and Motif retains the NHD layout (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16291&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16291/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16291&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recipes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Motif-3 NVFP4 recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;recipes/motif-3&lt;/code&gt; includes a shared model-cache PVC and Hugging Face download Job, an aggregated B200 chat profile, and a disaggregated 3P1D profile with KV-aware routing and NIXL transfer. Both default to real MTP2 verification. An optional synthetic acceptance length of 2.13 is available for benchmarking, including a concurrency-64 disaggregated run with a 32-request warmup (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/tree/b3132ac9f4757db523c79dc2f2066b52e0412848/recipes/motif-3&quot;&gt;recipe folder&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/b3132ac9f4757db523c79dc2f2066b52e0412848/recipes/motif-3/README.md&quot;&gt;README&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16392&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16392/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16392&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16314&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16314/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16314&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Getting Started&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deployment is Kubernetes-based (Dynamo Platform + &lt;code&gt;DynamoGraphDeployment&lt;/code&gt;). Full steps — namespace, &lt;code&gt;hf-token-secret&lt;/code&gt;, model-cache PVC, download Job, aggregated or 3P1D apply, and a &lt;code&gt;/v1/chat/completions&lt;/code&gt; smoke test — are in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/b3132ac9f4757db523c79dc2f2066b52e0412848/recipes/motif-3/README.md&quot;&gt;recipe README&lt;/a&gt; and the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/b3132ac9f4757db523c79dc2f2066b52e0412848/docs/fern/pages/recipes/model-recipes/motif-3.mdx&quot;&gt;Fern guide&lt;/a&gt;. The download Job is the only step that needs the Hugging Face token. For 3P1D, each TP2 worker occupies two GPUs on one node, and the fabric must allow NIXL/UCX transfer between nodes. Optional Nscale scheduling is a Kustomize component on the generic manifest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Known Issues / Limitations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experimental snapshot build — not QA-gated; not for production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The vLLM runtime image is amd64 only, and recipes reference it by tag rather than digest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The runtime image carries Motif-specific vLLM compatibility code. Do not replace its vLLM package with an unrelated wheel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Disaggregated serving is validated for TP2 on both prefill and decode. Other tensor-parallel sizes are unvalidated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shipped manifests use real MTP verification. Results measured with synthetic acceptance length 2.13 are a benchmark-only proxy and are not reproduced by the manifests as shipped.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In the reference aggregated chat trace, 35 requests exceed the 262,144-token context limit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;</content>
    <author>
      <name>ynpandey-nv</name>
    </author>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20666257?s=60&amp;v=4"/>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/942206898/v1.6.0-minimax-m3-dev.1</id>
    <updated>2026-10-12T18:28:55Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/releases/tag/v1.6.0-minimax-m3-dev.1"/>
    <title>Dynamo v1.6.0-minimax-m3-dev.1</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Notes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo v1.6.0-minimax-m3-dev.1&lt;/strong&gt; is an experimental snapshot build with early &lt;strong&gt;MiniMax M3&lt;/strong&gt; support on the Dynamo &lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt; backend. It is &lt;strong&gt;not recommended for production&lt;/strong&gt; and is not a QA-gated release. APIs, behavior, and defaults may change before stable support. Use it for evaluation, testing, and early feedback only.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dynamo v1.6.0-minimax-m3-dev.1 serves &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvidia/MiniMax-M3-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; on Dynamo &lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt;. The published container is built from pinned vLLM nightly &lt;code&gt;8a728663c1c3&lt;/code&gt; (CUDA 13) and includes the MiniMax M3 reasoning and structured-output parser, a GB200-safe vision patch embedding, and KV-offload fixes for EAGLE/MTP. vLLM-Omni is excluded from this image. Prefill load accounting charges only GPU compute, and finalized VP9/WebM inputs can be decoded when duration is stored on the container rather than the stream (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14856&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14856/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14856&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kubernetes recipes serve the same checkpoint on GB200 with tensor parallelism 4, FP8 KV cache, real EAGLE3 verification, KV-aware routing, and a one-million-token context. The aggregated profile uses 12 GPUs and 400 GB of CPU KV offload per replica. The disaggregated profile uses 24 GPUs and transfers KV from prefill to decode with NIXL. Both profiles share a model-cache download for the target and &lt;code&gt;Inferact/MiniMax-M3-EAGLE3-GQA&lt;/code&gt; draft, and a perf/trace reference ships with the recipes (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15096&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15096/hovercard&quot;&gt;#15096&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16043&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16043/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16043&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Branch&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;release/1.6.0-minimax-m3-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;, tip &lt;code&gt;1cf43bce3fc865a14dcd8f9bb857f6b726617ed0&lt;/code&gt; (2026-10-09)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt;: nightly &lt;code&gt;8a728663c1c3&lt;/code&gt; (CUDA 13), NIXL v1.3.2&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Container Images&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Arch&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Image&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;vLLM (CUDA 13)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;multi-arch (&lt;code&gt;amd64&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;arm64&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/ai-dynamo/vllm-runtime:1.6.0-minimax-m3-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend Versions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Source&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;CUDA&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Python&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;vLLM&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Dynamo-built runtime on pinned nightly &lt;code&gt;vllm-nightly-8a728663c1c3&lt;/code&gt;, with MiniMax M3 reasoning, vision, and KV-offload patches&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;13.0&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;3.12&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NIXL v1.3.2; Transformers 5.14.1; tokenizers 0.22.2; vLLM-Omni excluded&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Models&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Model&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Precision&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;GPU&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvidia/MiniMax-M3-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NVFP4&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;12x GB200 aggregated, 24x GB200 disaggregated&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;target checkpoint, revision &lt;code&gt;901464083161bf8612a29ff7ad29914cd4ab4a85&lt;/code&gt;; FP8 KV; up to 1M context; multimodal input enabled&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;Inferact/MiniMax-M3-EAGLE3-GQA&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;with both profiles&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;EAGLE3 draft, revision &lt;code&gt;96692486b5fd38ebf8fd2a5f6bb53427d30819a8&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About MiniMax M3&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MiniMax M3&lt;/strong&gt; is served in this preview as &lt;code&gt;nvidia/MiniMax-M3-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt; (NVFP4) through Dynamo&#39;s vLLM backend on GB200, with aggregated or prefill/decode disaggregated workers, EAGLE3 speculative decoding, and KV-aware routing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Changelog&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Backend&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MiniMax M3 runtime:&lt;/strong&gt; Pins the CUDA 13 vLLM runtime to nightly &lt;code&gt;8a728663c1c3&lt;/code&gt; and applies the MiniMax M3 reasoning/structured-output parser, the vision-tower patch embedding used on GB200, and KV-offload fixes that keep the final sampled token out of the prefix cache and preserve EAGLE/MTP offload hits. vLLM-Omni is not installed (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14856&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14856/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14856&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Routing and media decode:&lt;/strong&gt; Prefill load accounting counts only tokens that still need GPU compute, including when KV is already resident on host or disk. Finalized VP9/WebM inputs decode when duration is present on the container and missing from the video stream (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14856&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14856/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14856&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recipes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MiniMax M3 recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Added &lt;code&gt;recipes/minimax-m3&lt;/code&gt; — shared model-cache PVC and pinned Hugging Face download, vLLM aggregated (&lt;code&gt;agg-gb200-agentic&lt;/code&gt;, 3x TP4, 400 GB CPU KV offload per replica) and disaggregated (&lt;code&gt;disagg-gb200-agentic&lt;/code&gt;, 3 prefill + 3 decode TP4, NIXL transfer) GB200 profiles, real EAGLE3 verification by default, and a perf/trace reference (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/tree/1cf43bce3fc865a14dcd8f9bb857f6b726617ed0/recipes/minimax-m3&quot;&gt;recipe folder&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/1cf43bce3fc865a14dcd8f9bb857f6b726617ed0/recipes/minimax-m3/README.md&quot;&gt;README&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15096&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15096/hovercard&quot;&gt;#15096&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16043&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16043/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16043&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Getting Started&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deployment is Kubernetes-based (Dynamo Platform, ComputeDomain, the NVIDIA DRA driver, and &lt;code&gt;DynamoGraphDeployment&lt;/code&gt;). Full steps — namespace, &lt;code&gt;hf-token-secret&lt;/code&gt;, model-cache PVC, Hugging Face download of the target and EAGLE3 draft, cluster Kustomize render, DGD apply, and a &lt;code&gt;/v1/chat/completions&lt;/code&gt; smoke test — are in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/1cf43bce3fc865a14dcd8f9bb857f6b726617ed0/recipes/minimax-m3/README.md&quot;&gt;recipe README&lt;/a&gt;. The token needs access to &lt;code&gt;nvidia/MiniMax-M3-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;Inferact/MiniMax-M3-EAGLE3-GQA&lt;/code&gt;. Recipes expect registry credentials for &lt;code&gt;nvcr.io&lt;/code&gt; and a Hugging Face token secret named &lt;code&gt;hf-token-secret&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Known Issues / Limitations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experimental snapshot build — not QA-gated; not for production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This image does not include vLLM-Omni.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recipes in this build are vLLM on GB200 only.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Disaggregated workers must share a compatible NVLink domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The synthetic-acceptance benchmark option bypasses real EAGLE3 verification. Use it only for controlled performance experiments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;</content>
    <author>
      <name>nv-nmailhot</name>
    </author>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219894992?s=60&amp;v=4"/>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/942206898/v1.6.0-deepseek-v4.1-flash-dev.2</id>
    <updated>2026-10-08T23:42:32Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/releases/tag/v1.6.0-deepseek-v4.1-flash-dev.2"/>
    <title>Dynamo v1.6.0-deepseek-v4.1-flash-dev.2</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Notes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo v1.6.0-deepseek-v4.1-flash-dev.2&lt;/strong&gt; is an experimental snapshot build with early &lt;strong&gt;DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash&lt;/strong&gt; support on the Dynamo &lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt; backend. It is &lt;strong&gt;not recommended for production&lt;/strong&gt; and is not a QA-gated release. APIs, behavior, and defaults may change before stable support. Use it for evaluation, testing, and early feedback only.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dynamo v1.6.0-deepseek-v4.1-flash-dev.2 adds serving for &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; on Dynamo &lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt;. The published container is built from multi-arch &lt;code&gt;vllm/vllm-openai:v0.31.0&lt;/code&gt; (CUDA 13.0.2, source &lt;code&gt;db9527a46873454610df6dbedf79a36d6bf1a7f6&lt;/code&gt;) and carries NIXL transfer patches that advance the connector protocol to 14. vLLM Omni is disabled in this image (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15532&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15532/hovercard&quot;&gt;#15532&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kubernetes recipes cover aggregated and 1P1D disaggregated vLLM profiles on B200, GB200, and H200. B200 and GB200 use eight GPUs with MXFP4 sparse-indexer KV, sparse-indexer logits, and &lt;code&gt;deep_gemm_mega_moe&lt;/code&gt;. H200 uses 16 GPUs for aggregated serving or eight for disaggregated serving, with CUTLASS MoE. Every vLLM profile uses expert parallelism, expert load balancing, KV-aware routing, and DSpark with three draft tokens. Disaggregated profiles transfer KV over NIXL/UCX. The shared model-cache download pins Hugging Face revision &lt;code&gt;dba1be0a40aa45a94ad051997016db3960a90277&lt;/code&gt;, and measured agentic results ship with the recipes (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15941&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15941/hovercard&quot;&gt;#15941&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Branch&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;release/1.6.0-deepseek-v4.1-flash-dev.2&lt;/code&gt;, tip &lt;code&gt;a201d5bd608e67a3c1def7eebace3201e6de0000&lt;/code&gt; (2026-10-08)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;v0.31.0&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;vllm/vllm-openai&lt;/code&gt;, digest &lt;code&gt;sha256:c1c9f6fd5c109ba7f0546a59f5b2f15fb87f64c77782e90a27b648b42a8e67c3&lt;/code&gt;), NIXL v1.3.2 (connector protocol 14)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Container Images&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Arch&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Image&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;vLLM (CUDA 13.0.2)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;multi-arch (&lt;code&gt;amd64&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;arm64&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/ai-dynamo/vllm-runtime:1.6.0-deepseek-v4.1-flash-dev.2&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend Versions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Source&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;CUDA&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Python&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;vLLM&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Dynamo-built runtime on &lt;code&gt;vllm/vllm-openai:v0.31.0&lt;/code&gt;, with NIXL telemetry, region-dedup, and piecewise-prefix patches&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;13.0.2&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;3.12&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NIXL v1.3.2; connector protocol 14; vLLM Omni disabled&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Models&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Model&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Precision&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;GPU&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;MXFP4 experts; B200/GB200 sparse-indexer KV and sparse-indexer logits; H200 CUTLASS MoE&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;8x B200, 8x GB200, 16x H200 aggregated, 8x H200 disaggregated&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;deepseek_v41&lt;/code&gt; reasoning and tool-call parsers; DSpark-3; up to 1,048,576-token context; text serving&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash&lt;/strong&gt; is a Mixture-of-Experts checkpoint from DeepSeek (&lt;code&gt;deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash&lt;/code&gt;). This preview serves it through Dynamo&#39;s vLLM backend, with aggregated or 1P1D disaggregated workers, DSpark speculative decoding, and KV-aware routing on B200, GB200, and H200.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Changelog&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Backend&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Patched vLLM 0.31.0 runtime:&lt;/strong&gt; Pins the CUDA 13 vLLM runtime to multi-arch &lt;code&gt;v0.31.0&lt;/code&gt; and applies the NIXL telemetry, region-dedup, and piecewise-prefix patches so workers in this image use connector protocol 14. vLLM Omni stays disabled (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15532&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15532/hovercard&quot;&gt;#15532&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recipes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash vLLM recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Added aggregated and 1P1D disaggregated Kustomize profiles for B200 (8 GPU), GB200 (8 GPU), and H200 (16 GPU aggregated, 8 GPU disaggregated). Profiles use expert parallelism, EPLB, KV-aware routing, and DSpark-3. Disaggregated KV transfer uses NIXL/UCX (InfiniBand on B200 and H200; one NVLink clique on GB200). Includes the shared model-cache download, agentic benchmark job, and deployment guide (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/tree/a201d5bd608e67a3c1def7eebace3201e6de0000/recipes/deepseek-v4.1-flash&quot;&gt;recipe folder&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/a201d5bd608e67a3c1def7eebace3201e6de0000/docs/fern/pages/recipes/model-recipes/deepseek-v4-1-flash.mdx&quot;&gt;docs&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/a201d5bd608e67a3c1def7eebace3201e6de0000/recipes/deepseek-v4.1-flash/perf/README.md&quot;&gt;benchmarks&lt;/a&gt;) (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15941&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15941/hovercard&quot;&gt;#15941&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Getting Started&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deployment is Kubernetes-based (Dynamo Platform + &lt;code&gt;DynamoGraphDeployment&lt;/code&gt;). Full steps — namespace, model-cache PVC, Hugging Face download job pinned to revision &lt;code&gt;dba1be0a40aa45a94ad051997016db3960a90277&lt;/code&gt;, Kustomize render, DGD apply, and a &lt;code&gt;/v1/chat/completions&lt;/code&gt; smoke test — are in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/a201d5bd608e67a3c1def7eebace3201e6de0000/docs/fern/pages/recipes/model-recipes/deepseek-v4-1-flash.mdx&quot;&gt;recipe docs&lt;/a&gt;. Recipes expect an &lt;code&gt;nvcr.io&lt;/code&gt; image-pull secret, a Hugging Face token secret named &lt;code&gt;hf-token-secret&lt;/code&gt;, and Kustomize v5.8.1. GB200 workers schedule on ARM64 nodes; B200 and H200 workers schedule on AMD64 nodes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Known Issues / Limitations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a branch-specific snapshot build, not a QA-gated stable release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workers in this runtime image use NIXL connector protocol 14. CUDA dev and local-dev images stay on protocol 13; do not mix them in one KV transfer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GB200 disaggregated workers must share one NVLink clique.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;H200 disaggregated serving places prefill and decode on separate RDMA-capable nodes and selects NICs from the &lt;code&gt;rdma/ib&lt;/code&gt; device plugin. Do not set a static &lt;code&gt;UCX_NET_DEVICES&lt;/code&gt; value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B200 and GB200 disaggregated recipes still need the cluster&#39;s RDMA device and interface settings in the Kustomization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SGLang profiles in &lt;code&gt;recipes/deepseek-v4.1-flash&lt;/code&gt; still use &lt;code&gt;sglang-runtime:1.6.0-deepseek-v4.1-flash-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;. They are not served by this vLLM image.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;</content>
    <author>
      <name>ynpandey-nv</name>
    </author>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20666257?s=60&amp;v=4"/>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/942206898/v1.5.0-kimi-k3-post.1</id>
    <updated>2026-10-08T20:14:58Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/releases/tag/v1.5.0-kimi-k3-post.1"/>
    <title>Dynamo v1.5.0-kimi-k3-post.1</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Notes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo v1.5.0-kimi-k3-post.1&lt;/strong&gt; is an experimental snapshot build with &lt;strong&gt;Kimi-K3&lt;/strong&gt; support on the Dynamo &lt;strong&gt;SGLang&lt;/strong&gt; backend. It is &lt;strong&gt;not recommended for production&lt;/strong&gt; and is not a QA-gated release. APIs, behavior, and defaults may change before stable support. Use it for evaluation, testing, and early feedback only.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dynamo v1.5.0-kimi-k3-post.1 serves &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;moonshotai/Kimi-K3&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; from an SGLang runtime built on Dynamo 1.5.1 and SGLang &lt;code&gt;v0.5.18&lt;/code&gt;. The image includes the two Kimi-K3 fixes that base still needs: DCP prefill/decode with DSpark draft-KV transfer, and the SM100 MoonViT cuDNN guard for image encode (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15657&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15657/hovercard&quot;&gt;#15657&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GB300 SGLang recipes run that image. Aggregated serving uses two workers (16x GB300, DCP8 attention, TP8 MoE) with load-aware routing and DSpark. Disaggregated serving is 1P1D (16x GB300; prefill TEP8, decode DCP8 attention and TEP8 MoE) with Mooncake KV transfer over NVLink. Workers set &lt;code&gt;SGLANG_FORCE_COARSE_WAR_BARRIER=1&lt;/code&gt;. The recipe includes a shared model cache and an AIPerf replay of the 64K-ISL / 400-OSL / 90% KV-reuse agentic trace (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15658&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15658/hovercard&quot;&gt;#15658&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15919&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15919/hovercard&quot;&gt;#15919&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Branch&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;release/1.5.0-kimi-k3-post.1&lt;/code&gt;, tip &lt;code&gt;a0dcfbf6d3aa788e8dba806189f1611d9293a52f&lt;/code&gt; (2026-10-08)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;SGLang image commit&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;22031aba1fb33524370a26150e9fd7a7751d9fef&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;release/1.5.1-kimi-k3-post.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;SGLang&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;lmsysorg/sglang:v0.5.18-cu130-runtime&lt;/code&gt; (CUDA 13.0)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Container Images&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Arch&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Image&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;SGLang (CUDA 13)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;multi-arch (&lt;code&gt;amd64&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;arm64&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/ai-dynamo/sglang-runtime:1.5.1-kimi-k3-post.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend Versions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Source&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;CUDA&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Python&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;SGLang&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Dynamo-built runtime on &lt;code&gt;lmsysorg/sglang:v0.5.18-cu130-runtime&lt;/code&gt; with the Kimi-K3 DCP/DSpark and SM100 MoonViT patches&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;13.0&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;3.12&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Disaggregated KV transfer uses Mooncake; DSpark draft is &lt;code&gt;RadixArk/Kimi-K3-DSpark&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Models&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Model&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Precision&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;GPU&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;moonshotai/Kimi-K3&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;MXFP4 experts, FP8 KV cache&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;GB300&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;multimodal (text + image) MoE, up to 1M-token context; &lt;code&gt;kimi_k3&lt;/code&gt; reasoning and tool-call parsers&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Kimi-K3&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://huggingface.co/moonshotai/Kimi-K3&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;Kimi-K3&lt;/a&gt; is Moonshot AI&#39;s hybrid-attention mixture-of-experts model with multimodal (text + image) support and up to 1M-token context. This preview serves it through Dynamo&#39;s SGLang backend with aggregated and 1P1D disaggregated agentic recipes on GB300, using DSpark speculative decoding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Changelog&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Backend&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kimi-K3 runtime on SGLang v0.5.18:&lt;/strong&gt; The published runtime is Dynamo 1.5.1 SGLang with two baked-in fixes: DCP prefill/decode plus DSpark draft-KV transfer, and a MoonViT cuDNN guard so SM100 image encode does not crash. The image build checks the patched files against the benchmarked hashes (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15657&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15657/hovercard&quot;&gt;#15657&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recipes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GB300 SGLang recipes on the post.1 image:&lt;/strong&gt; Aggregated serving is two TP8/DCP8 workers (16x GB300) with load-aware routing, prefix caching, and DSpark. Disaggregated serving is 1P1D (16x GB300) with Mooncake KV transfer over MNNVL and the same DSpark draft. Workers set &lt;code&gt;SGLANG_FORCE_COARSE_WAR_BARRIER=1&lt;/code&gt;. Context length is 1,048,576. The perf job replays the agentic Mooncake trace; the published GB300 figures use synthetic acceptance length 4.05 (aggregated: 91.3 output tok/s/GPU, 55.6 user tok/s P50, TTFT P50 486 ms at concurrency 36; 1P1D: 62.0 output tok/s/GPU, 77.6 user tok/s P50, TTFT P50 4,793 ms at concurrency 18) (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/tree/a0dcfbf6d3aa788e8dba806189f1611d9293a52f/recipes/kimi-k3&quot;&gt;recipe folder&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/a0dcfbf6d3aa788e8dba806189f1611d9293a52f/docs/fern/pages/recipes/model-recipes/kimi-k3.mdx&quot;&gt;docs&lt;/a&gt;) (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15658&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15658/hovercard&quot;&gt;#15658&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15919&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15919/hovercard&quot;&gt;#15919&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Getting Started&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deployment is Kubernetes-based (Dynamo Platform + &lt;code&gt;DynamoGraphDeployment&lt;/code&gt;). Use the GB300 SGLang manifests under &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/tree/a0dcfbf6d3aa788e8dba806189f1611d9293a52f/recipes/kimi-k3/sglang&quot;&gt;recipes/kimi-k3/sglang&lt;/a&gt;: create the namespace, Hugging Face token secret &lt;code&gt;hf-token-secret&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;nvcr.io&lt;/code&gt; pull secret, populate the shared model cache, apply the aggregated or disaggregated manifest, and smoke-test &lt;code&gt;/v1/chat/completions&lt;/code&gt; with model &lt;code&gt;moonshotai/Kimi-K3&lt;/code&gt;. Benchmark steps are in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/a0dcfbf6d3aa788e8dba806189f1611d9293a52f/recipes/kimi-k3/perf/README.md&quot;&gt;perf README&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Known Issues / Limitations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a branch-specific snapshot build, not a QA-gated stable release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This snapshot publishes an SGLang image only. vLLM manifests on the branch still reference &lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/ai-dynamo/vllm-runtime:1.4.0-kimi-k3-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SGLang manifests on this branch are GB300-only (aggregated 16x and disaggregated 1P1D 16x). There is no H200 SGLang profile.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The GB300 tok/s figures above use synthetic speculative acceptance (&lt;code&gt;acc_len&lt;/code&gt; 4.05). They are not real DSpark verification results. The serving manifests default to real DSpark; synthetic acceptance is a benchmark-only setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;During a long prefill, the canary health check (&lt;code&gt;DYN_HEALTH_CHECK_REQUEST_TIMEOUT&lt;/code&gt;, 3 seconds) can fail and Kubernetes can restart a busy worker. If the worker log shows &lt;code&gt;Health check timeout for&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;generate&lt;/code&gt;, set &lt;code&gt;DYN_HEALTH_CHECK_ENABLED=false&lt;/code&gt; on each SGLang worker.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Requests containing &lt;code&gt;logprobs&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;stop_token_ids&lt;/code&gt; are not supported and may cause disaggregated recipes to crash or enter a bad state.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;With JSON structured decoding, output for non-object top-level items can appear in &lt;code&gt;reasoning_content&lt;/code&gt; instead of &lt;code&gt;content&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;</content>
    <author>
      <name>ynpandey-nv</name>
    </author>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20666257?s=60&amp;v=4"/>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/942206898/v1.5.1</id>
    <updated>2026-10-07T01:54:13Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/releases/tag/v1.5.1"/>
    <title>Dynamo v1.5.1</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo v1.5.1 - Release Notes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dynamo v1.5.1 is a patch release on top of &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/releases/tag/v1.5.0&quot;&gt;v1.5.0&lt;/a&gt;. It fixes &lt;strong&gt;Dynamo Router overload recovery&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;min_tokens&lt;/code&gt; on tokenizer-free SGLang decode workers&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Qwen3-VL video routing across mixed workers&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;reinforcement learning worker discovery on Kubernetes&lt;/strong&gt;. It bounds &lt;strong&gt;client-supplied multimodal input&lt;/strong&gt; (inline &lt;code&gt;data:&lt;/code&gt; URL size, remote media downloads, image dimensions, and base64 audio) across the SGLang, TensorRT-LLM, vLLM, and vLLM-Omni paths, and moves all media fetching onto a single aiohttp client. It also upgrades the frontend runtime libraries to fix &lt;strong&gt;Anthropic Messages API requests from Claude Code&lt;/strong&gt; against strict chat templates, moves ModelExpress to v0.6.0, pins PyNvVideoCodec at 2.2.3, and moves the in-tree FFmpeg build to 9.0.1.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Two changes need action on upgrade. See &lt;strong&gt;Breaking Changes&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base Branch&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;release/1.5.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Breaking Changes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Egress Proxy Opt-In:&lt;/strong&gt; Workers that fetch request media through an ambient HTTP proxy must now set &lt;code&gt;DYN_MM_TRUST_EGRESS_PROXY=1&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14474&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14474/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14474&lt;/a&gt;). Without it, a policy-checked media fetch that would route through a proxy is refused, because the proxy resolves the destination outside Dynamo&#39;s address check. Fetches that go direct, including hosts listed in &lt;code&gt;NO_PROXY&lt;/code&gt;, are unaffected, and the check does not run under &lt;code&gt;DYN_MM_ALLOW_INTERNAL=1&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Diffusion Local References:&lt;/strong&gt; Local image and video files passed as &lt;code&gt;input_reference&lt;/code&gt; to SGLang image-diffusion and video-generation workers now require &lt;code&gt;DYN_MM_LOCAL_PATH&lt;/code&gt; to name the allowed directory (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14435&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14435/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14435&lt;/a&gt;). Previously any local path was accepted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bug Fixes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Router Overload Hint Expiry:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed a Dynamo Router condition where a worker that rejected requests for lack of capacity stayed marked overloaded after the pressure ended, so clients kept receiving HTTP 529 from an idle worker (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5327287390&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14210&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14210/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14210&quot;&gt;#14210&lt;/a&gt;). Overload hints raised on the request path now expire after one second, while overload state reported by the worker monitor stays independent, so a drained worker returns to rotation without a restart.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Tokenizer-Free Min Tokens:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed requests with a positive &lt;code&gt;min_tokens&lt;/code&gt; failing on SGLang decode workers started with &lt;code&gt;skip_tokenizer_init&lt;/code&gt;, where SGLang rejects the &lt;code&gt;min_new_tokens&lt;/code&gt; field (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5340230535&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14276&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14276/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14276&quot;&gt;#14276&lt;/a&gt;). Dynamo now enforces the minimum itself on that path, and cancellation or early stream closure aborts every unfinished choice in multi-choice (&lt;code&gt;n&lt;/code&gt;) requests. Requests without &lt;code&gt;min_tokens&lt;/code&gt; and workers that keep a tokenizer are unchanged.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Split Stop-Sequence Leak:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed hidden stop sequences that arrive split across several decode steps leaking their leading fragments into client output (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5358967864&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14378&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14378/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14378&quot;&gt;#14378&lt;/a&gt;). The decoder now holds back text that could still complete a stop sequence and releases it only once it cannot match, or when the engine finishes on its own, for example at &lt;code&gt;max_tokens&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qwen3-VL Video Contract Agreement:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed a Qwen3-VL deployment serving video with a prompt-expansion contract that only some of its workers publish (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5415309304&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14624&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14624/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14624&quot;&gt;#14624&lt;/a&gt;). Replicas with different installed packages or engine flags can publish different video contracts; when the workers in a group disagree, Dynamo now disables exact video routing for that group while text serving continues, and keeps the existing group serving until a rebuilt one commits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sidecar Worker Namespace Suffix:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed vLLM sidecar and mocker workers registering under the base namespace while reinforcement learning discovery on Kubernetes searched the suffixed one, so RL workloads could not find their workers (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5479327786&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14955&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14955/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14955&quot;&gt;#14955&lt;/a&gt;). Worker registration now applies &lt;code&gt;DYN_NAMESPACE_WORKER_SUFFIX&lt;/code&gt; at most once, which keeps operator-upgraded workloads whose &lt;code&gt;DYN_NAMESPACE&lt;/code&gt; already carries the suffix working, and an explicit command-line namespace still takes precedence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GPU Memory Service Admission Timeout:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the vLLM GPU Memory Service worker ignoring a configured &lt;code&gt;gms_ro_connect_timeout_ms&lt;/code&gt; during its initial weights load, which could leave startup waiting indefinitely behind lock contention (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5466750118&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14877&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14877/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14877&quot;&gt;#14877&lt;/a&gt;). Deployments that do not set the timeout keep the existing unbounded wait.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inline Data URL Size Cap:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a size cap on inline &lt;code&gt;data:&lt;/code&gt; media URLs, enforced by both the frontend and the workers (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5380397334&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14437&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14437/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14437&quot;&gt;#14437&lt;/a&gt;). A &lt;code&gt;data:&lt;/code&gt; URL larger than &lt;code&gt;DYN_MM_MAX_DATA_URL_MB&lt;/code&gt; (default 16 MiB) now returns HTTP 400 with a message naming the variable, where before any size was accepted. To raise the limit, set the variable on both the frontend and the workers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Diffusion Input References:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed SGLang image-diffusion and video-generation workers handing a client-supplied &lt;code&gt;input_reference&lt;/code&gt; to the generator after only a non-empty check (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5380322309&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14435&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14435/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14435&quot;&gt;#14435&lt;/a&gt;). Dynamo now validates the reference and downloads a remote one to a temporary local file first, capped by &lt;code&gt;DYN_MM_MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB&lt;/code&gt; (default 64 MiB), which matches the vLLM-Omni and TensorRT-LLM workers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM-Omni Input Validation:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed non-numeric or out-of-range image &lt;code&gt;width&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;height&lt;/code&gt; values and malformed base64 audio crashing the vLLM-Omni worker or ending a realtime session (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5380375531&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14436&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14436/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14436&quot;&gt;#14436&lt;/a&gt;). Image dimensions outside 1 to 4096 are now rejected with a clear error, an unusable realtime audio chunk emits an &lt;code&gt;invalid_audio&lt;/code&gt; error event instead of closing the connection, and percent-encoded &lt;code&gt;data:&lt;/code&gt; reference audio for text-to-speech now decodes correctly instead of producing corrupted audio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Media Fetch Address Pinning:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed media fetches resolving a hostname once to validate it and again to connect, so a server that answered differently the second time was checked on one address and dialed on another (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5388237207&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14474&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14474/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14474&quot;&gt;#14474&lt;/a&gt;). The Python workers and the Rust frontend now connect only to the addresses that passed validation, while TLS still verifies the original hostname.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Single aiohttp HTTP Backend:&lt;/strong&gt; Removed the opt-in httpx backend from Dynamo&#39;s HTTP client, leaving aiohttp as the only backend (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5405531726&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14563&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14563/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14563&quot;&gt;#14563&lt;/a&gt;). Setting &lt;code&gt;DYN_HTTP_BACKEND=httpx&lt;/code&gt; now logs a warning and uses aiohttp. The TensorRT-LLM multimodal processor&#39;s remote &lt;code&gt;.safetensors&lt;/code&gt; download now streams asynchronously, so it no longer blocks the event loop for up to the 300-second download timeout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dependency Changes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend Runtime Libraries:&lt;/strong&gt; Upgraded &lt;code&gt;dynamo-renderer&lt;/code&gt; to v5.1.2 and &lt;code&gt;dynamo-tokenizers&lt;/code&gt; to v1.8.1, fixing Anthropic Messages API failures when Claude Code sends a non-leading system message to a model whose chat template requires system content first (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5406732075&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14595&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14595/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14595&quot;&gt;#14595&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DeepSeek V4 Reasoning Effort:&lt;/strong&gt; The renderer now defaults an omitted or invalid reasoning effort to &lt;code&gt;high&lt;/code&gt;, treats &lt;code&gt;none&lt;/code&gt; as thinking disabled, and lets a top-level &lt;code&gt;reasoning_effort&lt;/code&gt; override the template argument (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5406732075&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14595&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14595/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14595&quot;&gt;#14595&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OpenAI Response Fields:&lt;/strong&gt; Upgraded &lt;code&gt;dynamo-protocols&lt;/code&gt; to v5.4.1, so &lt;code&gt;/v1/chat/completions&lt;/code&gt; responses omit absent optional fields such as &lt;code&gt;usage&lt;/code&gt; instead of returning &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5318628594&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14154&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14154/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14154&quot;&gt;#14154&lt;/a&gt;). Client code that indexes raw response dictionaries should check for those keys.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ModelExpress:&lt;/strong&gt; Upgraded ModelExpress to v0.6.0 in the SGLang and vLLM runtime images (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5493386742&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15026&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15026/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15026&quot;&gt;#15026&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PyNvVideoCodec and FFmpeg:&lt;/strong&gt; Pinned PyNvVideoCodec at 2.2.3 in the runtime images and moved the in-tree FFmpeg build to 9.0.1 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5470819217&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14925&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14925/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14925&quot;&gt;#14925&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend aiohttp:&lt;/strong&gt; Raised aiohttp in the Frontend image to 3.14.4, matching the other images (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5719493506&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15676&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15676/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15676&quot;&gt;#15676&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migration After Shutdown Grace:&lt;/strong&gt; Clarified across the fault-tolerance guides that requests can finish during the shutdown grace period, that unfinished requests are cancelled when it expires, and that they can migrate to another worker when migration is enabled and the request allows it, with configuration guidance for rolling upgrades and scale-downs (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5466311140&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14872&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14872/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14872&quot;&gt;#14872&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stale Documentation Links:&lt;/strong&gt; Repaired documentation links that pointed at moved pages on &lt;code&gt;main&lt;/code&gt; and returned 404 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5613334124&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/15308&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15308/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15308&quot;&gt;#15308&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agent Skills Tab:&lt;/strong&gt; Moved Agent Skills from a single Reference page into its own documentation tab, with an overview and one page per skill category, and listed all 27 skills (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5317974399&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14146&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14146/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14146&quot;&gt;#14146&lt;/a&gt;). The old Reference URL redirects to the new overview.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Dependencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backend runtime versions are unchanged from v1.5.0:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
